other is looking for his shoes."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"5-07-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"体育行事がある曜日を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"Friday","accepted":["Friday"],"why":"本文の根拠：Sports day is next Friday.","context":"Sports day is next Friday. It starts at ten. Wear your white shirt and blue shorts. Bring water and a towel. Your family can watch from the school garden. Lunch is at twelve. We finish at two in the afternoon.","title":"A sports day message","evidence":"Sports day is next Friday."},{"id":"5-07-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"着てくるシャツの色を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"white","accepted":["white"],"why":"本文の根拠：Wear your white shirt and blue shorts.","context":"Sports day is next Friday. It starts at ten. Wear your white shirt and blue shorts. Bring water and a towel. Your family can watch from the school garden. Lunch is at twelve. We finish at two in the afternoon.","title":"A sports day message","evidence":"Wear your white shirt and blue shorts."},{"id":"5-07-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"行事が終わる午後の時刻を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"2","accepted":["2"],"why":"本文の根拠：We finish at two in the afternoon.","context":"Sports day is next Friday. It starts at ten. Wear your white shirt and blue shorts. Bring water and a towel. Your family can watch from the school garden. Lunch is at twelve. We finish at two in the afternoon.","title":"A sports day message","evidence":"We finish at two in the afternoon."},{"id":"5-07-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"買いたかったのに売っていなかった果物を本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"strawberries","accepted":["strawberries"],"why":"本文の根拠：Lily wants strawberries, but the shop has no strawberries today.","context":"Lily and her father go to the market on Sunday. They buy bread, eggs, and cheese. Lily wants strawberries, but the shop has no strawberries today. She buys peaches instead. At home, her father makes sandwiches. Lily cuts the peaches for dessert.","title":"At a market","evidence":"Lily wants strawberries, but the shop has no strawberries today."},{"id":"5-07-19","n":19,"kind":"reading","q":"代わりに買った果物を本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"peaches","accepted":["peaches"],"why":"本文の根拠：She buys peaches instead.","context":"Lily and her father go to the market on Sunday. They buy bread, eggs, and cheese. Lily wants strawberries, but the shop has no strawberries today. She buys peaches instead. At home, her father makes sandwiches. Lily cuts the peaches for dessert.","title":"At a market","evidence":"She buys peaches instead."},{"id":"5-07-20","n":20,"kind":"reading","q":"家でサンドイッチを作る人を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"father","accepted":["father"],"why":"本文の根拠：At home, her father makes sandwiches.","context":"Lily and her father go to the market on Sunday. They buy bread, eggs, and cheese. Lily wants strawberries, but the shop has no strawberries today. She buys peaches instead. At home, her father makes sandwiches. Lily cuts the peaches for dessert.","title":"At a market","evidence":"At home, her father makes sandwiches."}]},{"n":8,"questions":[{"id":"5-08-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"The children ( enjoy / enjoys / enjoying ) their art class.","answer":"enjoy","accepted":["enjoy"],"why":"主語childrenは複数なので動詞の原形enjoyです。"},{"id":"5-08-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"My class begins ( at / for / on ) eight fifteen.","answer":"at","accepted":["at"],"why":"時刻の前にはatを使います。"},{"id":"5-08-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"The cat is ( behind / about / during ) the sofa. I can't see it.","answer":"behind","accepted":["behind"],"why":"ソファの後ろという位置はbehindです。"},{"id":"5-08-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: ( Which / Who / When ) do you want, the red shirt or the blue shirt?","answer":"Which","accepted":["Which"],"why":"示された二つのうちどちらかを選ぶ質問はWhichです。"},{"id":"5-08-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"I know that girl. ( Her / She / Hers ) name is Miki.","answer":"Her","accepted":["Her"],"why":"nameを修飾する所有格Herです。"},{"id":"5-08-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"There ( aren't / isn't / doesn't ) any eggs in the fridge.","answer":"aren't","accepted":["aren't"],"why":"eggsは複数なのでThere aren'tです。"},{"id":"5-08-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"Let's ( make / makes / made ) a card for our teacher.","answer":"make","accepted":["make"],"why":"Let'sの後には原形makeを置きます。"},{"id":"5-08-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: What are you doing? B: I am ( clean / cleaning / cleans ) my room.","answer":"cleaning","accepted":["cleaning"],"why":"今していることにはamとing形を使います。"},{"id":"5-08-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"We need an ( umbrella / envelope / eraser ) because it is raining.","answer":"umbrella","accepted":["umbrella"],"why":"雨を防ぐための傘はumbrellaです。"},{"id":"5-08-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"I like apples ( and / so / because ) bananas.","answer":"and","accepted":["and"],"why":"二つの名詞を並べるのでandです。"},{"id":"5-08-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私はコーヒーよりお茶が好きです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( coffee / like / tea / I / than / better )","answer":"I like tea better than coffee.","accepted":["I like tea better than coffee."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 比較する相手はthanの後ろに置きます。"},{"id":"5-08-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"あなたはどちらのバッグが欲しいですか。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( you / want / Which / do / bag )","answer":"Which bag do you want?","accepted":["Which bag do you want?"],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"5-08-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"彼らは学校の後ろに住んでいます。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( the / live / behind / They / school )","answer":"They live behind the school.","accepted":["They live behind the school."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"5-08-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"その女の人は自分の犬と歩いています。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( The / woman / dog / with / walking / her / is )","answer":"The woman is walking with her dog.","accepted":["The woman is walking with her dog."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"5-08-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"音楽に参加する生徒は何人ですか。数字で答えなさい。","answer":"5","accepted":["5"],"why":"本文の根拠：Five students play music at the school show.","context":"Five students play music at the school show. Emi plays the piano. Tom plays the guitar. Three other students sing. The show is in the school hall, not in the music room. It starts at six in the evening. Everyone can come.","title":"A music show","evidence":"Five students play music at the school show."},{"id":"5-08-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"Emiが弾く楽器を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"piano","accepted":["piano"],"why":"本文の根拠：Emi plays the piano.","context":"Five students play music at the school show. Emi plays the piano. Tom plays the guitar. Three other students sing. The show is in the school hall, not in the music room. It starts at six in the evening. Everyone can come.","title":"A music show","evidence":"Emi plays the piano."},{"id":"5-08-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"開演は夕方何時ですか。数字で答えなさい。","answer":"6","accepted":["6"],"why":"本文の根拠：It starts at six in the evening.","context":"Five students play music at the school show. Emi plays the piano. Tom plays the guitar. Three other students sing. The show is in the school hall, not in the music room. It starts at six in the evening. Everyone can come.","title":"A music show","evidence":"It starts at six in the evening."},{"id":"5-08-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"今日の天気を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"raining","accepted":["rain","rainy","raining"],"why":"本文の根拠：It is raining today.","context":"It is raining today. Hiro cannot ride his bike outside. He plays a card game with his sister. Their mother is reading in the living room. At four, the rain stops. Hiro goes to the park, but his sister stays home to draw.","title":"A rainy afternoon","evidence":"It is raining today."},{"id":"5-08-19","n":19,"kind":"reading","q":"母がしていることを本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"reading","accepted":["reading"],"why":"本文の根拠：Their mother is reading in the living room.","context":"It is raining today. Hiro cannot ride his bike outside. He plays a card game with his sister. Their mother is reading in the living room. At four, the rain stops. Hiro goes to the park, but his sister stays home to draw.","title":"A rainy afternoon","evidence":"Their mother is reading in the living room."},{"id":"5-08-20","n":20,"kind":"reading","q":"雨がやむ時刻を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"4","accepted":["4"],"why":"本文の根拠：At four, the rain stops.","context":"It is raining today. Hiro cannot ride his bike outside. He plays a card game with his sister. Their mother is reading in the living room. At four, the rain stops. Hiro goes to the park, but his sister stays home to draw.","title":"A rainy afternoon","evidence":"At four, the rain stops."}]},{"n":9,"questions":[{"id":"5-09-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"My friends ( live / lives / living ) near the station.","answer":"live","accepted":["live"],"why":"複数の主語friendsに対する現在形はliveです。"},{"id":"5-09-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"Mr. Green ( teaches / teach / teaching ) science at our school.","answer":"teaches","accepted":["teaches"],"why":"三人称単数でteachはesを付けます。"},{"id":"5-09-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"My birthday is ( in / on / at ) July.","answer":"in","accepted":["in"],"why":"月の前にはinを使います。"},{"id":"5-09-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: ( Whose / Who / When ) hat is this? B: It's my brother's.","answer":"Whose","accepted":["Whose"],"why":"持ち主をたずねるのはWhoseです。"},{"id":"5-09-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"This is your seat. Please sit ( down / across / under ).","answer":"down","accepted":["down"],"why":"sit downで「座る」という表現です。"},{"id":"5-09-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"I ( don't / doesn't / am not ) need a new phone.","answer":"don't","accepted":["don't"],"why":"主語Iと一般動詞needの否定はdon'tです。"},{"id":"5-09-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"My father can ( fix / fixes / fixed ) this chair.","answer":"fix","accepted":["fix"],"why":"助動詞canの後は原形です。"},{"id":"5-09-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"The woman is ( talk / talking / talks ) to the clerk now.","answer":"talking","accepted":["talking"],"why":"isとing形で現在進行形を作ります。"},{"id":"5-09-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"We borrow books from a ( library / restaurant / stadium ).","answer":"library","accepted":["library"],"why":"本を借りる施設はlibraryです。"},{"id":"5-09-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Do they know the answer? B: No, they ( don't / aren't / doesn't ).","answer":"don't","accepted":["don't"],"why":"Do theyへの否定の返答はthey don'tです。"},{"id":"5-09-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私たちは毎週金曜日に音楽があります。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( We / have / every / music / Friday )","answer":"We have music every Friday.","accepted":["We have music every Friday."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"5-09-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"この傘は誰のものですか。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( is / umbrella / Whose / this )","answer":"Whose umbrella is this?","accepted":["Whose umbrella is this?"],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"5-09-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"どうぞ私たちと一緒に来てください。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( come / with / Please / us )","answer":"Please come with us.","accepted":["Please come with us."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"5-09-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"私は母への手紙を書いています。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( my / writing / a / mother / am / I / letter / to )","answer":"I am writing a letter to my mother.","accepted":["I am writing a letter to my mother."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"5-09-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"Ritaが滞在している建物を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"hotel","accepted":["hotel"],"why":"本文の根拠：We stay in a small hotel.","context":"Dear Alex, I am in the mountains with my family. It is cool here. We stay in a small hotel. Every morning, we walk by a lake. My father likes the birds. I like the flowers. Tomorrow we go home by car. From Rita.","title":"A postcard","evidence":"We stay in a small hotel."},{"id":"5-09-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"Ritaが好きなものを本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"flowers","accepted":["flowers"],"why":"本文の根拠：I like the flowers.","context":"Dear Alex, I am in the mountains with my family. It is cool here. We stay in a small hotel. Every morning, we walk by a lake. My father likes the birds. I like the flowers. Tomorrow we go home by car. From Rita.","title":"A postcard","evidence":"I like the flowers."},{"id":"5-09-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"帰宅するときの乗り物を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"car","accepted":["car"],"why":"本文の根拠：Tomorrow we go home by car.","context":"Dear Alex, I am in the mountains with my family. It is cool here. We stay in a small hotel. Every morning, we walk by a lake. My father likes the birds. I like the flowers. Tomorrow we go home by car. From Rita.","title":"A postcard","evidence":"Tomorrow we go home by car."},{"id":"5-09-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"今週話す動物を本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"rabbits","accepted":["rabbits"],"why":"本文の根拠：We talk about rabbits this week.","context":"Come to the pet club on Monday. We talk about rabbits this week. Bring a photo of your pet if you have one. Do not bring live animals to school. The club meets in Room Seven. We finish at half past four.","title":"A pet club poster","evidence":"We talk about rabbits this week."},{"id":"5-09-19","n":19,"kind":"reading","q":"ペットについて持ってきてよいものを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"photo","accepted":["photo"],"why":"本文の根拠：Bring a photo of your pet if you have one.","context":"Come to the pet club on Monday. We talk about rabbits this week. Bring a photo of your pet if you have one. Do not bring live animals to school. The club meets in Room Seven. We finish at half past four.","title":"A pet club poster","evidence":"Bring a photo of your pet if you have one."},{"id":"5-09-20","n":20,"kind":"reading","q":"クラブの教室番号を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"7","accepted":["7"],"why":"本文の根拠：The club meets in Room Seven.","context":"Come to the pet club on Monday. We talk about rabbits this week. Bring a photo of your pet if you have one. Do not bring live animals to school. The club meets in Room Seven. We finish at half past four.","title":"A pet club poster","evidence":"The club meets in Room Seven."}]},{"n":10,"questions":[{"id":"5-10-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Are these flowers real? B: Yes, they ( are / is / do ).","answer":"are","accepted":["are"],"why":"複数の主語theyに対するbe動詞はareです。"},{"id":"5-10-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"My sister ( does / do / doing ) her homework before dinner.","answer":"does","accepted":["does"],"why":"三人称単数でdoはdoesになります。"},{"id":"5-10-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"We play soccer ( with / during / from ) our classmates.","answer":"with","accepted":["with"],"why":"一緒にする相手にはwithを使います。"},{"id":"5-10-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: ( How / When / Which ) do you go to school? B: By bus.","answer":"How","accepted":["How"],"why":"移動手段を尋ねるのはHowです。"},{"id":"5-10-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"That is my friend. I play tennis with ( her / she / hers ).","answer":"her","accepted":["her"],"why":"前置詞withの後は目的格herです。"},{"id":"5-10-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"( Is / Does / Do ) there a bank near here?","answer":"Is","accepted":["Is"],"why":"There isの疑問文ではIsを先頭に置きます。"},{"id":"5-10-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"You can't ( park / parks / parking ) your car here.","answer":"park","accepted":["park"],"why":"can'tの後は動詞の原形です。"},{"id":"5-10-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"The students are ( taking / take / takes ) a test now.","answer":"taking","accepted":["taking"],"why":"areとing形。takeのeを取ってtakingにします。"},{"id":"5-10-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"My shoes are too small. I need a new ( pair / piece / glass ).","answer":"pair","accepted":["pair"],"why":"靴のように二つで一組のものにはpairを使います。"},{"id":"5-10-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Would you like some tea? B: Yes, ( please / sorry / fine ).","answer":"please","accepted":["please"],"why":"申し出を丁寧に受ける表現はYes, please.です。"},{"id":"5-10-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"あなたはここで写真を撮れません。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( take / You / cannot / here / pictures )","answer":"You cannot take pictures here.","accepted":["You cannot take pictures here."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"5-10-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"あなたのお父さんは英語を教えますか。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( your / English / father / teach / Does )","answer":"Does your father teach English?","accepted":["Does your father teach English?"],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"5-10-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私の靴はベッドの下にあります。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( the / bed / are / My / shoes / under )","answer":"My shoes are under the bed.","accepted":["My shoes are under the bed."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"5-10-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"男の子たちは歌を練習しています。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( practicing / song / boys / a / The / are )","answer":"The boys are practicing a song.","accepted":["The boys are practicing a song."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"5-10-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"姉が作っているものを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"cake","accepted":["cake"],"why":"本文の根拠：My sister is making a cake.","context":"It's Dad's birthday on Saturday. My sister is making a cake. I am drawing a card. Mom is buying flowers. We put the presents in the kitchen. Dad comes home at seven. We will say happy birthday before dinner.","title":"A birthday plan","evidence":"My sister is making a cake."},{"id":"5-10-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"プレゼントを置く部屋を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"kitchen","accepted":["kitchen"],"why":"本文の根拠：We put the presents in the kitchen.","context":"It's Dad's birthday on Saturday. My sister is making a cake. I am drawing a card. Mom is buying flowers. We put the presents in the kitchen. Dad comes home at seven. We will say happy birthday before dinner.","title":"A birthday plan","evidence":"We put the presents in the kitchen."},{"id":"5-10-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"父が帰宅する時刻を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"7","accepted":["7"],"why":"本文の根拠：Dad comes home at seven.","context":"It's Dad's birthday on Saturday. My sister is making a cake. I am drawing a card. Mom is buying flowers. We put the presents in the kitchen. Dad comes home at seven. We will say happy birthday before dinner.","title":"A birthday plan","evidence":"Dad comes home at seven."},{"id":"5-10-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"今週の物語に出る動物を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"horse","accepted":["horse"],"why":"本文の根拠：This week, we read a story about a horse.","context":"Our reading group meets at the library on Friday. This week, we read a story about a horse. We sit in a circle and talk about the story. Please bring your notebook. There are eight people in our group. New members are welcome.","title":"A reading group","evidence":"This week, we read a story about a horse."},{"id":"5-10-19","n":19,"kind":"reading","q":"持ってくる物を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"notebook","accepted":["notebook"],"why":"本文の根拠：Please bring your notebook.","context":"Our reading group meets at the library on Friday. This week, we read a story about a horse. We sit in a circle and talk about the story. Please bring your notebook. There are eight people in our group. New members are welcome.","title":"A reading group","evidence":"Please bring your notebook."},{"id":"5-10-20","n":20,"kind":"reading","q":"グループの人数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"8","accepted":["8"],"why":"本文の根拠：There are eight people in our group.","context":"Our reading group meets at the library on Friday. This week, we read a story about a horse. We sit in a circle and talk about the story. Please bring your notebook. There are eight people in our group. New members are welcome.","title":"A reading group","evidence":"There are eight people in our group."}]}]},{"id":"4","label":"4級","sets":[{"n":1,"questions":[{"id":"4-01-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"I ( buy / bought / buying ) a notebook at that shop yesterday.","answer":"bought","accepted":["bought"],"why":"yesterdayは過去。buyの過去形はboughtです。"},{"id":"4-01-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Did Hana finish her homework? B: Yes, she ( did / does / is ).","answer":"did","accepted":["did"],"why":"Didで始まる質問にはdidで答えます。"},{"id":"4-01-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"This street is ( wide / wider / widest ) than the street near my school.","answer":"wider","accepted":["wider"],"why":"thanを伴って二つを比べるので比較級widerです。"},{"id":"4-01-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"Of the three boxes, this one is the ( heavy / heavier / heaviest ).","answer":"heaviest","accepted":["heaviest"],"why":"三つの中で最も重いので最上級heaviestです。"},{"id":"4-01-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"We are going ( visit / to visit / visiting ) our uncle next week.","answer":"to visit","accepted":["to visit"],"why":"be going toと動詞の原形で予定を表します。"},{"id":"4-01-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"I went to the station ( meet / to meet / met ) my cousin.","answer":"to meet","accepted":["to meet"],"why":"目的「会うために」はtoと動詞の原形で表します。"},{"id":"4-01-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"Thank you for ( help / helped / helping ) me with my bag.","answer":"helping","accepted":["helping"],"why":"前置詞forのあとで動作を表すにはing形を使います。"},{"id":"4-01-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"There isn't ( some / any / many ) milk in the bottle.","answer":"any","accepted":["any"],"why":"否定文で不特定の量を表すときはany。milkは数えない名詞です。"},{"id":"4-01-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"I went to bed early ( because / during / despite ) I was tired.","answer":"because","accepted":["because"],"why":"疲れていたことが早く寝た理由なのでBecauseです。"},{"id":"4-01-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: How ( long / far / many ) does the trip take? B: About forty minutes.","answer":"long","accepted":["long"],"why":"時間の長さをたずねるにはHow longです。距離はHow farです。"},{"id":"4-01-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"「私は昨日、駅で彼女に会いました。」( at the station / her / yesterday / I / met )","answer":"I met her at the station yesterday.","accepted":["I met her at the station yesterday.","Yesterday I met her at the station.","I met her yesterday at the station."],"why":"metはmeetの過去形。人herのあとに場所、時を置きます。"},{"id":"4-01-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"「私の兄は私より背が高いです。」( than / taller / my brother / I am / is )","answer":"My brother is taller than I am.","accepted":["My brother is taller than I am."],"why":"比較級tallerのあとにthanを置き、比べる相手を続けます。"},{"id":"4-01-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"「私たちは明日、公園を掃除する予定です。」( tomorrow / clean / going to / we / the park / are )","answer":"We are going to clean the park tomorrow.","accepted":["We are going to clean the park tomorrow.","Tomorrow we are going to clean the park."],"why":"are going to cleanで掃除する予定を表します。"},{"id":"4-01-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"「私は科学について学びたいです。」( about / want / science / I / to learn )","answer":"I want to learn about science.","accepted":["I want to learn about science."],"why":"want to learnは学びたい、about scienceは科学についてです。"},{"id":"4-01-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"集合は変更後、何時ですか。数字で答えなさい。","answer":"10","accepted":["10"],"why":"We will now meet at tenが新しい集合時刻。eightは変更前です。","context":"Our hiking club planned to meet at the station at eight on Sunday. The weather report says it will rain in the morning. We will now meet at ten, when the rain should stop. Please bring lunch and a jacket. The walk will take two hours.","title":"A club message"},{"id":"4-01-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"朝の天気予報を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"rain","accepted":["rain","rainy"],"why":"it will rain in the morningが根拠です。rainyも天気の表現として認めます。","context":"Our hiking club planned to meet at the station at eight on Sunday. The weather report says it will rain in the morning. We will now meet at ten, when the rain should stop. Please bring lunch and a jacket. The walk will take two hours.","title":"A club message"},{"id":"4-01-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"歩く時間は何時間ですか。数字で答えなさい。","answer":"2","accepted":["2"],"why":"The walk will take two hoursから2時間です。","context":"Our hiking club planned to meet at the station at eight on Sunday. The weather report says it will rain in the morning. We will now meet at ten, when the rain should stop. Please bring lunch and a jacket. The walk will take two hours.","title":"A club message"},{"id":"4-01-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"Rikuに料理を教えている家族を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"grandfather","accepted":["grandfather"],"why":"started cooking with his grandfatherから祖父です。","context":"Last month, Riku started cooking with his grandfather. At first, cutting vegetables was difficult for him. He practiced every Saturday. Yesterday he made vegetable soup for his family. His sister asked for another bowl. Next weekend he wants to make bread.","title":"A new hobby"},{"id":"4-01-19","n":19,"kind":"reading","q":"Rikuが練習した曜日を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"Saturday","accepted":["Saturday"],"why":"He practiced every Saturdayが根拠です。","context":"Last month, Riku started cooking with his grandfather. At first, cutting vegetables was difficult for him. He practiced every Saturday. Yesterday he made vegetable soup for his family. His sister asked for another bowl. Next weekend he wants to make bread.","title":"A new hobby"},{"id":"4-01-20","n":20,"kind":"reading","q":"次に作りたい食べ物を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"bread","accepted":["bread"],"why":"Next weekend he wants to make breadが根拠です。","context":"Last month, Riku started cooking with his grandfather. At first, cutting vegetables was difficult for him. He practiced every Saturday. Yesterday he made vegetable soup for his family. His sister asked for another bowl. Next weekend he wants to make bread.","title":"A new hobby"}]},{"n":2,"questions":[{"id":"4-02-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"We ( saw / see / seen ) a rainbow after the storm yesterday.","answer":"saw","accepted":["saw"],"why":"yesterdayに合わせ、seeの過去形sawを使います。"},{"id":"4-02-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Did the bus arrive on time? B: No, it ( didn't / doesn't / wasn't ).","answer":"didn't","accepted":["didn't"],"why":"Didへの否定の返事はdidn'tです。"},{"id":"4-02-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"My suitcase is ( heavier / heavy / heaviest ) than yours.","answer":"heavier","accepted":["heavier"],"why":"thanで二つを比較するので比較級heavierです。"},{"id":"4-02-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"This is the ( oldest / older / old ) building in our town.","answer":"oldest","accepted":["oldest"],"why":"町全体で最も古いので最上級oldestです。"},{"id":"4-02-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"They are going ( to build / building / build ) a new playground.","answer":"to build","accepted":["to build"],"why":"be going toと動詞の原形で予定を表します。"},{"id":"4-02-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"I saved money ( to buy / bought / buy ) a bicycle.","answer":"to buy","accepted":["to buy"],"why":"目的「買うために」はtoと動詞の原形です。"},{"id":"4-02-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"My grandmother enjoys ( gardening / garden / gardens ).","answer":"gardening","accepted":["gardening"],"why":"enjoyの目的語に動作を置く場合はing形を使います。"},{"id":"4-02-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"There aren't ( any / some / much ) clean cups in the cupboard.","answer":"any","accepted":["any"],"why":"否定文で数や量があるかを表すのはanyです。"},{"id":"4-02-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"We stayed inside ( because / during / despite ) it was snowing.","answer":"because","accepted":["because"],"why":"後ろが主語と動詞を持つ理由の節なのでbecauseです。"},{"id":"4-02-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: How ( often / many / much ) do you visit your uncle? B: Once a month.","answer":"often","accepted":["often"],"why":"頻度を尋ねるHow oftenです。"},{"id":"4-02-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私は昨夜、料理の番組を見ました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( night / watched / I / a / cooking / last / program )","answer":"I watched a cooking program last night.","accepted":["I watched a cooking program last night."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-02-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"この道はあの道より短いです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( shorter / that / is / road / This / than / one )","answer":"This road is shorter than that one.","accepted":["This road is shorter than that one."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 比較する相手はthanの後ろに置きます。"},{"id":"4-02-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私たちは来週、博物館を訪ねるつもりです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( museum / the / We / visit / next / going / to / are / week )","answer":"We are going to visit the museum next week.","accepted":["We are going to visit the museum next week."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-02-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"彼女はピアノを弾くことを楽しみます。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( enjoys / She / the / playing / piano )","answer":"She enjoys playing the piano.","accepted":["She enjoys playing the piano."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-02-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"変更後の練習開始時刻を数字で書きなさい（時:分）。","answer":"5:30","accepted":["5:30"],"why":"本文の根拠：practice will now start at five thirty.","context":"Our basketball practice was going to start at four on Thursday. The gym will be used for a school meeting until five, so practice will now start at five thirty. Please bring indoor shoes. We will finish at seven. Ask the coach if you cannot stay until then.","title":"A changed practice","evidence":"practice will now start at five thirty."},{"id":"4-02-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"体育館を先に使う行事を英語2語で答えなさい。","answer":"school meeting","accepted":["school meeting"],"why":"本文の根拠：The gym will be used for a school meeting until five, so practice will now start at five thirty.","context":"Our basketball practice was going to start at four on Thursday. The gym will be used for a school meeting until five, so practice will now start at five thirty. Please bring indoor shoes. We will finish at seven. Ask the coach if you cannot stay until then.","title":"A changed practice","evidence":"The gym will be used for a school meeting until five, so practice will now start at five thirty."},{"id":"4-02-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"練習の終了時刻を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"7","accepted":["7"],"why":"本文の根拠：We will finish at seven.","context":"Our basketball practice was going to start at four on Thursday. The gym will be used for a school meeting until five, so practice will now start at five thirty. Please bring indoor shoes. We will finish at seven. Ask the coach if you cannot stay until then.","title":"A changed practice","evidence":"We will finish at seven."},{"id":"4-02-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"Sotaが入れすぎた材料を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"milk","accepted":["milk"],"why":"本文の根拠：He used too much milk, and the mixture was very thin.","context":"Sota wanted to make pancakes for his mother. He used too much milk, and the mixture was very thin. His older sister showed him how to add more flour. The pancakes became better. Next time, Sota will measure the ingredients carefully before mixing them. His mother thanked both children.","title":"A useful mistake","evidence":"He used too much milk, and the mixture was very thin."},{"id":"4-02-19","n":19,"kind":"reading","q":"姉が足すように教えた材料を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"flour","accepted":["flour"],"why":"本文の根拠：His older sister showed him how to add more flour.","context":"Sota wanted to make pancakes for his mother. He used too much milk, and the mixture was very thin. His older sister showed him how to add more flour. The pancakes became better. Next time, Sota will measure the ingredients carefully before mixing them. His mother thanked both children.","title":"A useful mistake","evidence":"His older sister showed him how to add more flour."},{"id":"4-02-20","n":20,"kind":"reading","q":"次回、混ぜる前に材料に対して行う動作を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"measure","accepted":["measure"],"why":"本文の根拠：Next time, Sota will measure the ingredients carefully before mixing them.","context":"Sota wanted to make pancakes for his mother. He used too much milk, and the mixture was very thin. His older sister showed him how to add more flour. The pancakes became better. Next time, Sota will measure the ingredients carefully before mixing them. His mother thanked both children.","title":"A useful mistake","evidence":"Next time, Sota will measure the ingredients carefully before mixing them."}]},{"n":3,"questions":[{"id":"4-03-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"Hana ( wrote / writes / written ) a postcard last night.","answer":"wrote","accepted":["wrote"],"why":"last nightは過去。writeの過去形はwroteです。"},{"id":"4-03-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"There ( were / was / is ) many people at the concert yesterday.","answer":"were","accepted":["were"],"why":"過去で主語が複数のmany peopleなのでwereです。"},{"id":"4-03-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"A horse is usually ( larger / large / largest ) than a sheep.","answer":"larger","accepted":["larger"],"why":"二つの大きさを比べるので比較級largerです。"},{"id":"4-03-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"Of the five runners, Mai was the ( fastest / faster / fast ).","answer":"fastest","accepted":["fastest"],"why":"五人の中で一番速いので最上級fastestです。"},{"id":"4-03-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"I will ( call / calls / called ) you after lunch.","answer":"call","accepted":["call"],"why":"助動詞willの後は動詞の原形です。"},{"id":"4-03-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"My father wants ( to learn / learning / learned ) Spanish.","answer":"to learn","accepted":["to learn"],"why":"wantのあとにtoと動詞の原形を置きます。"},{"id":"4-03-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"Thank you for ( inviting / invite / invited ) me to your party.","answer":"inviting","accepted":["inviting"],"why":"前置詞forの後にはing形を使います。"},{"id":"4-03-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Would you like ( some / any / many ) juice? B: Yes, please.","answer":"some","accepted":["some"],"why":"肯定の返答を期待する申し出にはsomeを使います。"},{"id":"4-03-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: ( Why / Where / When ) did you leave early? B: Because I felt sick.","answer":"Why","accepted":["Why"],"why":"理由を答えているので疑問詞はWhyです。"},{"id":"4-03-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"Please ( take off / turn on / pick up ) your shoes before entering the room.","answer":"take off","accepted":["take off"],"why":"靴を脱ぐという動作はtake offです。"},{"id":"4-03-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私の祖父は昨日、魚を二匹釣りました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( two / caught / fish / My / grandfather / yesterday )","answer":"My grandfather caught two fish yesterday.","accepted":["My grandfather caught two fish yesterday."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-03-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"これは町で一番高い建物です。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( tallest / the / is / This / building / in / town )","answer":"This is the tallest building in town.","accepted":["This is the tallest building in town."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-03-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私は水泳を練習するために早く起きました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( I / got / practice / early / to / up / swimming )","answer":"I got up early to practice swimming.","accepted":["I got up early to practice swimming."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-03-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"あなたはどのくらいの頻度で図書館へ行きますか。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( go / to / do / How / often / library / you / the )","answer":"How often do you go to the library?","accepted":["How often do you go to the library?"],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-03-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"集合場所を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"school","accepted":["school"],"why":"本文の根拠：The group will meet at school at nine and take a bus.","context":"Class 1B will visit the city museum next Tuesday. The group will meet at school at nine and take a bus. Students must bring a notebook, but lunch will be provided at the museum cafe. The museum has a new exhibition about ships. We will return to school at three.","title":"A museum trip","evidence":"The group will meet at school at nine and take a bus."},{"id":"4-03-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"新しい展示のテーマを本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"ships","accepted":["ships"],"why":"本文の根拠：The museum has a new exhibition about ships.","context":"Class 1B will visit the city museum next Tuesday. The group will meet at school at nine and take a bus. Students must bring a notebook, but lunch will be provided at the museum cafe. The museum has a new exhibition about ships. We will return to school at three.","title":"A museum trip","evidence":"The museum has a new exhibition about ships."},{"id":"4-03-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"学校に戻る時刻を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"3","accepted":["3"],"why":"本文の根拠：We will return to school at three.","context":"Class 1B will visit the city museum next Tuesday. The group will meet at school at nine and take a bus. Students must bring a notebook, but lunch will be provided at the museum cafe. The museum has a new exhibition about ships. We will return to school at three.","title":"A museum trip","evidence":"We will return to school at three."},{"id":"4-03-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"Emmaが最初に泳げた距離を数字で答えなさい（m）。","answer":"5","accepted":["5"],"why":"本文の根拠：At first, she could swim only five meters.","context":"Last summer, Emma was afraid of swimming. She started lessons with a patient teacher. At first, she could swim only five meters. After eight lessons, she could swim twenty meters. She now enjoys going to the pool with her friends. She wants to try a longer distance next month.","title":"Learning to swim","evidence":"At first, she could swim only five meters."},{"id":"4-03-19","n":19,"kind":"reading","q":"20m泳げるようになるまで受けたレッスンの回数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"8","accepted":["8"],"why":"本文の根拠：After eight lessons, she could swim twenty meters.","context":"Last summer, Emma was afraid of swimming. She started lessons with a patient teacher. At first, she could swim only five meters. After eight lessons, she could swim twenty meters. She now enjoys going to the pool with her friends. She wants to try a longer distance next month.","title":"Learning to swim","evidence":"After eight lessons, she could swim twenty meters."},{"id":"4-03-20","n":20,"kind":"reading","q":"今一緒にプールへ行く相手を本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"friends","accepted":["friends"],"why":"本文の根拠：She now enjoys going to the pool with her friends.","context":"Last summer, Emma was afraid of swimming. She started lessons with a patient teacher. At first, she could swim only five meters. After eight lessons, she could swim twenty meters. She now enjoys going to the pool with her friends. She wants to try a longer distance next month.","title":"Learning to swim","evidence":"She now enjoys going to the pool with her friends."}]},{"n":4,"questions":[{"id":"4-04-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"I ( found / find / finding ) my lost key under the sofa yesterday.","answer":"found","accepted":["found"],"why":"findの過去形はfoundです。"},{"id":"4-04-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Were you at the library? B: Yes, I ( was / were / did ).","answer":"was","accepted":["was"],"why":"Were youへの答えは主語がIになるのでwasです。"},{"id":"4-04-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"This question is ( easier / easy / easiest ) than the last one.","answer":"easier","accepted":["easier"],"why":"easyの比較級はyをiに変えてeasierです。"},{"id":"4-04-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"This chair is the ( most comfortable / more comfortable / comfortable ) of all.","answer":"most comfortable","accepted":["most comfortable"],"why":"三つ以上を比べ、長い形容詞の最上級はmostを前に置きます。"},{"id":"4-04-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"It is going to ( rain / rains / raining ) this afternoon.","answer":"rain","accepted":["rain"],"why":"be going toの後は動詞の原形です。"},{"id":"4-04-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"We went to the library ( to study / studied / studying ) together.","answer":"to study","accepted":["to study"],"why":"勉強するためにという目的はto studyです。"},{"id":"4-04-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"My sister finished ( cleaning / clean / cleans ) the kitchen.","answer":"cleaning","accepted":["cleaning"],"why":"finishのあとに動作を続けるときはing形です。"},{"id":"4-04-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"I need a ( few / little / much ) more pencils for the class.","answer":"few","accepted":["few"],"why":"pencilsは数えられる複数名詞なのでa fewです。"},{"id":"4-04-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"I was brushing my teeth ( when / during / because of ) the phone rang.","answer":"when","accepted":["when"],"why":"出来事の時を示すwhen。duringとbecause ofには節を直接続けません。"},{"id":"4-04-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: How ( far / long / old ) is the station from here? B: About two kilometers.","answer":"far","accepted":["far"],"why":"距離を尋ねるHow farです。"},{"id":"4-04-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"昨日はとてもたくさん雨が降りました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( lot / rained / It / yesterday / a )","answer":"It rained a lot yesterday.","accepted":["It rained a lot yesterday."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-04-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"この映画はあの映画より面白いです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( more / than / film / one / is / interesting / that / This )","answer":"This film is more interesting than that one.","accepted":["This film is more interesting than that one."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 比較する相手はthanの後ろに置きます。"},{"id":"4-04-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私は将来、医者になりたいです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( to / a / want / doctor / I / the / in / future / be )","answer":"I want to be a doctor in the future.","accepted":["I want to be a doctor in the future."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-04-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"彼は写真を撮るのが得意です。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( is / pictures / taking / good / at / He )","answer":"He is good at taking pictures.","accepted":["He is good at taking pictures."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-04-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"子供の切符の値段を数字で答えなさい（ドル）。","answer":"6","accepted":["6"],"why":"本文の根拠：Adults pay twelve dollars, and children pay six dollars.","context":"The Green Line has a special weekend ticket. Adults pay twelve dollars, and children pay six dollars. The ticket is valid on Saturday or Sunday, but only for one day. You can get on and off at any Green Line station. Buy it at the station, not on the train.","title":"A weekend train ticket","evidence":"Adults pay twelve dollars, and children pay six dollars."},{"id":"4-04-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"一枚の切符を使える日数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"1","accepted":["1"],"why":"本文の根拠：The ticket is valid on Saturday or Sunday, but only for one day.","context":"The Green Line has a special weekend ticket. Adults pay twelve dollars, and children pay six dollars. The ticket is valid on Saturday or Sunday, but only for one day. You can get on and off at any Green Line station. Buy it at the station, not on the train.","title":"A weekend train ticket","evidence":"The ticket is valid on Saturday or Sunday, but only for one day."},{"id":"4-04-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"切符を購入する場所を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"station","accepted":["station"],"why":"本文の根拠：Buy it at the station, not on the train.","context":"The Green Line has a special weekend ticket. Adults pay twelve dollars, and children pay six dollars. The ticket is valid on Saturday or Sunday, but only for one day. You can get on and off at any Green Line station. Buy it at the station, not on the train.","title":"A weekend train ticket","evidence":"Buy it at the station, not on the train."},{"id":"4-04-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"水に落ちたものを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"notebook","accepted":["notebook"],"why":"本文の根拠：His notebook fell into the water.","context":"Leo dropped his bag near a pond. His notebook fell into the water. A woman walking her dog stopped to help. She used a long branch to reach the notebook. Leo dried the pages at home. Some words were hard to read, so he copied his friend's notes the next day.","title":"An unexpected helper","evidence":"His notebook fell into the water."},{"id":"4-04-19","n":19,"kind":"reading","q":"助けた人が使ったものを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"branch","accepted":["branch"],"why":"本文の根拠：She used a long branch to reach the notebook.","context":"Leo dropped his bag near a pond. His notebook fell into the water. A woman walking her dog stopped to help. She used a long branch to reach the notebook. Leo dried the pages at home. Some words were hard to read, so he copied his friend's notes the next day.","title":"An unexpected helper","evidence":"She used a long branch to reach the notebook."},{"id":"4-04-20","n":20,"kind":"reading","q":"ページを乾かした場所を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"home","accepted":["home"],"why":"本文の根拠：Leo dried the pages at home.","context":"Leo dropped his bag near a pond. His notebook fell into the water. A woman walking her dog stopped to help. She used a long branch to reach the notebook. Leo dried the pages at home. Some words were hard to read, so he copied his friend's notes the next day.","title":"An unexpected helper","evidence":"Leo dried the pages at home."}]},{"n":5,"questions":[{"id":"4-05-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"The children ( ate / eat / eaten ) all the cookies this morning.","answer":"ate","accepted":["ate"],"why":"過去の出来事。eatの過去形はateです。"},{"id":"4-05-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Did you take any photos? B: Yes, I ( did / was / do ).","answer":"did","accepted":["did"],"why":"Didで始まる過去の質問にはdidで答えます。"},{"id":"4-05-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"A train is usually ( faster / fast / fastest ) than a bicycle.","answer":"faster","accepted":["faster"],"why":"二つを比べるので比較級fasterです。"},{"id":"4-05-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"Which is the ( longest / longer / long ) river in this country?","answer":"longest","accepted":["longest"],"why":"国内全体で一番長い川をたずねる最上級です。"},{"id":"4-05-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"We ( will / did / were ) leave tomorrow morning.","answer":"will","accepted":["will"],"why":"tomorrowに合わせ未来のwillを使い、その後に原形leaveを続けます。"},{"id":"4-05-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"I hope ( to become / became / becoming ) a nurse.","answer":"to become","accepted":["to become"],"why":"hopeの後はtoと動詞の原形で希望を表します。"},{"id":"4-05-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"Yuki is good at ( drawing / draw / draws ) animals.","answer":"drawing","accepted":["drawing"],"why":"前置詞atの後にはing形です。"},{"id":"4-05-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"There is a ( little / few / many ) water left in the jug.","answer":"little","accepted":["little"],"why":"waterは数えない名詞なのでa littleです。"},{"id":"4-05-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"You can go out ( if / during / because of ) you finish your homework.","answer":"if","accepted":["if"],"why":"条件を表すifの後に主語と動詞を置きます。"},{"id":"4-05-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"Please ( turn off / get up / take off ) the lights before you leave.","answer":"turn off","accepted":["turn off"],"why":"照明を消す動作はturn offです。"},{"id":"4-05-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私は今朝、電車に乗り遅れました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( train / I / the / missed / this / morning )","answer":"I missed the train this morning.","accepted":["I missed the train this morning."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-05-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"私の兄は家族の中で一番上手に歌います。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( sings / brother / family / My / the / best / in / my )","answer":"My brother sings the best in my family.","accepted":["My brother sings the best in my family."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-05-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"明日の午後、私はあなたに電話します。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( tomorrow / call / will / you / afternoon / I )","answer":"I will call you tomorrow afternoon.","accepted":["I will call you tomorrow afternoon."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-05-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"彼らはその試合について話すのをやめました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( stopped / about / talking / They / the / game )","answer":"They stopped talking about the game.","accepted":["They stopped talking about the game."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-05-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"青いスカーフの値段を数字で答えなさい（ドル）。","answer":"20","accepted":["20"],"why":"本文の根拠：A blue scarf cost twenty dollars, and a green one cost fifteen.","context":"Mina wanted to buy a gift for her grandfather. A blue scarf cost twenty dollars, and a green one cost fifteen. She had eighteen dollars. She bought the green scarf and a card for two dollars. Her grandfather said the scarf was warm and the color was his favorite.","title":"Choosing a gift","evidence":"A blue scarf cost twenty dollars, and a green one cost fifteen."},{"id":"4-05-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"Minaが買ったスカーフの色を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"green","accepted":["green"],"why":"本文の根拠：She bought the green scarf and a card for two dollars.","context":"Mina wanted to buy a gift for her grandfather. A blue scarf cost twenty dollars, and a green one cost fifteen. She had eighteen dollars. She bought the green scarf and a card for two dollars. Her grandfather said the scarf was warm and the color was his favorite.","title":"Choosing a gift","evidence":"She bought the green scarf and a card for two dollars."},{"id":"4-05-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"スカーフとカードを買って残った金額を数字で答えなさい（ドル）。","answer":"1","accepted":["1"],"why":"本文の根拠：She had eighteen dollars. She bought the green scarf and a card for two dollars. 持っていた18ドルから15ドルと2ドルを引くと1ドルです。","context":"Mina wanted to buy a gift for her grandfather. A blue scarf cost twenty dollars, and a green one cost fifteen. She had eighteen dollars. She bought the green scarf and a card for two dollars. Her grandfather said the scarf was warm and the color was his favorite.","title":"Choosing a gift","evidence":"She had eighteen dollars. She bought the green scarf and a card for two dollars."},{"id":"4-05-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"植えた植物を本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"beans","accepted":["beans"],"why":"本文の根拠：Our class planted beans in April.","context":"Our class planted beans in April. We put two pots by a sunny window and two in a darker corner. We gave all the plants the same amount of water. After two weeks, the plants near the window were taller. We will put all four pots near the window now.","title":"A garden project","evidence":"Our class planted beans in April."},{"id":"4-05-19","n":19,"kind":"reading","q":"鉢の合計数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"4","accepted":["4"],"why":"本文の根拠：We put two pots by a sunny window and two in a darker corner. 窓際2鉢と暗い場所2鉢を足すと4鉢です。","context":"Our class planted beans in April. We put two pots by a sunny window and two in a darker corner. We gave all the plants the same amount of water. After two weeks, the plants near the window were taller. We will put all four pots near the window now.","title":"A garden project","evidence":"We put two pots by a sunny window and two in a darker corner."},{"id":"4-05-20","n":20,"kind":"reading","q":"今後すべての鉢を置く場所は何の近くですか。英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"window","accepted":["window"],"why":"本文の根拠：We will put all four pots near the window now.","context":"Our class planted beans in April. We put two pots by a sunny window and two in a darker corner. We gave all the plants the same amount of water. After two weeks, the plants near the window were taller. We will put all four pots near the window now.","title":"A garden project","evidence":"We will put all four pots near the window now."}]},{"n":6,"questions":[{"id":"4-06-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"We ( brought / bring / bringing ) our own lunch to the picnic yesterday.","answer":"brought","accepted":["brought"],"why":"bringの過去形はbroughtです。"},{"id":"4-06-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Was your brother asleep? B: No, he ( wasn't / didn't / weren't ).","answer":"wasn't","accepted":["wasn't"],"why":"Wasの質問にはwasn'tで否定します。"},{"id":"4-06-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"This winter is ( colder / cold / coldest ) than last winter.","answer":"colder","accepted":["colder"],"why":"thanを使って比べるので比較級colderです。"},{"id":"4-06-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"Of these four films, that one is the ( most interesting / more interesting / interesting ).","answer":"most interesting","accepted":["most interesting"],"why":"四つの中で最も面白いのでmost interestingです。"},{"id":"4-06-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Will you join us? B: Yes, I ( will / do / am ).","answer":"will","accepted":["will"],"why":"Willで始まる質問にwillで答えます。"},{"id":"4-06-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"I would like ( to try / trying / tried ) the new restaurant.","answer":"to try","accepted":["to try"],"why":"would like toと動詞の原形で希望を丁寧に伝えます。"},{"id":"4-06-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"He stopped ( talking / talk / talks ) when the teacher came in.","answer":"talking","accepted":["talking"],"why":"stop talkingは話すのをやめるという意味です。"},{"id":"4-06-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"How ( many / much / long ) students are in your class?","answer":"many","accepted":["many"],"why":"studentsは数えられる複数名詞なのでHow manyです。"},{"id":"4-06-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"I couldn't sleep ( because / during / despite ) the room was too hot.","answer":"because","accepted":["because"],"why":"主語と動詞のある理由の節を続けるbecauseです。"},{"id":"4-06-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"Our meeting will last ( for / at / on ) an hour.","answer":"for","accepted":["for"],"why":"継続する時間の長さにはforを使います。"},{"id":"4-06-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"彼女は昨日、帽子をなくしました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( lost / her / hat / yesterday / She )","answer":"She lost her hat yesterday.","accepted":["She lost her hat yesterday."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-06-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"その青い箱は赤い箱より重いです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( the / box / box / is / heavier / than / red / blue / The )","answer":"The blue box is heavier than the red box.","accepted":["The blue box is heavier than the red box."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 比較する相手はthanの後ろに置きます。"},{"id":"4-06-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私たちは駅で会うことに決めました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( the / meet / decided / to / We / station / at )","answer":"We decided to meet at the station.","accepted":["We decided to meet at the station."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-06-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"この旅行はどのくらい時間がかかりますか。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( this / How / trip / long / does / take )","answer":"How long does this trip take?","accepted":["How long does this trip take?"],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-06-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"高価なカメラの代わりに使える機器を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"phone","accepted":["phone"],"why":"本文の根拠：You do not need an expensive camera; a phone camera is fine.","context":"Would you like to join our photo club? We meet every other Saturday at ten. You do not need an expensive camera; a phone camera is fine. At our next meeting, we will photograph trees in the park. The meeting lasts ninety minutes. Please send an email before Friday if you want to come.","title":"A club invitation","evidence":"You do not need an expensive camera; a phone camera is fine."},{"id":"4-06-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"次回撮るものを本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"trees","accepted":["trees"],"why":"本文の根拠：At our next meeting, we will photograph trees in the park.","context":"Would you like to join our photo club? We meet every other Saturday at ten. You do not need an expensive camera; a phone camera is fine. At our next meeting, we will photograph trees in the park. The meeting lasts ninety minutes. Please send an email before Friday if you want to come.","title":"A club invitation","evidence":"At our next meeting, we will photograph trees in the park."},{"id":"4-06-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"会の所要時間を数字で答えなさい（分）。","answer":"90","accepted":["90"],"why":"本文の根拠：The meeting lasts ninety minutes.","context":"Would you like to join our photo club? We meet every other Saturday at ten. You do not need an expensive camera; a phone camera is fine. At our next meeting, we will photograph trees in the park. The meeting lasts ninety minutes. Please send an email before Friday if you want to come.","title":"A club invitation","evidence":"The meeting lasts ninety minutes."},{"id":"4-06-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"普段の道で閉鎖されているものを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"bridge","accepted":["bridge"],"why":"本文の根拠：A bridge on Taro's usual route to school is closed for repairs.","context":"A bridge on Taro's usual route to school is closed for repairs. He now walks through a small park. The new route takes fifteen minutes, five minutes longer than before. Taro likes it because he can see birds near the pond. The bridge will open again next month.","title":"A different route","evidence":"A bridge on Taro's usual route to school is closed for repairs."},{"id":"4-06-19","n":19,"kind":"reading","q":"元の通学時間は何分でしたか。数字で答えなさい。","answer":"10","accepted":["10"],"why":"本文の根拠：The new route takes fifteen minutes, five minutes longer than before. 新しい15分は元より5分長いので、15 - 5 = 10分です。","context":"A bridge on Taro's usual route to school is closed for repairs. He now walks through a small park. The new route takes fifteen minutes, five minutes longer than before. Taro likes it because he can see birds near the pond. The bridge will open again next month.","title":"A different route","evidence":"The new route takes fifteen minutes, five minutes longer than before."},{"id":"4-06-20","n":20,"kind":"reading","q":"新しい道でTaroが見られるものを本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"birds","accepted":["birds"],"why":"本文の根拠：Taro likes it because he can see birds near the pond.","context":"A bridge on Taro's usual route to school is closed for repairs. He now walks through a small park. The new route takes fifteen minutes, five minutes longer than before. Taro likes it because he can see birds near the pond. The bridge will open again next month.","title":"A different route","evidence":"Taro likes it because he can see birds near the pond."}]},{"n":7,"questions":[{"id":"4-07-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"My dad ( made / make / makes ) a wooden shelf last weekend.","answer":"made","accepted":["made"],"why":"last weekendは過去。makeの過去形はmadeです。"},{"id":"4-07-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"I ( was reading / readed / am read ) a book when the doorbell rang.","answer":"was reading","accepted":["was reading"],"why":"過去のある時に進行中だった動作はwasとing形です。"},{"id":"4-07-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"My new bag is ( more useful / most useful / usefully ) than the old one.","answer":"more useful","accepted":["more useful"],"why":"thanによる比較なのでmore usefulです。"},{"id":"4-07-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"Today is the ( hottest / hotter / hot ) day of the month.","answer":"hottest","accepted":["hottest"],"why":"月全体の中で最も暑い日なので最上級hottestです。"},{"id":"4-07-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"I'm going ( to send / sending / sent ) this package tomorrow.","answer":"to send","accepted":["to send"],"why":"am going toと原形sendで予定を表します。"},{"id":"4-07-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"It is fun ( to ride / ridden / ride ) a horse.","answer":"to ride","accepted":["to ride"],"why":"It is形容詞to動詞で、何が楽しいかを説明します。"},{"id":"4-07-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"They practiced ( singing / sang / sing ) the song every day.","answer":"singing","accepted":["singing"],"why":"practiceのあとで動作を示すにはing形を使います。"},{"id":"4-07-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"How ( much / many / few ) bread should we buy?","answer":"much","accepted":["much"],"why":"breadは数えない名詞なのでHow muchです。"},{"id":"4-07-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"( Before / During / Because of ) you cook, wash your hands.","answer":"Before","accepted":["Before"],"why":"節の前で「～する前に」を表すBeforeを使います。"},{"id":"4-07-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"She walks to school ( instead of / next to / in front of ) taking a bus.","answer":"instead of","accepted":["instead of"],"why":"バスに乗る代わりに歩くのでinstead ofです。"},{"id":"4-07-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私たちは昨夏、北海道へ行きました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( to / Hokkaido / We / summer / last / went )","answer":"We went to Hokkaido last summer.","accepted":["We went to Hokkaido last summer."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-07-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"これは三つの中で一番小さいカップです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( the / three / smallest / This / cup / of / is / the )","answer":"This is the smallest cup of the three.","accepted":["This is the smallest cup of the three."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-07-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私は数学の宿題をする必要があります。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( math / to / do / my / homework / I / have )","answer":"I have to do my math homework.","accepted":["I have to do my math homework."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 have to＋動詞の原形で「～する必要がある」を表し、haveの後にtoを置きます。"},{"id":"4-07-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"私を待ってくれてありがとう。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( me / you / waiting / Thank / for / for )","answer":"Thank you for waiting for me.","accepted":["Thank you for waiting for me."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-07-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"座席予約の締切は12月何日ですか。数字で答えなさい。","answer":"3","accepted":["3"],"why":"本文の根拠：You can reserve by calling the school office until December third.","context":"The school concert is on December fifth. Tickets are free, but everyone must reserve a seat. You can reserve by calling the school office until December third. The doors open at six, and the music starts at six thirty. Please arrive early because the first song is very quiet.","title":"A school concert","evidence":"You can reserve by calling the school office until December third."},{"id":"4-07-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"開場時刻を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"6","accepted":["6"],"why":"本文の根拠：The doors open at six, and the music starts at six thirty.","context":"The school concert is on December fifth. Tickets are free, but everyone must reserve a seat. You can reserve by calling the school office until December third. The doors open at six, and the music starts at six thirty. Please arrive early because the first song is very quiet.","title":"A school concert","evidence":"The doors open at six, and the music starts at six thirty."},{"id":"4-07-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"演奏の開始時刻を数字で書きなさい（時:分）。","answer":"6:30","accepted":["6:30"],"why":"本文の根拠：The doors open at six, and the music starts at six thirty.","context":"The school concert is on December fifth. Tickets are free, but everyone must reserve a seat. You can reserve by calling the school office until December third. The doors open at six, and the music starts at six thirty. Please arrive early because the first song is very quiet.","title":"A school concert","evidence":"The doors open at six, and the music starts at six thirty."},{"id":"4-07-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"一週間に弁当を作る日数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"3","accepted":["3"],"why":"本文の根拠：This month, she started making her own lunch three days a week.","context":"Aki used to buy lunch at school every day. This month, she started making her own lunch three days a week. She cooks extra rice at dinner and keeps it for the next morning. Her father helps her cut vegetables. Aki says making lunch saves money and is more fun than she expected.","title":"Making a lunch box","evidence":"This month, she started making her own lunch three days a week."},{"id":"4-07-19","n":19,"kind":"reading","q":"夕食時に多めに作る食べ物を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"rice","accepted":["rice"],"why":"本文の根拠：She cooks extra rice at dinner and keeps it for the next morning.","context":"Aki used to buy lunch at school every day. This month, she started making her own lunch three days a week. She cooks extra rice at dinner and keeps it for the next morning. Her father helps her cut vegetables. Aki says making lunch saves money and is more fun than she expected.","title":"Making a lunch box","evidence":"She cooks extra rice at dinner and keeps it for the next morning."},{"id":"4-07-20","n":20,"kind":"reading","q":"野菜を切るのを手伝う家族を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"father","accepted":["father"],"why":"本文の根拠：Her father helps her cut vegetables.","context":"Aki used to buy lunch at school every day. This month, she started making her own lunch three days a week. She cooks extra rice at dinner and keeps it for the next morning. Her father helps her cut vegetables. Aki says making lunch saves money and is more fun than she expected.","title":"Making a lunch box","evidence":"Her father helps her cut vegetables."}]},{"n":8,"questions":[{"id":"4-08-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"I ( lost / lose / losing ) my ticket on the way to the theater.","answer":"lost","accepted":["lost"],"why":"loseの過去形はlostです。"},{"id":"4-08-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: What ( were / are / do ) you doing at nine last night? B: Watching TV.","answer":"were","accepted":["were"],"why":"last nightのある時点の動作なので過去進行形were doingです。"},{"id":"4-08-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"This apple is ( sweeter / sweet / sweetest ) than that one.","answer":"sweeter","accepted":["sweeter"],"why":"二つの甘さを比べるので比較級sweeterです。"},{"id":"4-08-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"Sunday is the ( busiest / busier / busy ) day of the week at this shop.","answer":"busiest","accepted":["busiest"],"why":"一週間で最も忙しいという最上級。busyはbusiestになります。"},{"id":"4-08-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"We ( are going to / did / were ) visit the zoo next Friday.","answer":"are going to","accepted":["are going to"],"why":"next Fridayの予定なのでare going toです。"},{"id":"4-08-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"Riku decided ( to join / joining / joins ) the science club.","answer":"to join","accepted":["to join"],"why":"decideの後にtoと原形を置きます。"},{"id":"4-08-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"How about ( making / make / made ) a poster for the festival?","answer":"making","accepted":["making"],"why":"How aboutの後で動作を表すにはing形です。"},{"id":"4-08-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"I don't have ( enough / many / several ) time to finish this today.","answer":"enough","accepted":["enough"],"why":"timeは数えない名詞で、十分な時間という意味のenoughです。"},{"id":"4-08-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"We left ( after / during / because of ) the rain stopped.","answer":"after","accepted":["after"],"why":"主語と動詞のある節を続けられるafterです。"},{"id":"4-08-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"Please ( look after / look for / look at ) my dog while I am away.","answer":"look after","accepted":["look after"],"why":"不在の間、世話をするのでlook afterです。"},{"id":"4-08-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私は昨夜、本を読むのを終えました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( I / reading / book / finished / last / night / the )","answer":"I finished reading the book last night.","accepted":["I finished reading the book last night."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-08-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"私の新しい靴は古い靴より快適です。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( My / are / more / old / ones / shoes / than / new / my / comfortable )","answer":"My new shoes are more comfortable than my old ones.","accepted":["My new shoes are more comfortable than my old ones."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 比較する相手はthanの後ろに置きます。"},{"id":"4-08-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"雨が降っていたので、私たちは家にいました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( it / stayed / was / raining / because / at / home / We )","answer":"We stayed at home because it was raining.","accepted":["We stayed at home because it was raining."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-08-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"彼女は友達に会うために東京へ行きました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( see / Tokyo / went / to / She / her / friend / to )","answer":"She went to Tokyo to see her friend.","accepted":["She went to Tokyo to see her friend."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-08-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"値引きされるスポーツ用品を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"rackets","accepted":["rackets"],"why":"本文の根拠：Before we move, all tennis rackets are twenty percent off.","context":"We are moving our sports shop next month. Before we move, all tennis rackets are twenty percent off. The sale ends on October twelfth. The shop will close for three days and reopen on October sixteenth at our new location beside the station. Other items are sold at their usual prices.","title":"A sports shop notice","evidence":"Before we move, all tennis rackets are twenty percent off."},{"id":"4-08-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"セール終了日は10月何日ですか。数字で答えなさい。","answer":"12","accepted":["12"],"why":"本文の根拠：The sale ends on October twelfth.","context":"We are moving our sports shop next month. Before we move, all tennis rackets are twenty percent off. The sale ends on October twelfth. The shop will close for three days and reopen on October sixteenth at our new location beside the station. Other items are sold at their usual prices.","title":"A sports shop notice","evidence":"The sale ends on October twelfth."},{"id":"4-08-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"新しい店は何の隣にありますか。英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"station","accepted":["station"],"why":"本文の根拠：The shop will close for three days and reopen on October sixteenth at our new location beside the station.","context":"We are moving our sports shop next month. Before we move, all tennis rackets are twenty percent off. The sale ends on October twelfth. The shop will close for three days and reopen on October sixteenth at our new location beside the station. Other items are sold at their usual prices.","title":"A sports shop notice","evidence":"The shop will close for three days and reopen on October sixteenth at our new location beside the station."},{"id":"4-08-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"Yunaが作った案内資料を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"map","accepted":["map"],"why":"本文の根拠：Yuna made a map for the information desk.","context":"Visitors often asked where the old castle entrance was. Yuna made a map for the information desk. She used big arrows and short sentences. The staff tested it with five visitors. Four found the entrance easily, but one went the wrong way. Yuna changed an arrow to make it clearer.","title":"A helpful sign","evidence":"Yuna made a map for the information desk."},{"id":"4-08-19","n":19,"kind":"reading","q":"最初の案内で入口を簡単に見つけた人数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"4","accepted":["4"],"why":"本文の根拠：Four found the entrance easily, but one went the wrong way.","context":"Visitors often asked where the old castle entrance was. Yuna made a map for the information desk. She used big arrows and short sentences. The staff tested it with five visitors. Four found the entrance easily, but one went the wrong way. Yuna changed an arrow to make it clearer.","title":"A helpful sign","evidence":"Four found the entrance easily, but one went the wrong way."},{"id":"4-08-20","n":20,"kind":"reading","q":"Yunaが修正したものを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"arrow","accepted":["arrow"],"why":"本文の根拠：Yuna changed an arrow to make it clearer.","context":"Visitors often asked where the old castle entrance was. Yuna made a map for the information desk. She used big arrows and short sentences. The staff tested it with five visitors. Four found the entrance easily, but one went the wrong way. Yuna changed an arrow to make it clearer.","title":"A helpful sign","evidence":"Yuna changed an arrow to make it clearer."}]},{"n":9,"questions":[{"id":"4-09-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"The team ( won / win / winning ) the game by one point yesterday.","answer":"won","accepted":["won"],"why":"winの過去形はwonです。"},{"id":"4-09-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"We ( were / was / did ) very tired after the long walk.","answer":"were","accepted":["were"],"why":"過去の状態と主語Weに合わせwereです。"},{"id":"4-09-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"This path is ( narrower / narrow / narrowest ) than the main road.","answer":"narrower","accepted":["narrower"],"why":"二つを比べる比較級narrowerです。"},{"id":"4-09-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"Mika is the ( best / better / good ) tennis player in our class.","answer":"best","accepted":["best"],"why":"クラスで最も上手という最上級。goodの最上級はbestです。"},{"id":"4-09-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"The bus will ( arrive / arrives / arrived ) in ten minutes.","answer":"arrive","accepted":["arrive"],"why":"助動詞willの後は原形です。"},{"id":"4-09-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"I have many things ( to do / doing / done ) this weekend.","answer":"to do","accepted":["to do"],"why":"「するべきこと」を名詞thingsの後のto doで説明します。"},{"id":"4-09-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"He is interested in ( collecting / collect / collected ) old coins.","answer":"collecting","accepted":["collecting"],"why":"前置詞inの後にはing形です。"},{"id":"4-09-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"There are ( fewer / less / little ) cars on this road than yesterday.","answer":"fewer","accepted":["fewer"],"why":"数えられる複数名詞carsの比較はfewerです。"},{"id":"4-09-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"I'll call you ( as soon as / during / because of ) I get home.","answer":"as soon as","accepted":["as soon as"],"why":"「帰宅するとすぐに」はas soon asと節で表します。"},{"id":"4-09-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: How ( tall / high / long ) is your brother? B: About 170 centimeters.","answer":"tall","accepted":["tall"],"why":"人の身長をたずねるにはHow tallです。"},{"id":"4-09-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"あなたは昨日、何時に家を出ましたか。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( leave / did / you / home / What / time / yesterday )","answer":"What time did you leave home yesterday?","accepted":["What time did you leave home yesterday?"],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-09-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"その店は町で一番混んでいます。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( busiest / in / shop / the / town / is / That )","answer":"That shop is the busiest in town.","accepted":["That shop is the busiest in town."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-09-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私は来月、自転車を買う予定です。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( to / I / bicycle / going / next / a / buy / am / month )","answer":"I am going to buy a bicycle next month.","accepted":["I am going to buy a bicycle next month."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-09-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"夕食後に散歩しませんか。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( walk / about / dinner / after / taking / How / a )","answer":"How about taking a walk after dinner?","accepted":["How about taking a walk after dinner?"],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-09-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"集合時刻を数字で書きなさい（時:分）。","answer":"8:30","accepted":["8:30"],"why":"本文の根拠：We will meet at the bus stop at eight thirty, not at the beach car park.","context":"Our beach clean-up is this Sunday. We will meet at the bus stop at eight thirty, not at the beach car park. Bring gloves and drinking water. Bags for rubbish will be provided. We will work for one hour and then count the bags. Children must come with an adult.","title":"A beach clean-up","evidence":"We will meet at the bus stop at eight thirty, not at the beach car park."},{"id":"4-09-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"用意してもらえる物を本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"bags","accepted":["bags"],"why":"本文の根拠：Bags for rubbish will be provided.","context":"Our beach clean-up is this Sunday. We will meet at the bus stop at eight thirty, not at the beach car park. Bring gloves and drinking water. Bags for rubbish will be provided. We will work for one hour and then count the bags. Children must come with an adult.","title":"A beach clean-up","evidence":"Bags for rubbish will be provided."},{"id":"4-09-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"清掃に取り組む時間を数字で答えなさい（時間）。","answer":"1","accepted":["1"],"why":"本文の根拠：We will work for one hour and then count the bags.","context":"Our beach clean-up is this Sunday. We will meet at the bus stop at eight thirty, not at the beach car park. Bring gloves and drinking water. Bags for rubbish will be provided. We will work for one hour and then count the bags. Children must come with an adult.","title":"A beach clean-up","evidence":"We will work for one hour and then count the bags."},{"id":"4-09-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"叔父からもらった物を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"kite","accepted":["kite"],"why":"本文の根拠：One day, his uncle gave him a small kite.","context":"Noah usually played video games after school. One day, his uncle gave him a small kite. Noah took it to a field, but there was not enough wind. He tried again on Saturday, and the kite flew high. He now checks the weather before going out and wants to build his own kite.","title":"A surprising hobby","evidence":"One day, his uncle gave him a small kite."},{"id":"4-09-19","n":19,"kind":"reading","q":"最初に足りなかったものを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"wind","accepted":["wind"],"why":"本文の根拠：Noah took it to a field, but there was not enough wind.","context":"Noah usually played video games after school. One day, his uncle gave him a small kite. Noah took it to a field, but there was not enough wind. He tried again on Saturday, and the kite flew high. He now checks the weather before going out and wants to build his own kite.","title":"A surprising hobby","evidence":"Noah took it to a field, but there was not enough wind."},{"id":"4-09-20","n":20,"kind":"reading","q":"うまく飛んだ曜日を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"Saturday","accepted":["Saturday"],"why":"本文の根拠：He tried again on Saturday, and the kite flew high.","context":"Noah usually played video games after school. One day, his uncle gave him a small kite. Noah took it to a field, but there was not enough wind. He tried again on Saturday, and the kite flew high. He now checks the weather before going out and wants to build his own kite.","title":"A surprising hobby","evidence":"He tried again on Saturday, and the kite flew high."}]},{"n":10,"questions":[{"id":"4-10-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"She ( took / take / taken ) the wrong bus this morning.","answer":"took","accepted":["took"],"why":"takeの過去形はtookです。"},{"id":"4-10-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Where ( did / was / does ) you buy this cap? B: At the station.","answer":"did","accepted":["did"],"why":"過去の一般動詞buyを用いた疑問文はdidです。"},{"id":"4-10-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"Your answer is ( better / good / best ) than mine.","answer":"better","accepted":["better"],"why":"goodの比較級はbetterです。"},{"id":"4-10-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"This is the ( worst / worse / bad ) weather we have had this week.","answer":"worst","accepted":["worst"],"why":"今週の中で最も悪いという最上級。badはworstになります。"},{"id":"4-10-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"We are going to ( have / has / had ) a barbecue on Sunday.","answer":"have","accepted":["have"],"why":"be going toの後は原形です。"},{"id":"4-10-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"I was happy ( to hear / heard / hearing ) the good news.","answer":"to hear","accepted":["to hear"],"why":"感情の理由を表すtoと動詞の原形です。"},{"id":"4-10-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"Before ( leaving / leave / left ) the house, I checked the windows.","answer":"leaving","accepted":["leaving"],"why":"前置詞Beforeの後で動作を表すにはing形です。"},{"id":"4-10-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"Can you give me a ( little / few / many ) advice?","answer":"little","accepted":["little"],"why":"adviceは数えない名詞なのでa littleです。"},{"id":"4-10-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"We need to hurry ( because / during / despite ) the train leaves soon.","answer":"because","accepted":["because"],"why":"急ぐ理由を節で表すのでbecauseです。"},{"id":"4-10-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"The hospital is ( across from / during / because of ) the bank.","answer":"across from","accepted":["across from"],"why":"銀行の向かいという位置を表すacross fromです。"},{"id":"4-10-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私の叔母は先週、手紙を書きました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( letter / last / wrote / a / week / aunt / My )","answer":"My aunt wrote a letter last week.","accepted":["My aunt wrote a letter last week."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-10-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"あなたの家は私の家より駅に近いです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( station / house / is / Your / to / the / mine / than / closer )","answer":"Your house is closer to the station than mine.","accepted":["Your house is closer to the station than mine."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 比較する相手はthanの後ろに置きます。"},{"id":"4-10-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私たちは食べ物を買うために店へ行きました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( went / We / to / shop / the / buy / food / to )","answer":"We went to the shop to buy food.","accepted":["We went to the shop to buy food."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-10-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"私は歴史について学ぶことに興味があります。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( about / interested / in / learning / history / am / I )","answer":"I am interested in learning about history.","accepted":["I am interested in learning about history."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"4-10-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"参加できる年齢の上限を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"15","accepted":["15"],"why":"本文の根拠：The town baking contest is open to students aged twelve to fifteen.","context":"The town baking contest is open to students aged twelve to fifteen. Bring your cake to the community hall by ten on Saturday. The judges will taste the cakes at eleven. Cakes must not contain nuts because some visitors have allergies. Each student can enter only one cake.","title":"A baking contest","evidence":"The town baking contest is open to students aged twelve to fifteen."},{"id":"4-10-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"ケーキの持ち込み締切の時刻を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"10","accepted":["10"],"why":"本文の根拠：Bring your cake to the community hall by ten on Saturday.","context":"The town baking contest is open to students aged twelve to fifteen. Bring your cake to the community hall by ten on Saturday. The judges will taste the cakes at eleven. Cakes must not contain nuts because some visitors have allergies. Each student can enter only one cake.","title":"A baking contest","evidence":"Bring your cake to the community hall by ten on Saturday."},{"id":"4-10-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"ケーキに入れてはいけない食材を本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"nuts","accepted":["nuts"],"why":"本文の根拠：Cakes must not contain nuts because some visitors have allergies.","context":"The town baking contest is open to students aged twelve to fifteen. Bring your cake to the community hall by ten on Saturday. The judges will taste the cakes at eleven. Cakes must not contain nuts because some visitors have allergies. Each student can enter only one cake.","title":"A baking contest","evidence":"Cakes must not contain nuts because some visitors have allergies."},{"id":"4-10-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"Rinが使った地図の素材を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"paper","accepted":["paper"],"why":"本文の根拠：Her phone battery was low, so she used a paper map.","context":"Rin wanted to walk to a new library. Her phone battery was low, so she used a paper map. She followed the river and crossed the second bridge. The library was between a cafe and a flower shop. Rin arrived in twenty minutes and borrowed a book about drawing.","title":"Learning from a map","evidence":"Her phone battery was low, so she used a paper map."},{"id":"4-10-19","n":19,"kind":"reading","q":"渡った橋は何番目ですか。数字で答えなさい。","answer":"2","accepted":["2"],"why":"本文の根拠：She followed the river and crossed the second bridge.","context":"Rin wanted to walk to a new library. Her phone battery was low, so she used a paper map. She followed the river and crossed the second bridge. The library was between a cafe and a flower shop. Rin arrived in twenty minutes and borrowed a book about drawing.","title":"Learning from a map","evidence":"She followed the river and crossed the second bridge."},{"id":"4-10-20","n":20,"kind":"reading","q":"借りた本のテーマを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"drawing","accepted":["drawing"],"why":"本文の根拠：Rin arrived in twenty minutes and borrowed a book about drawing.","context":"Rin wanted to walk to a new library. Her phone battery was low, so she used a paper map. She followed the river and crossed the second bridge. The library was between a cafe and a flower shop. Rin arrived in twenty minutes and borrowed a book about drawing.","title":"Learning from a map","evidence":"Rin arrived in twenty minutes and borrowed a book about drawing."}]}]},{"id":"3","label":"3級","sets":[{"n":1,"questions":[{"id":"3-01-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"I have ( lived / living / live ) in this town for three years.","answer":"lived","accepted":["lived"],"why":"haveと過去分詞、for three yearsで現在までの継続を表します。"},{"id":"3-01-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"The bridge was ( build / built / building ) fifty years ago.","answer":"built","accepted":["built"],"why":"受動態wasと過去分詞。buildの過去分詞はbuiltです。"},{"id":"3-01-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"This is the book ( who / which / where ) I borrowed yesterday.","answer":"which","accepted":["which"],"why":"先行詞bookは物。目的格の関係代名詞whichを使います。"},{"id":"3-01-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"It is important for us ( save / to save / saved ) water.","answer":"to save","accepted":["to save"],"why":"It is形容詞for人to動詞の形。to saveが内容を表します。"},{"id":"3-01-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"If it ( rains / rained / will rain ) tomorrow, we will stay inside.","answer":"rains","accepted":["rains"],"why":"未来のことでも条件を表すif節では現在形を使います。"},{"id":"3-01-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"I have never ( went / go / been ) to Canada.","answer":"been","accepted":["been"],"why":"have never been toで「一度も行ったことがない」という経験です。"},{"id":"3-01-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"Please speak more ( slow / slowly / slower ) so I can understand.","answer":"slowly","accepted":["slowly"],"why":"動詞speakを説明する副詞slowly。more slowlyで「もっとゆっくり」です。"},{"id":"3-01-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"My father asked me ( wash / washing / to wash ) the dishes.","answer":"to wash","accepted":["to wash"],"why":"ask人to動詞で、人に何かするよう頼むことを表します。"},{"id":"3-01-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"The boy ( sit / sitting / sits ) by the window is my cousin.","answer":"sitting","accepted":["sitting"],"why":"名詞boyのあとに現在分詞sittingを置いて、座っている少年を説明します。"},{"id":"3-01-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"You may bring your own lunch, but you ( mustn't / don't have to / couldn't ) because meals are provided.","answer":"don't have to","accepted":["don't have to"],"why":"食事が用意されるので持参する必要がない。禁止を表すmustn'tとは異なります。"},{"id":"3-01-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"「私はすでにその手紙を書きました。」( already / the letter / have / I / written )","answer":"I have already written the letter.","accepted":["I have already written the letter.","I have written the letter already."],"why":"haveと過去分詞writtenで完了。alreadyをhaveとwrittenの間に置きます。"},{"id":"3-01-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"「この部屋は毎日掃除されます。」( every day / cleaned / this room / is )","answer":"This room is cleaned every day.","accepted":["This room is cleaned every day."],"why":"is cleanedで現在の受動態を作ります。"},{"id":"3-01-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"「私はどこで切符を買うべきか分かりません。」( tickets / where / I / to buy / don't know )","answer":"I don't know where to buy tickets.","accepted":["I don't know where to buy tickets."],"why":"where to buyでどこで買うべきかという内容をまとめます。"},{"id":"3-01-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"「音楽を聴くことは私を幸せにします。」( makes / to music / me / listening / happy )","answer":"Listening to music makes me happy.","accepted":["Listening to music makes me happy."],"why":"動名詞のまとまりが主語。make人形容詞で「人をその状態にする」です。"},{"id":"3-01-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"最初の行事で修理できた傘の数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"18","accepted":["18"],"why":"repaired eighteen umbrellasが根拠です。fourは修理できなかった数です。","context":"At Elm School, students used to throw away broken umbrellas. Mina suggested a repair event. A local shop owner showed volunteers how to replace small parts. At the first event, they repaired eighteen umbrellas but could not fix four. Those four were sent to a recycling center. The next event will be in November. Students should book a place by email because only twelve volunteers can work safely in the room.","title":"Repair Saturday"},{"id":"3-01-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"予約に使う手段を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"email","accepted":["email"],"why":"book a place by emailが根拠。作業スペースの安全を保つため予約します。","context":"At Elm School, students used to throw away broken umbrellas. Mina suggested a repair event. A local shop owner showed volunteers how to replace small parts. At the first event, they repaired eighteen umbrellas but could not fix four. Those four were sent to a recycling center. The next event will be in November. Students should book a place by email because only twelve volunteers can work safely in the room.","title":"Repair Saturday"},{"id":"3-01-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"最初にLeoへ提案した人を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"teacher","accepted":["teacher"],"why":"His teacher suggested a short nature guideが根拠です。","context":"Leo did not enjoy reading long books. His teacher suggested a short nature guide. Leo took it to a riverside park and looked for birds shown in the pictures. He became interested in learning more and borrowed a longer book about birds. He now visits the park twice a month. On rainy days, he reads at home instead. He says the first guide helped him connect reading with something he could actually see.","title":"Reading outside"},{"id":"3-01-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"毎月、公園へ行く回数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"2","accepted":["2"],"why":"twice a monthは月に2回です。雨の日は家で読書します。","context":"Leo did not enjoy reading long books. His teacher suggested a short nature guide. Leo took it to a riverside park and looked for birds shown in the pictures. He became interested in learning more and borrowed a longer book about birds. He now visits the park twice a month. On rainy days, he reads at home instead. He says the first guide helped him connect reading with something he could actually see.","title":"Reading outside"},{"id":"3-01-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"友達へのメールです。英語30語程度で返事を書き、二つの質問両方に答えなさい。Hi! I want to learn a new sport. What sport do you recommend? Why do you recommend it?","answer":"I recommend badminton. You can play it indoors, so rain is not a problem. It is also easy to start with friends. I think you will enjoy playing it.","accepted":["I recommend badminton. You can play it indoors, so rain is not a problem. It is also easy to start with friends. I think you will enjoy playing it."],"why":"模範例は一例です。競技名と薦める理由の両方が必要。理由が競技の特徴とつながっているか、主語と動詞があるかを確認します。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"3-01-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Do you think students should help clean their local parks? 英語40語程度で自分の考えと理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"Yes, I do. First, clean parks are safer for children because there is less trash on the ground. Second, students can learn to take care of their town. Working together can also help them make new friends.","accepted":["Yes, I do. First, clean parks are safer for children because there is less trash on the ground. Second, students can learn to take care of their town. Working together can also help them make new friends."],"why":"YesでもNoでもよい。立場、異なる理由二つ、理由とのつながりを評価します。模範例と同じ文章である必要はありません。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":2,"questions":[{"id":"3-02-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"I have ( known / know / knew ) my best friend since we were six.","answer":"known","accepted":["known"],"why":"haveと過去分詞で継続を表します。knowの過去分詞はknownです。"},{"id":"3-02-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"This song is ( sung / sang / singing ) by many children.","answer":"sung","accepted":["sung"],"why":"受動態isと過去分詞。singの過去分詞はsungです。"},{"id":"3-02-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"The man ( who / which / where ) lives next door is a pilot.","answer":"who","accepted":["who"],"why":"人を先行詞として主語の役割を持つ関係代名詞whoです。"},{"id":"3-02-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"If you ( practice / practiced / will practice ) every day, you will improve.","answer":"practice","accepted":["practice"],"why":"未来の条件を表すif節は現在形です。"},{"id":"3-02-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"I don't know ( how / what / who ) to use this machine.","answer":"how","accepted":["how"],"why":"使い方を表すhow to useです。"},{"id":"3-02-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"The box is too heavy for me ( to carry / carrying / carried ).","answer":"to carry","accepted":["to carry"],"why":"too形容詞for人to動詞で、その動作ができないほどという意味です。"},{"id":"3-02-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"She told me ( to wait / waiting / waited ) outside the office.","answer":"to wait","accepted":["to wait"],"why":"tell人to動詞で人に何かするよう伝えます。"},{"id":"3-02-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"Please drive ( carefully / careful / care ) on this narrow road.","answer":"carefully","accepted":["carefully"],"why":"動詞driveを説明する副詞carefullyです。"},{"id":"3-02-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"I haven't finished my report ( yet / already / ever ).","answer":"yet","accepted":["yet"],"why":"否定文で「まだ」の意味はyetです。"},{"id":"3-02-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"You ( mustn't / don't have to / needn't ) touch these wires; it is dangerous.","answer":"mustn't","accepted":["mustn't"],"why":"危険なので触れてはいけないという禁止はmustn'tです。"},{"id":"3-02-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私は三年間、このクラブの一員です。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( have / this / years / a / three / I / of / member / been / for / club )","answer":"I have been a member of this club for three years.","accepted":["I have been a member of this club for three years."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 現在完了はhave/hasと過去分詞を組み合わせます。期間はfor、開始時点はsince、経験や完了は文中の時を表す語句で確認します。"},{"id":"3-02-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"この橋は去年、建てられました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( This / was / last / built / year / bridge )","answer":"This bridge was built last year.","accepted":["This bridge was built last year."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-02-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私は何を持っていくべきか分かりません。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( to / I / what / not / do / bring / know )","answer":"I do not know what to bring.","accepted":["I do not know what to bring."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-02-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"私はあなたにここで待ってほしいです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( wait / here / to / want / I / you )","answer":"I want you to wait here.","accepted":["I want you to wait here."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-02-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"雨のため、最初の交換会はどこで開かれましたか。英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"library","accepted":["library"],"why":"本文の根拠：The first event was held in the library because rain made the playground unsuitable.","context":"Students at Oak School used to buy new uniforms each year. This spring, the student council organized a uniform exchange. Families brought clean uniforms that were too small for their children. Volunteers sorted them by size rather than by school year. The first event was held in the library because rain made the playground unsuitable. Forty uniforms found new owners. The council plans another exchange before the next school term and will ask families to wash items before bringing them.","title":"A school exchange","evidence":"The first event was held in the library because rain made the playground unsuitable."},{"id":"3-02-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"制服は何を基準に整理されましたか。英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"size","accepted":["size"],"why":"本文の根拠：Volunteers sorted them by size rather than by school year.","context":"Students at Oak School used to buy new uniforms each year. This spring, the student council organized a uniform exchange. Families brought clean uniforms that were too small for their children. Volunteers sorted them by size rather than by school year. The first event was held in the library because rain made the playground unsuitable. Forty uniforms found new owners. The council plans another exchange before the next school term and will ask families to wash items before bringing them.","title":"A school exchange","evidence":"Volunteers sorted them by size rather than by school year."},{"id":"3-02-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"最初の原稿で繰り返していたものを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"information","accepted":["information"],"why":"本文の根拠：Nao noticed that some sentences repeated the same information.","context":"Nao joined a school radio group because she wanted to talk about music. At first, she wrote long introductions and often ran out of time. A teacher suggested recording a practice program and listening to it. Nao noticed that some sentences repeated the same information. She shortened them, leaving more time for songs. Her next program lasted exactly fifteen minutes. She now asks another student to read her script before recording, but chooses the music herself.","title":"Making a radio program","evidence":"Nao noticed that some sentences repeated the same information."},{"id":"3-02-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"改善後の番組の長さを数字で答えなさい（分）。","answer":"15","accepted":["15"],"why":"本文の根拠：Her next program lasted exactly fifteen minutes.","context":"Nao joined a school radio group because she wanted to talk about music. At first, she wrote long introductions and often ran out of time. A teacher suggested recording a practice program and listening to it. Nao noticed that some sentences repeated the same information. She shortened them, leaving more time for songs. Her next program lasted exactly fifteen minutes. She now asks another student to read her script before recording, but chooses the music herself.","title":"Making a radio program","evidence":"Her next program lasted exactly fifteen minutes."},{"id":"3-02-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語30語程度で返信し、二つの質問に答えなさい。Hi! I want to read an English book. What kind of book do you recommend? When is a good time to read it?","answer":"I recommend a short mystery because it can keep you interested. You can read it before dinner, when you are not too tired. Start with just a few pages each day.","accepted":[],"why":"本の種類と読む時の両方を答える。薦める理由は補足として有効です。時刻は例と違ってもかまいません。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"3-02-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Do you think students should learn to cook? 英語40語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"Yes, I do. First, students can make healthy meals when their parents are busy. Second, cooking teaches them to plan and use ingredients carefully. These skills can help them live independently in the future.","accepted":[],"why":"健康的な食事と計画性という別の理由を挙げています。反対の意見でも理由二つがあれば認めます。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":3,"questions":[{"id":"3-03-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"My parents have ( been / went / going ) to Australia twice.","answer":"been","accepted":["been"],"why":"have been toと回数で訪問の経験を表します。"},{"id":"3-03-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"These chairs were ( made / make / making ) in a local workshop.","answer":"made","accepted":["made"],"why":"受動態wereと過去分詞madeです。"},{"id":"3-03-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"I found the wallet ( which / who / where ) I lost last week.","answer":"which","accepted":["which"],"why":"先行詞walletは物で、lostの目的語になるwhichです。"},{"id":"3-03-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"I'll send you a message when I ( arrive / arrived / will arrive ).","answer":"arrive","accepted":["arrive"],"why":"未来の時を表すwhen節では現在形です。"},{"id":"3-03-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"It was difficult for me ( to choose / choosing / chose ) a gift.","answer":"to choose","accepted":["to choose"],"why":"It was形容詞for人to動詞の形です。"},{"id":"3-03-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"This bag is light enough ( to carry / carrying / carried ) with one hand.","answer":"to carry","accepted":["to carry"],"why":"形容詞enough to動詞で、動作ができる程度を表します。"},{"id":"3-03-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"The teacher asked us ( to read / reading / reads ) the next page.","answer":"to read","accepted":["to read"],"why":"ask人to動詞で、人に何かするよう頼みます。"},{"id":"3-03-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"My sister sings ( beautifully / beautiful / beauty ).","answer":"beautifully","accepted":["beautifully"],"why":"動詞singsを修飾する副詞beautifullyです。"},{"id":"3-03-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"I have ( already / yet / never ) finished, so I can help you now.","answer":"already","accepted":["already"],"why":"すでに終わったから手伝えるという完了のalreadyです。"},{"id":"3-03-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Must I come tomorrow? B: No, you ( don't have to / mustn't / can't ).","answer":"don't have to","accepted":["don't have to"],"why":"必要がないという意味でdon't have toです。禁止とは異なります。"},{"id":"3-03-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"あなたは今までに外国を訪れたことがありますか。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( country / foreign / you / Have / visited / a / ever )","answer":"Have you ever visited a foreign country?","accepted":["Have you ever visited a foreign country?"],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-03-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"これらの机は毎朝、きれいにされます。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( every / are / morning / These / cleaned / desks )","answer":"These desks are cleaned every morning.","accepted":["These desks are cleaned every morning."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-03-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私は自転車の修理の仕方を知っています。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( how / I / know / repair / bicycle / a / to )","answer":"I know how to repair a bicycle.","accepted":["I know how to repair a bicycle."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-03-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"その医者は私にもっと眠るよう言いました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( The / doctor / told / more / to / me / sleep )","answer":"The doctor told me to sleep more.","accepted":["The doctor told me to sleep more."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 人に動作を求める部分は人とto不定詞のまとまりにします。"},{"id":"3-03-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"安全のために一回の教室へ入れる人数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"12","accepted":["12"],"why":"本文の根拠：Twenty students applied, but the room could safely hold only twelve people.","context":"The bicycle club wanted to help students repair flat tires. They invited a local mechanic to teach a short lesson. Twenty students applied, but the room could safely hold only twelve people. The club decided to hold the same lesson twice, instead of asking students to watch from the corridor. Tools were provided, and students brought their own bicycles. After the lesson, a printed guide was given to everyone so they could review the steps at home.","title":"A repair lesson","evidence":"Twenty students applied, but the room could safely hold only twelve people."},{"id":"3-03-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"家で復習できるように配られたものを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"guide","accepted":["guide"],"why":"本文の根拠：After the lesson, a printed guide was given to everyone so they could review the steps at home.","context":"The bicycle club wanted to help students repair flat tires. They invited a local mechanic to teach a short lesson. Twenty students applied, but the room could safely hold only twelve people. The club decided to hold the same lesson twice, instead of asking students to watch from the corridor. Tools were provided, and students brought their own bicycles. After the lesson, a printed guide was given to everyone so they could review the steps at home.","title":"A repair lesson","evidence":"After the lesson, a printed guide was given to everyone so they could review the steps at home."},{"id":"3-03-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"Evaが写真の中で見覚えのあった建物を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"church","accepted":["church"],"why":"本文の根拠：Eva recognized the church, but not the small shops that had disappeared.","context":"Eva thought the town museum was only for tourists. One rainy afternoon, she went there with her grandmother. A volunteer showed them old photographs of their street. Eva recognized the church, but not the small shops that had disappeared. Her grandmother told her how people used to buy food there. Eva began collecting stories from older neighbors. She now wants to make a map showing the former shops, using the photographs and the stories together.","title":"A quiet discovery","evidence":"Eva recognized the church, but not the small shops that had disappeared."},{"id":"3-03-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"地図で示したいものを本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"shops","accepted":["shops"],"why":"本文の根拠：She now wants to make a map showing the former shops, using the photographs and the stories together.","context":"Eva thought the town museum was only for tourists. One rainy afternoon, she went there with her grandmother. A volunteer showed them old photographs of their street. Eva recognized the church, but not the small shops that had disappeared. Her grandmother told her how people used to buy food there. Eva began collecting stories from older neighbors. She now wants to make a map showing the former shops, using the photographs and the stories together.","title":"A quiet discovery","evidence":"She now wants to make a map showing the former shops, using the photographs and the stories together."},{"id":"3-03-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語30語程度で返信し、二つの質問に答えなさい。Hi! I am visiting your town. Which place should I visit? How can I get there from the station?","answer":"You should visit the small museum near the river. It has interesting old photographs. You can walk there from the station in about fifteen minutes. Follow the main street and turn right.","accepted":[],"why":"訪れる場所と駅からの行き方を答える。架空の場所を設定してよく、方角や交通手段が分かる説明にします。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"3-03-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Is studying with friends better than studying alone? 英語40語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I think studying alone is better. First, I can work at my own speed without waiting for others. Second, it is easier for me to concentrate in a quiet room. I can ask friends questions later.","accepted":[],"why":"自分の速さと集中しやすさを別の理由にしています。友達と勉強する立場でもよいです。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":4,"questions":[{"id":"3-04-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"We have ( used / use / using ) this computer for five years.","answer":"used","accepted":["used"],"why":"haveと過去分詞usedで継続を表します。"},{"id":"3-04-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"French is ( spoken / spoke / speaking ) in some parts of Canada.","answer":"spoken","accepted":["spoken"],"why":"受動態isとspeakの過去分詞spokenです。"},{"id":"3-04-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"The woman ( who / which / where ) helped me was very kind.","answer":"who","accepted":["who"],"why":"先行詞womanは人。helpedの主語になるwhoです。"},{"id":"3-04-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"I will bring a jacket if it ( gets / got / will get ) cold.","answer":"gets","accepted":["gets"],"why":"未来の条件でもif節では現在形getsです。"},{"id":"3-04-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"Could you tell me where the station ( is / does / be )?","answer":"is","accepted":["is"],"why":"間接疑問はwhereと主語と動詞の順。be動詞isを使います。"},{"id":"3-04-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"I'm too busy ( to watch / watching / watched ) the film tonight.","answer":"to watch","accepted":["to watch"],"why":"too busy to動詞で、忙しすぎてできないことを表します。"},{"id":"3-04-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"My mother wants me ( to clean / cleaning / cleaned ) my room.","answer":"to clean","accepted":["to clean"],"why":"want人to動詞で、人にしてほしいことを表します。"},{"id":"3-04-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"He answered the question ( correctly / correct / correction ).","answer":"correctly","accepted":["correctly"],"why":"動詞answeredを修飾する副詞correctlyです。"},{"id":"3-04-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"Have you ( ever / yet / already ) climbed this mountain before?","answer":"ever","accepted":["ever"],"why":"経験を尋ねる疑問文の「今までに」はeverです。"},{"id":"3-04-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"We ( should / mustn't / can't ) wear helmets to stay safe when cycling.","answer":"should","accepted":["should"],"why":"安全のための助言なのでshouldです。禁止や不可能ではありません。"},{"id":"3-04-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私たちはまだ、そのニュースを聞いていません。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( yet / heard / the / have / news / We / not )","answer":"We have not heard the news yet.","accepted":["We have not heard the news yet."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 現在完了はhave/hasと過去分詞を組み合わせます。期間はfor、開始時点はsince、経験や完了は文中の時を表す語句で確認します。"},{"id":"3-04-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"その男の子が描いた絵はきれいです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( which / is / boy / the / drew / picture / beautiful / The )","answer":"The picture which the boy drew is beautiful.","accepted":["The picture which the boy drew is beautiful."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-04-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"そのバッグは私が運べるほど軽いです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( enough / bag / light / carry / me / for / to / is / The )","answer":"The bag is light enough for me to carry.","accepted":["The bag is light enough for me to carry."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-04-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"川で泳ぐことは危険です。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( the / in / is / Swimming / river / dangerous )","answer":"Swimming in the river is dangerous.","accepted":["Swimming in the river is dangerous."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-04-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"最初に職員が問題だと考えていた家具を本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"chairs","accepted":["chairs"],"why":"本文の根拠：Staff first thought the chairs were uncomfortable.","context":"The library wanted more teenagers to use its study room. Staff first thought the chairs were uncomfortable. They asked students to fill in a short survey. Most students said the chairs were fine, but the room closed before their after-school clubs ended. The library kept the same furniture and extended the opening time by one hour on weekdays. A month later, more students were using the room. Staff plan to ask users again before making further changes.","title":"A useful survey","evidence":"Staff first thought the chairs were uncomfortable."},{"id":"3-04-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"平日の開館時間を何時間延ばしましたか。数字で答えなさい。","answer":"1","accepted":["1"],"why":"本文の根拠：The library kept the same furniture and extended the opening time by one hour on weekdays.","context":"The library wanted more teenagers to use its study room. Staff first thought the chairs were uncomfortable. They asked students to fill in a short survey. Most students said the chairs were fine, but the room closed before their after-school clubs ended. The library kept the same furniture and extended the opening time by one hour on weekdays. A month later, more students were using the room. Staff plan to ask users again before making further changes.","title":"A useful survey","evidence":"The library kept the same furniture and extended the opening time by one hour on weekdays."},{"id":"3-04-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"弟が理解したとき、Hiroが使ったものを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"picture","accepted":["picture"],"why":"本文の根拠：One day, he drew a simple picture to explain why a shadow changed during the day.","context":"Hiro enjoyed science, but his younger brother often found his explanations difficult. Hiro used words from his school textbook and spoke quickly. One day, he drew a simple picture to explain why a shadow changed during the day. His brother understood and asked another question. Hiro realized that being correct was not enough; he also needed to choose words his listener knew. He now begins with an example before explaining a scientific idea.","title":"Learning to explain","evidence":"One day, he drew a simple picture to explain why a shadow changed during the day."},{"id":"3-04-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"現在、説明の最初に使うものを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"example","accepted":["example"],"why":"本文の根拠：He now begins with an example before explaining a scientific idea.","context":"Hiro enjoyed science, but his younger brother often found his explanations difficult. Hiro used words from his school textbook and spoke quickly. One day, he drew a simple picture to explain why a shadow changed during the day. His brother understood and asked another question. Hiro realized that being correct was not enough; he also needed to choose words his listener knew. He now begins with an example before explaining a scientific idea.","title":"Learning to explain","evidence":"He now begins with an example before explaining a scientific idea."},{"id":"3-04-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語30語程度で返信し、二つの質問に答えなさい。Hi! I want to start exercising. What activity should I try? How often should I do it?","answer":"You should try walking because you do not need special equipment. You can start with a short walk three times a week. Choose a safe route and increase the distance slowly.","accepted":[],"why":"活動と頻度を答える。頻度をevery dayやtwice a weekなどで具体的にします。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"3-04-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Do you think schools should have more plants? 英語40語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"Yes, I do. First, plants make classrooms look friendly and pleasant. Second, caring for plants helps students learn responsibility. Students can take turns watering them, so the work does not become too difficult for one person.","accepted":[],"why":"見た目のよさと責任を学ぶことの二つ。単なる同じ理由の言い換えにしません。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":5,"questions":[{"id":"3-05-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"I have ( lost / lose / losing ) my key, so I can't open the door.","answer":"lost","accepted":["lost"],"why":"have lostで、紛失の結果が現在に及ぶことを表します。"},{"id":"3-05-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"The package was ( delivered / deliver / delivering ) this morning.","answer":"delivered","accepted":["delivered"],"why":"受動態wasと過去分詞deliveredです。"},{"id":"3-05-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"This is the camera ( which / who / where ) takes clear pictures.","answer":"which","accepted":["which"],"why":"先行詞cameraは物。takesの主語になるwhichです。"},{"id":"3-05-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"Let's wait here until the rain ( stops / stopped / will stop ).","answer":"stops","accepted":["stops"],"why":"未来の時を表すuntil節では現在形です。"},{"id":"3-05-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"I can't decide which shoes ( to buy / buying / bought ).","answer":"to buy","accepted":["to buy"],"why":"whichと名詞とto動詞で、どれを買うべきかを表します。"},{"id":"3-05-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"The ladder is long enough ( to reach / reaching / reached ) the roof.","answer":"to reach","accepted":["to reach"],"why":"enough to動詞で、その動作ができる程度を表します。"},{"id":"3-05-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"Please remind me ( to take / taking / took ) my medicine.","answer":"to take","accepted":["to take"],"why":"remind人to動詞で、忘れずにするよう注意する意味です。"},{"id":"3-05-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"She speaks English more ( fluently / fluent / fluency ) than I do.","answer":"fluently","accepted":["fluently"],"why":"動詞speaksを修飾する副詞。more fluentlyは副詞の比較級です。"},{"id":"3-05-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Has he left yet? B: Yes, he ( has / did / is ).","answer":"has","accepted":["has"],"why":"Hasで始まる現在完了の質問にはhasで答えます。"},{"id":"3-05-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"We ( have to / mustn't / can't ) show our tickets before entering; it is required.","answer":"have to","accepted":["have to"],"why":"規則で必要とされることはhave toです。"},{"id":"3-05-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私はすでに鍵を見つけました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( key / the / I / already / found / have )","answer":"I have already found the key.","accepted":["I have already found the key."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 現在完了はhave/hasと過去分詞を組み合わせます。期間はfor、開始時点はsince、経験や完了は文中の時を表す語句で確認します。"},{"id":"3-05-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"この歌は世界中で歌われています。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( sung / the / world / This / around / song / is )","answer":"This song is sung around the world.","accepted":["This song is sung around the world."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-05-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私はいつ出発すべきか決められません。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( cannot / decide / to / I / leave / when )","answer":"I cannot decide when to leave.","accepted":["I cannot decide when to leave."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-05-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"私の母は私に毎日読むよう勧めました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( day / advised / every / mother / read / My / me / to )","answer":"My mother advised me to read every day.","accepted":["My mother advised me to read every day."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 人に動作を求める部分は人とto不定詞のまとまりにします。"},{"id":"3-05-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"最初のメニューに載っていた情報を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"price","accepted":["price"],"why":"本文の根拠：Staff discovered that the menu listed only the price, not the ingredients.","context":"Students asked the school cafe to sell more healthy lunches. The cafe introduced vegetable wraps, but few students bought them during the first week. Staff discovered that the menu listed only the price, not the ingredients. They added pictures and ingredient lists. Students could see that the wraps contained familiar foods such as cheese and carrots. Sales increased without changing the recipe or the price. The cafe will use the same approach for its next new dish.","title":"A new lunch choice","evidence":"Staff discovered that the menu listed only the price, not the ingredients."},{"id":"3-05-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"紹介後も変更しなかった料理の作り方を示す英語1語を本文から書きなさい。","answer":"recipe","accepted":["recipe"],"why":"本文の根拠：Sales increased without changing the recipe or the price.","context":"Students asked the school cafe to sell more healthy lunches. The cafe introduced vegetable wraps, but few students bought them during the first week. Staff discovered that the menu listed only the price, not the ingredients. They added pictures and ingredient lists. Students could see that the wraps contained familiar foods such as cheese and carrots. Sales increased without changing the recipe or the price. The cafe will use the same approach for its next new dish.","title":"A new lunch choice","evidence":"Sales increased without changing the recipe or the price."},{"id":"3-05-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"父と作ったものを英語2語で答えなさい。","answer":"bird box","accepted":["bird box"],"why":"本文の根拠：His father invited him to help build a bird box.","context":"Kota decided to spend one weekend without online games. On Saturday morning, he felt bored and kept looking at his phone. His father invited him to help build a bird box. Measuring and cutting the wood took longer than Kota expected, but he enjoyed seeing it take shape. On Sunday, they put it in the garden. Kota still likes games, but he now plans one outdoor activity each weekend instead of staying inside all day.","title":"A weekend challenge","evidence":"His father invited him to help build a bird box."},{"id":"3-05-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"今後、一週間ごとに予定する活動の数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"1","accepted":["1"],"why":"本文の根拠：Kota still likes games, but he now plans one outdoor activity each weekend instead of staying inside all day.","context":"Kota decided to spend one weekend without online games. On Saturday morning, he felt bored and kept looking at his phone. His father invited him to help build a bird box. Measuring and cutting the wood took longer than Kota expected, but he enjoyed seeing it take shape. On Sunday, they put it in the garden. Kota still likes games, but he now plans one outdoor activity each weekend instead of staying inside all day.","title":"A weekend challenge","evidence":"Kota still likes games, but he now plans one outdoor activity each weekend instead of staying inside all day."},{"id":"3-05-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語30語程度で返信し、二つの質問に答えなさい。Hi! Our class will have a party. What food should we prepare? What activity would be fun?","answer":"You could prepare small sandwiches because they are easy to eat. A quiz about our class would be fun. Everyone could help write the questions, and we would not need expensive materials.","accepted":[],"why":"食べ物と活動の両方が必要です。食べ物だけ詳しく説明して活動を忘れないようにします。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"3-05-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Should students help at home every day? 英語40語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I think they should help when they can, but not necessarily every day. First, important homework sometimes takes a long time. Second, sharing larger jobs on weekends can be more useful than doing a small job each evening.","accepted":[],"why":"毎日という条件への意見を明確にし、宿題の時間と週末の分担を理由にしています。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":6,"questions":[{"id":"3-06-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"My cousin has ( visited / visit / visiting ) Kyoto three times.","answer":"visited","accepted":["visited"],"why":"haveと過去分詞visitedで経験を表します。"},{"id":"3-06-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"The windows are ( cleaned / clean / cleaning ) every Friday.","answer":"cleaned","accepted":["cleaned"],"why":"定期的に掃除されるので現在の受動態です。"},{"id":"3-06-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"Do you know the girl ( who / which / where ) is holding a violin?","answer":"who","accepted":["who"],"why":"先行詞girlは人。主格の関係代名詞whoです。"},{"id":"3-06-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"If the shop ( is / was / will be ) open tomorrow, I'll buy the notebook.","answer":"is","accepted":["is"],"why":"未来の条件を表すif節でも現在形isです。"},{"id":"3-06-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"I learned how ( to make / making / made ) a paper crane.","answer":"to make","accepted":["to make"],"why":"how to動詞で方法を表します。"},{"id":"3-06-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"The music was too loud for us ( to talk / talking / talked ) easily.","answer":"to talk","accepted":["to talk"],"why":"too形容詞for人to動詞で、容易に話せないほど大きい音です。"},{"id":"3-06-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"He invited me ( to join / joining / joined ) his team.","answer":"to join","accepted":["to join"],"why":"invite人to動詞で、人を何かに誘うことを表します。"},{"id":"3-06-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"The students listened ( quietly / quiet / silence ) to the story.","answer":"quietly","accepted":["quietly"],"why":"動詞listenedを修飾する副詞quietlyです。"},{"id":"3-06-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"She has ( just / yet / ever ) arrived, so her bag is still by the door.","answer":"just","accepted":["just"],"why":"到着したばかりであることはhas just arrivedです。"},{"id":"3-06-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"You ( mustn't / needn't / don't have to ) park here. The sign says parking is forbidden.","answer":"mustn't","accepted":["mustn't"],"why":"明確な禁止なのでmustn'tです。"},{"id":"3-06-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"彼は今までに一度も飛行機に乗ったことがありません。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( by / traveled / has / never / plane / He )","answer":"He has never traveled by plane.","accepted":["He has never traveled by plane."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 現在完了はhave/hasと過去分詞を組み合わせます。期間はfor、開始時点はsince、経験や完了は文中の時を表す語句で確認します。"},{"id":"3-06-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"私たちが昨日見た映画は面白かったです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( film / we / saw / yesterday / which / interesting / The / was )","answer":"The film which we saw yesterday was interesting.","accepted":["The film which we saw yesterday was interesting."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-06-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私が空港に着いたら、あなたに電話します。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( I / will / I / call / at / arrive / you / when / the / airport )","answer":"I will call you when I arrive at the airport.","accepted":["I will call you when I arrive at the airport."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-06-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"彼女は私にその窓を開けるよう頼みました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( the / asked / me / to / open / window / She )","answer":"She asked me to open the window.","accepted":["She asked me to open the window."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 人に動作を求める部分は人とto不定詞のまとまりにします。"},{"id":"3-06-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"色と日付を記録したものを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"notebook","accepted":["notebook"],"why":"本文の根拠：A student volunteer suggested attaching a numbered tag and writing the color and date in a notebook.","context":"The station used to keep all lost umbrellas in one large box. Finding a particular umbrella took a long time. A student volunteer suggested attaching a numbered tag and writing the color and date in a notebook. The staff tried this system for a month. They could answer questions more quickly, and fewer people had to wait. Owners still needed to describe their umbrellas before receiving them, so the numbers alone were not enough to claim an item.","title":"A lost umbrella system","evidence":"A student volunteer suggested attaching a numbered tag and writing the color and date in a notebook."},{"id":"3-06-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"新しい仕組みを試した期間を数字で答えなさい（か月）。","answer":"1","accepted":["1"],"why":"本文の根拠：The staff tried this system for a month.","context":"The station used to keep all lost umbrellas in one large box. Finding a particular umbrella took a long time. A student volunteer suggested attaching a numbered tag and writing the color and date in a notebook. The staff tried this system for a month. They could answer questions more quickly, and fewer people had to wait. Owners still needed to describe their umbrellas before receiving them, so the numbers alone were not enough to claim an item.","title":"A lost umbrella system","evidence":"The staff tried this system for a month."},{"id":"3-06-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"貸出用のカップを洗うボランティアの人数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"6","accepted":["6"],"why":"本文の根拠：The club expects cleaning to take longer, so six volunteers will help wash the cups after the concert.","context":"The music club sold drinks at its school concert last year. Afterward, many plastic cups were left on the ground. This year, visitors will borrow washable cups and return them to a collection table. A small deposit will be returned with each cup. The club expects cleaning to take longer, so six volunteers will help wash the cups after the concert. Visitors may also bring their own cups, but glass containers will not be allowed for safety reasons.","title":"A concert without waste","evidence":"The club expects cleaning to take longer, so six volunteers will help wash the cups after the concert."},{"id":"3-06-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"安全のために禁止する容器の素材を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"glass","accepted":["glass"],"why":"本文の根拠：Visitors may also bring their own cups, but glass containers will not be allowed for safety reasons.","context":"The music club sold drinks at its school concert last year. Afterward, many plastic cups were left on the ground. This year, visitors will borrow washable cups and return them to a collection table. A small deposit will be returned with each cup. The club expects cleaning to take longer, so six volunteers will help wash the cups after the concert. Visitors may also bring their own cups, but glass containers will not be allowed for safety reasons.","title":"A concert without waste","evidence":"Visitors may also bring their own cups, but glass containers will not be allowed for safety reasons."},{"id":"3-06-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語30語程度で返信し、二つの質問に答えなさい。Hi! I want to improve my English. What should I practice first? Where can I practice it?","answer":"You should practice short conversations first. Try speaking with a classmate after school or at an English club. Choose familiar topics, such as food and hobbies, so you can feel more confident.","accepted":[],"why":"練習内容と場所の両方を答える。場所は部活や家庭など具体的なものにします。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"3-06-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Do you think children should spend more time outdoors? 英語40語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"Yes, I do. First, outdoor activities help children move their bodies and stay healthy. Second, they can notice plants and animals that they would not see on a screen. Safe places and suitable weather are important, too.","accepted":[],"why":"健康と自然に気付くことが二つの理由。安全という補足も主張と矛盾しません。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":7,"questions":[{"id":"3-07-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"We haven't ( seen / saw / see ) our former teacher for a year.","answer":"seen","accepted":["seen"],"why":"have notと過去分詞。seeの過去分詞はseenです。"},{"id":"3-07-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"The new road will be ( opened / open / opening ) next month.","answer":"opened","accepted":["opened"],"why":"will beと過去分詞で未来の受動態です。"},{"id":"3-07-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"I like stories ( which / who / where ) have surprising endings.","answer":"which","accepted":["which"],"why":"先行詞storiesは物。haveの主語になるwhichです。"},{"id":"3-07-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"I will wash the dishes after I ( finish / finished / will finish ) dinner.","answer":"finish","accepted":["finish"],"why":"未来の時を表すafter節は現在形です。"},{"id":"3-07-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"It is necessary ( to check / checking / checked ) the address before mailing it.","answer":"to check","accepted":["to check"],"why":"It is形容詞to動詞で必要なことを述べます。"},{"id":"3-07-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"He is old enough ( to travel / traveling / traveled ) alone.","answer":"to travel","accepted":["to travel"],"why":"形容詞enough to動詞で、一人で旅行できる年齢を表します。"},{"id":"3-07-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"My doctor advised me ( to rest / resting / rested ) for a few days.","answer":"to rest","accepted":["to rest"],"why":"advise人to動詞で、人に何かするよう助言します。"},{"id":"3-07-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"The children played ( happily / happy / happiness ) in the garden.","answer":"happily","accepted":["happily"],"why":"動詞playedを説明する副詞happilyです。"},{"id":"3-07-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Have you read the article? B: No, I ( haven't / didn't / wasn't ).","answer":"haven't","accepted":["haven't"],"why":"Haveで聞く現在完了の否定の返事はhaven'tです。"},{"id":"3-07-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"We ( should / mustn't / can't ) check the weather before hiking; it is a good idea.","answer":"should","accepted":["should"],"why":"よい行動として薦める場合はshouldです。"},{"id":"3-07-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私は先月から英語を勉強しています。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( last / English / since / I / month / studied / have )","answer":"I have studied English since last month.","accepted":["I have studied English since last month."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 現在完了はhave/hasと過去分詞を組み合わせます。期間はfor、開始時点はsince、経験や完了は文中の時を表す語句で確認します。"},{"id":"3-07-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"この町では多くの花が育てられています。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( in / this / grown / are / flowers / Many / town )","answer":"Many flowers are grown in this town.","accepted":["Many flowers are grown in this town."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-07-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"この道は歩くには狭すぎます。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( to / road / walk / This / narrow / too / along / is )","answer":"This road is too narrow to walk along.","accepted":["This road is too narrow to walk along."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-07-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"健康でいることは私たちにとって重要です。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( for / is / stay / to / important / It / us / healthy )","answer":"It is important for us to stay healthy.","accepted":["It is important for us to stay healthy."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-07-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"Mayaが見落としたものをLuisが見つけました。それを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"clue","accepted":["clue"],"why":"本文の根拠：Luis noticed a clue that Maya had missed.","context":"Maya liked reading stories alone, while her friend Luis preferred talking about films. Their teacher asked them to read the same short story and discuss its ending. Luis noticed a clue that Maya had missed. Maya explained why one character had changed his mind. Both enjoyed the conversation more than they expected. They decided to choose one book each month. They will take turns choosing, so both can introduce something new to the other.","title":"A reading partner","evidence":"Luis noticed a clue that Maya had missed."},{"id":"3-07-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"一か月に選ぶ本の数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"1","accepted":["1"],"why":"本文の根拠：They decided to choose one book each month.","context":"Maya liked reading stories alone, while her friend Luis preferred talking about films. Their teacher asked them to read the same short story and discuss its ending. Luis noticed a clue that Maya had missed. Maya explained why one character had changed his mind. Both enjoyed the conversation more than they expected. They decided to choose one book each month. They will take turns choosing, so both can introduce something new to the other.","title":"A reading partner","evidence":"They decided to choose one book each month."},{"id":"3-07-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"特に危険だった時間帯の長さを数字で答えなさい（分）。","answer":"15","accepted":["15"],"why":"本文の根拠：They found that the most dangerous period was the fifteen minutes before school started.","context":"Parents worried about students walking past a busy car park. Some wanted the school to stop students using the nearby gate. A class investigated the route and counted cars at different times. They found that the most dangerous period was the fifteen minutes before school started. The school arranged for two adults to guide students during that period. The gate remained open, and students could still use the shortest route without crossing the car park alone.","title":"A safer walk","evidence":"They found that the most dangerous period was the fifteen minutes before school started."},{"id":"3-07-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"その時間に生徒を案内する大人の人数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"2","accepted":["2"],"why":"本文の根拠：The school arranged for two adults to guide students during that period.","context":"Parents worried about students walking past a busy car park. Some wanted the school to stop students using the nearby gate. A class investigated the route and counted cars at different times. They found that the most dangerous period was the fifteen minutes before school started. The school arranged for two adults to guide students during that period. The gate remained open, and students could still use the shortest route without crossing the car park alone.","title":"A safer walk","evidence":"The school arranged for two adults to guide students during that period."},{"id":"3-07-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語30語程度で返信し、二つの質問に答えなさい。Hi! I want to give my teacher a thank-you gift. What should I give? Why is it a good choice?","answer":"You could give your teacher a handmade card. It is a good choice because you can write a personal message. You do not need to spend much money to show your thanks.","accepted":[],"why":"贈り物と理由を答える。高額な物を必要な条件とせず、気持ちが伝わる理由にします。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"3-07-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Should students watch the news regularly? 英語40語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I think they should. First, the news helps students understand what is happening in their community. Second, learning about different problems can give them useful ideas for school discussions. They should choose reliable programs suitable for their age.","accepted":[],"why":"地域の理解と議論の材料を別の理由として述べます。情報源の選び方は補足です。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":8,"questions":[{"id":"3-08-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"I have ( kept / keep / keeping ) this diary since January.","answer":"kept","accepted":["kept"],"why":"haveと過去分詞keptで継続を表します。"},{"id":"3-08-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"This picture was ( painted / painting / paint ) by my grandfather.","answer":"painted","accepted":["painted"],"why":"wasと過去分詞paintedで受動態です。"},{"id":"3-08-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"The boy ( who / which / where ) won the speech contest is in my class.","answer":"who","accepted":["who"],"why":"人boyを説明する主格の関係代名詞whoです。"},{"id":"3-08-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"Please call me before you ( leave / left / will leave ) tomorrow.","answer":"leave","accepted":["leave"],"why":"未来の時を表すbefore節は現在形です。"},{"id":"3-08-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"I don't know what ( to say / saying / said ) to her.","answer":"to say","accepted":["to say"],"why":"what to動詞で、何を言うべきかを表します。"},{"id":"3-08-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"The river is too deep ( to cross / crossing / crossed ) safely on foot.","answer":"to cross","accepted":["to cross"],"why":"too deep to動詞で、深すぎて安全に渡れないことを表します。"},{"id":"3-08-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"Our coach encouraged us ( to try / trying / tried ) again.","answer":"to try","accepted":["to try"],"why":"encourage人to動詞で、人に何かするよう励まします。"},{"id":"3-08-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"He closed the door ( slowly / slow / slowness ) to avoid making noise.","answer":"slowly","accepted":["slowly"],"why":"動詞closedを説明する副詞slowlyです。"},{"id":"3-08-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"How long have you ( studied / study / studying ) Chinese?","answer":"studied","accepted":["studied"],"why":"現在完了のhaveと過去分詞studiedです。"},{"id":"3-08-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"You ( don't have to / mustn't / can't ) pay for this map; it is free.","answer":"don't have to","accepted":["don't have to"],"why":"無料で支払いが不要なのでdon't have toです。"},{"id":"3-08-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"あなたはどのくらいの期間、このカメラを使っていますか。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( this / How / you / long / have / used / camera )","answer":"How long have you used this camera?","accepted":["How long have you used this camera?"],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 現在完了はhave/hasと過去分詞を組み合わせます。期間はfor、開始時点はsince、経験や完了は文中の時を表す語句で確認します。"},{"id":"3-08-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"彼の自転車は誰かによって持ち去られました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( was / His / away / bicycle / someone / taken / by )","answer":"His bicycle was taken away by someone.","accepted":["His bicycle was taken away by someone."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-08-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私はどちらのシャツを選ぶべきか分かりません。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( do / which / to / I / know / shirt / choose / not )","answer":"I do not know which shirt to choose.","accepted":["I do not know which shirt to choose."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-08-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"先生は私たちに辞書を使うことを許可しました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( The / to / teacher / allowed / dictionaries / use / us )","answer":"The teacher allowed us to use dictionaries.","accepted":["The teacher allowed us to use dictionaries."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 人に動作を求める部分は人とto不定詞のまとまりにします。"},{"id":"3-08-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"初心者に教える人の職業・役割を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"gardener","accepted":["gardener"],"why":"本文の根拠：An experienced gardener gave short lessons every second Saturday.","context":"Residents wanted to turn an empty area into a garden. They first planned to grow vegetables for sale. However, many volunteers were beginners and wanted to learn without pressure. The group decided to share the vegetables instead. An experienced gardener gave short lessons every second Saturday. Children helped water the plants, while adults did heavier work. By autumn, the garden had become a place where neighbors met regularly, even when there were no vegetables ready to pick.","title":"Growing together","evidence":"An experienced gardener gave short lessons every second Saturday."},{"id":"3-08-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"子供たちが植物に対してした作業の動詞を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"water","accepted":["water"],"why":"本文の根拠：Children helped water the plants, while adults did heavier work.","context":"Residents wanted to turn an empty area into a garden. They first planned to grow vegetables for sale. However, many volunteers were beginners and wanted to learn without pressure. The group decided to share the vegetables instead. An experienced gardener gave short lessons every second Saturday. Children helped water the plants, while adults did heavier work. By autumn, the garden had become a place where neighbors met regularly, even when there were no vegetables ready to pick.","title":"Growing together","evidence":"Children helped water the plants, while adults did heavier work."},{"id":"3-08-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"静かな通りを薦めた人を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"shopkeeper","accepted":["shopkeeper"],"why":"本文の根拠：At a market, a shopkeeper recommended a quiet street with small art studios.","context":"Before visiting a new city, Anna used to make a list of famous places. On her latest trip, she also left empty pages in her notebook. At a market, a shopkeeper recommended a quiet street with small art studios. Anna wrote down the directions and visited it the next day. It became her favorite part of the trip. She now plans some activities but leaves time for advice from local people rather than following a fixed list all day.","title":"A travel notebook","evidence":"At a market, a shopkeeper recommended a quiet street with small art studios."},{"id":"3-08-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"その通りにある施設を英語2語で答えなさい。","answer":"art studios","accepted":["art studios"],"why":"本文の根拠：At a market, a shopkeeper recommended a quiet street with small art studios.","context":"Before visiting a new city, Anna used to make a list of famous places. On her latest trip, she also left empty pages in her notebook. At a market, a shopkeeper recommended a quiet street with small art studios. Anna wrote down the directions and visited it the next day. It became her favorite part of the trip. She now plans some activities but leaves time for advice from local people rather than following a fixed list all day.","title":"A travel notebook","evidence":"At a market, a shopkeeper recommended a quiet street with small art studios."},{"id":"3-08-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語30語程度で返信し、二つの質問に答えなさい。Hi! I am planning a picnic. What should I bring? What should I do if it rains?","answer":"Bring water, simple food, and a mat to sit on. If it rains, you could eat indoors and play board games. Check the weather before leaving and tell everyone about the backup plan.","accepted":[],"why":"持ち物と雨の代案を答える。雨でも屋外に出ることだけを述べず、質問への対応を明確にします。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"3-08-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Is it better to borrow books or buy them? 英語40語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I prefer borrowing books. First, it saves money, so I can try many different kinds of stories. Second, I do not need extra shelves at home. However, I may buy a book if I want to read it many times.","accepted":[],"why":"お金と置き場所が二つの理由。お気に入りは買うという例外を述べても意見は成立します。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":9,"questions":[{"id":"3-09-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"My brother has ( become / became / becoming ) interested in cooking.","answer":"become","accepted":["become"],"why":"現在完了haveと過去分詞。becomeの過去分詞はbecomeです。"},{"id":"3-09-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"The bike was ( stolen / stole / stealing ) outside the shop.","answer":"stolen","accepted":["stolen"],"why":"受動態wasとstealの過去分詞stolenです。"},{"id":"3-09-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"This is the place ( where / who / when ) we meet every Sunday.","answer":"where","accepted":["where"],"why":"場所を表す先行詞placeを説明するwhereです。"},{"id":"3-09-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"If you ( need / needed / will need ) help tomorrow, tell me.","answer":"need","accepted":["need"],"why":"未来の条件でもif節は現在形です。"},{"id":"3-09-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"Please show me how ( to fold / folding / folded ) this map.","answer":"to fold","accepted":["to fold"],"why":"how to foldで折り方を表します。"},{"id":"3-09-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"This table is big enough ( to seat / seating / seated ) six people.","answer":"to seat","accepted":["to seat"],"why":"enough to動詞で、六人が座れる大きさです。"},{"id":"3-09-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"The guide asked everyone ( to stay / staying / stayed ) together.","answer":"to stay","accepted":["to stay"],"why":"ask人to動詞で、みんなに一緒にいるよう頼みます。"},{"id":"3-09-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"The athlete moved ( quickly / quick / speed ) toward the finish line.","answer":"quickly","accepted":["quickly"],"why":"動詞movedを修飾する副詞quicklyです。"},{"id":"3-09-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"A: Has the film started? B: No, it ( hasn't / didn't / wasn't ).","answer":"hasn't","accepted":["hasn't"],"why":"Hasで聞かれた現在完了にhasn'tで答えます。"},{"id":"3-09-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"Students ( have to / mustn't / can't ) return the books by Friday; this is the library rule.","answer":"have to","accepted":["have to"],"why":"規則で必要な行動なのでhave toです。"},{"id":"3-09-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私の父はちょうど仕事を終えたところです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( My / work / just / has / father / finished / his )","answer":"My father has just finished his work.","accepted":["My father has just finished his work."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 現在完了はhave/hasと過去分詞を組み合わせます。期間はfor、開始時点はsince、経験や完了は文中の時を表す語句で確認します。"},{"id":"3-09-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"日本語はこの学校で教えられています。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( this / is / Japanese / school / taught / at )","answer":"Japanese is taught at this school.","accepted":["Japanese is taught at this school."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-09-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"彼女は一人で旅行できる年齢です。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( travel / enough / is / old / alone / to / She )","answer":"She is old enough to travel alone.","accepted":["She is old enough to travel alone."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-09-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"山を登ることは私を疲れさせます。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( mountain / tired / makes / Climbing / the / me )","answer":"Climbing the mountain makes me tired.","accepted":["Climbing the mountain makes me tired."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-09-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"最初のポスターで知らせていなかった授業の対象者を本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"beginner","accepted":["beginner"],"why":"本文の根拠：It showed photographs of strong players, but no information about beginner lessons.","context":"The sports club made a poster to attract new members. It showed photographs of strong players, but no information about beginner lessons. Only experienced students joined. The club then added a sentence saying that beginners were welcome and listed the practice times. More students came to the next meeting. The club kept the original photographs because they showed what members could achieve, but made sure the poster also answered new students' practical questions.","title":"Testing a poster","evidence":"It showed photographs of strong players, but no information about beginner lessons."},{"id":"3-09-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"元のまま残したものを本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"photographs","accepted":["photographs"],"why":"本文の根拠：The club kept the original photographs because they showed what members could achieve, but made sure the poster also answered new students' practical questions.","context":"The sports club made a poster to attract new members. It showed photographs of strong players, but no information about beginner lessons. Only experienced students joined. The club then added a sentence saying that beginners were welcome and listed the practice times. More students came to the next meeting. The club kept the original photographs because they showed what members could achieve, but made sure the poster also answered new students' practical questions.","title":"Testing a poster","evidence":"The club kept the original photographs because they showed what members could achieve, but made sure the poster also answered new students' practical questions."},{"id":"3-09-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"シャツをくれた家族を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"sister","accepted":["sister"],"why":"本文の根拠：However, the old shirt had been a birthday gift from his sister, and he wanted to keep it.","context":"Ren's grandfather showed him how to mend a torn shirt. Ren first thought buying a new shirt would be easier. However, the old shirt had been a birthday gift from his sister, and he wanted to keep it. His first stitches were uneven, so he practiced on a spare piece of cloth. After several attempts, he repaired the shirt. He now keeps a small sewing kit at home and helps his family with simple repairs.","title":"A forgotten skill","evidence":"However, the old shirt had been a birthday gift from his sister, and he wanted to keep it."},{"id":"3-09-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"今、家に置いている修理道具を英語2語で答えなさい。","answer":"sewing kit","accepted":["sewing kit"],"why":"本文の根拠：He now keeps a small sewing kit at home and helps his family with simple repairs.","context":"Ren's grandfather showed him how to mend a torn shirt. Ren first thought buying a new shirt would be easier. However, the old shirt had been a birthday gift from his sister, and he wanted to keep it. His first stitches were uneven, so he practiced on a spare piece of cloth. After several attempts, he repaired the shirt. He now keeps a small sewing kit at home and helps his family with simple repairs.","title":"A forgotten skill","evidence":"He now keeps a small sewing kit at home and helps his family with simple repairs."},{"id":"3-09-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語30語程度で返信し、二つの質問に答えなさい。Hi! I have a free afternoon. What hobby could I try? What do I need for it?","answer":"You could try drawing things around your home. You only need paper and a pencil. Start with a simple object, such as a cup, and do not worry about making a perfect picture.","accepted":[],"why":"趣味と必要な道具を答える。抽象的な楽しい活動という返答だけでは具体性が不足します。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"3-09-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Should students use bicycles to go to school? 英語40語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I do not think bicycles are suitable for every student. First, some roads have heavy traffic and can be dangerous. Second, students who live nearby may get enough exercise by walking. Each family should consider the route carefully.","accepted":[],"why":"交通安全と近距離なら徒歩でよいという二つの理由。全員について一律の結論にする必要はありません。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":10,"questions":[{"id":"3-10-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"I have ( forgotten / forgot / forgetting ) her phone number.","answer":"forgotten","accepted":["forgotten"],"why":"haveとforgetの過去分詞forgottenです。"},{"id":"3-10-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"The lost dog was ( found / find / finding ) near the river.","answer":"found","accepted":["found"],"why":"受動態wasと過去分詞foundです。"},{"id":"3-10-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"The woman ( who / which / where ) works at the bakery speaks three languages.","answer":"who","accepted":["who"],"why":"人womanを説明し、worksの主語になるwhoです。"},{"id":"3-10-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"We will start as soon as everyone ( arrives / arrived / will arrive ).","answer":"arrives","accepted":["arrives"],"why":"未来の時を表すas soon asの節では現在形です。"},{"id":"3-10-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"Could you tell me what this word ( means / does / meaning )?","answer":"means","accepted":["means"],"why":"間接疑問はwhatと主語と動詞の順。wordが単数なのでmeansです。"},{"id":"3-10-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"The sentence is simple enough ( to understand / understanding / understood ) without a dictionary.","answer":"to understand","accepted":["to understand"],"why":"enough to動詞で理解できる程度の簡単さを表します。"},{"id":"3-10-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"My father taught me how ( to swim / swimming / swam ).","answer":"to swim","accepted":["to swim"],"why":"how to swimで泳ぎ方を表します。"},{"id":"3-10-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"She explained the rules ( clearly / clear / clarity ) to the new members.","answer":"clearly","accepted":["clearly"],"why":"動詞explainedを説明する副詞clearlyです。"},{"id":"3-10-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"Have you ( ever / yet / just ) tried skiing before?","answer":"ever","accepted":["ever"],"why":"beforeと共に、今までに経験があるかを尋ねるeverです。"},{"id":"3-10-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"You ( don't have to / mustn't / can't ) print the form; showing it on your phone is also allowed.","answer":"don't have to","accepted":["don't have to"],"why":"電話で示す方法も許可されているので印刷は不要です。"},{"id":"3-10-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私はこの町に五年間住んでいます。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( this / have / five / for / lived / town / years / I / in )","answer":"I have lived in this town for five years.","accepted":["I have lived in this town for five years."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 現在完了はhave/hasと過去分詞を組み合わせます。期間はfor、開始時点はsince、経験や完了は文中の時を表す語句で確認します。"},{"id":"3-10-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"電話で話している女の人は私の叔母です。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( my / on / woman / is / talking / phone / The / who / is / the / aunt )","answer":"The woman who is talking on the phone is my aunt.","accepted":["The woman who is talking on the phone is my aunt."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-10-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私はこのプログラムの使い方を学びたいです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( how / I / to / use / learn / to / want / program / this )","answer":"I want to learn how to use this program.","accepted":["I want to learn how to use this program."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"3-10-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"彼は私にあきらめないよう言いました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( up / to / told / He / give / not / me )","answer":"He told me not to give up.","accepted":["He told me not to give up."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 人に動作を求める部分は人とto不定詞のまとまりにします。"},{"id":"3-10-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"各橋に使える紙の枚数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"2","accepted":["2"],"why":"本文の根拠：The rules required each bridge to cross the same gap and use only two sheets of paper.","context":"A science club held a competition to build paper bridges. At first, teams thought the widest bridge would be the strongest. The rules required each bridge to cross the same gap and use only two sheets of paper. A narrow bridge with folded sides held the greatest weight. Afterward, the teams compared their designs and explained what they would change next time. The teacher gave a prize for the clearest explanation as well as for the strongest bridge.","title":"A different competition","evidence":"The rules required each bridge to cross the same gap and use only two sheets of paper."},{"id":"3-10-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"最も重さに耐えた橋の側面はどうなっていましたか。本文の英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"folded","accepted":["folded"],"why":"本文の根拠：A narrow bridge with folded sides held the greatest weight.","context":"A science club held a competition to build paper bridges. At first, teams thought the widest bridge would be the strongest. The rules required each bridge to cross the same gap and use only two sheets of paper. A narrow bridge with folded sides held the greatest weight. Afterward, the teams compared their designs and explained what they would change next time. The teacher gave a prize for the clearest explanation as well as for the strongest bridge.","title":"A different competition","evidence":"A narrow bridge with folded sides held the greatest weight."},{"id":"3-10-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"最初に利用したかったバスの出発時刻を数字で答えなさい（時:分）。","answer":"5:15","accepted":["5:15"],"why":"本文の根拠：Sana's club finished at five twenty, but the bus she usually took left at five fifteen.","context":"Sana's club finished at five twenty, but the bus she usually took left at five fifteen. She had to wait forty minutes for the next one. Rather than asking the driver to wait, she checked another route. A bus from a stop near the library left at five thirty. Walking there took five minutes. Sana could reach it after practice and get home earlier. She shared the route with other club members who had the same problem.","title":"An early bus decision","evidence":"Sana's club finished at five twenty, but the bus she usually took left at five fifteen."},{"id":"3-10-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"新しい停留所へ歩く時間を数字で答えなさい（分）。","answer":"5","accepted":["5"],"why":"本文の根拠：Walking there took five minutes.","context":"Sana's club finished at five twenty, but the bus she usually took left at five fifteen. She had to wait forty minutes for the next one. Rather than asking the driver to wait, she checked another route. A bus from a stop near the library left at five thirty. Walking there took five minutes. Sana could reach it after practice and get home earlier. She shared the route with other club members who had the same problem.","title":"An early bus decision","evidence":"Walking there took five minutes."},{"id":"3-10-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語30語程度で返信し、二つの質問に答えなさい。Hi! I want to join a school club. Which club do you recommend? What can I learn there?","answer":"I recommend the science club. You can learn to plan experiments and explain your results. The members often work in teams, so you can also practice sharing ideas and listening to other people.","accepted":[],"why":"部活とそこで学べることを答える。自分が薦める部活と学べる内容を一致させます。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"3-10-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Do you think schools should organize more local trips? 英語40語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"Yes, I do. First, local trips help students connect lessons with real places. Second, they can meet people who do different jobs and learn about their town. Trips should be planned carefully so that all students can take part.","accepted":[],"why":"授業と現実のつながり、地域の仕事を知ることが理由です。参加しやすさは補足です。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]}]},{"id":"pre2","label":"準2級","sets":[{"n":1,"questions":[{"id":"pre2-01-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"The museum offers free ( admission / attention / direction ) to children under six.","answer":"admission","accepted":["admission"],"why":"入場を表すadmission。attentionは注意、directionは方向です。"},{"id":"pre2-01-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"The heavy snow caused a ( delay / habit / purpose ) in train services.","answer":"delay","accepted":["delay"],"why":"列車の運行が遅れることはdelay。habitは習慣、purposeは目的です。"},{"id":"pre2-01-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"We need to ( reduce / refuse / replace ) food waste by buying only what we need.","answer":"reduce","accepted":["reduce"],"why":"必要な分だけ買うことで食品廃棄を減らすのでreduceです。"},{"id":"pre2-01-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"Our prediction was wrong: the results were different from what we had ( expected / protected / collected ).","answer":"expected","accepted":["expected"],"why":"予想していた内容との違いなのでexpected。protectは守る、collectは集めるです。"},{"id":"pre2-01-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"The match was put ( off / out / away ) until Monday because of the storm.","answer":"off","accepted":["off"],"why":"put offは延期する。put outは火を消す、put awayは片付けるです。"},{"id":"pre2-01-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"Although the route was longer, it was much ( safe / safely / safer ).","answer":"safer","accepted":["safer"],"why":"wasの補語は形容詞。muchは比較級saferを強めます。"},{"id":"pre2-01-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"I wish I ( have / had / will have ) more time to practice now.","answer":"had","accepted":["had"],"why":"現在の事実と異なる願いはI wishと過去形で表します。"},{"id":"pre2-01-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"By the time I arrived, the meeting had already ( begun / began / begin ).","answer":"begun","accepted":["begun"],"why":"hadと過去分詞で到着前の開始を表します。beginの過去分詞はbegunです。"},{"id":"pre2-01-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"She is used to ( work / working / worked ) with people from different countries.","answer":"working","accepted":["working"],"why":"be used toは「慣れている」。このtoは前置詞なのでing形を続けます。"},{"id":"pre2-01-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"The device allows users ( check / checking / to check ) the temperature remotely.","answer":"to check","accepted":["to check"],"why":"allow人to動詞で、人が何かできるようにすることを表します。"},{"id":"pre2-01-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"「彼はその申し出を受け入れるかどうか決めていません。」( the offer / decided / he / whether to accept / hasn't )","answer":"He hasn't decided whether to accept the offer.","accepted":["He hasn't decided whether to accept the offer."],"why":"whether to acceptは受け入れるかどうか。hasn't decidedの目的語になります。"},{"id":"pre2-01-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"「悪天候にもかかわらず、彼らは調査を続けました。」( the survey / despite / continued / they / the bad weather )","answer":"Despite the bad weather, they continued the survey.","accepted":["Despite the bad weather, they continued the survey.","They continued the survey despite the bad weather."],"why":"despiteのあとに名詞句を置き、逆接を表します。文末に置いても認めます。"},{"id":"pre2-01-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"「その説明は、私が理解できるほど明確でした。」( for me / clear enough / the explanation / to understand / was )","answer":"The explanation was clear enough for me to understand.","accepted":["The explanation was clear enough for me to understand."],"why":"形容詞enough for人to動詞で、人がその動作をできる程度であることを表します。"},{"id":"pre2-01-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"「誰がその展示を担当するのか教えてください。」( the display / tell me / in charge of / please / who is )","answer":"Please tell me who is in charge of the display.","accepted":["Please tell me who is in charge of the display."],"why":"間接疑問はwho isの語順。be in charge ofは担当しているという意味です。"},{"id":"pre2-01-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"ラベルのない食品では何の確認が難しかったですか。日本語で答えなさい。","answer":"食品がどれくらいの期間保存されていたか","accepted":["食品がどれくらいの期間保存されていたか","食品の保存期間","食品がいつから保存されているか"],"why":"how long food had been storedが根拠。種類や量だけを答えると目的を捉えられていません。","context":"Westfield residents opened a shared freezer for extra garden vegetables. At first, anyone could leave food without a label. Volunteers soon found that this made it difficult to check how long food had been stored. They introduced labels showing the date and the name of the vegetable. Cooked meals are not accepted because the volunteers cannot check all ingredients. The freezer is open three afternoons a week. A nearby cafe pays the electricity bill, while residents take turns cleaning the area.","title":"A shared freezer","self":true},{"id":"pre2-01-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"電気代を払っている施設を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"cafe","accepted":["cafe"],"why":"A nearby cafe pays the electricity billが根拠です。住民は清掃を分担します。","context":"Westfield residents opened a shared freezer for extra garden vegetables. At first, anyone could leave food without a label. Volunteers soon found that this made it difficult to check how long food had been stored. They introduced labels showing the date and the name of the vegetable. Cooked meals are not accepted because the volunteers cannot check all ingredients. The freezer is open three afternoons a week. A nearby cafe pays the electricity bill, while residents take turns cleaning the area.","title":"A shared freezer"},{"id":"pre2-01-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"利用者が少なかった理由を日本語で答えなさい。","answer":"多くの授業が終わる10分前にバスが出発していたから","accepted":["多くの授業が終わる10分前にバスが出発していたから","多くの授業の終了より10分早くバスが出発したから"],"why":"wanted the serviceへの肯定と実際の利用は別。2回目の調査で出発時刻の問題が分かりました。","context":"A town tested a late bus for students attending evening classes. The first survey asked whether people wanted the service, and most said yes. However, only a few used it during the first month. A second survey revealed that the bus left ten minutes before many classes ended. The town changed the departure time rather than canceling the route. Passenger numbers then increased. Officials decided to continue the test for three more months before making a final decision.","title":"Testing a bus route","self":true},{"id":"pre2-01-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"最終判断の前に、さらに何か月試験運行しますか。数字で答えなさい。","answer":"3","accepted":["3"],"why":"for three more monthsが根拠です。first monthは最初の実施期間です。","context":"A town tested a late bus for students attending evening classes. The first survey asked whether people wanted the service, and most said yes. However, only a few used it during the first month. A second survey revealed that the bus left ten minutes before many classes ended. The town changed the departure time rather than canceling the route. Passenger numbers then increased. Officials decided to continue the test for three more months before making a final decision.","title":"Testing a bus route"},{"id":"pre2-01-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語50語程度でメールへの返信を書きなさい。相手の提案に賛成か反対かと理由を述べ、必要な情報を一つ質問しなさい。Our club may hold a weekend event where students exchange books. Do you think this is a good idea?","answer":"I think a book exchange is a good idea because students can discover new stories without spending much money. It also gives us a chance to talk about our favorite writers. Could you tell me where we would hold the event? We will need enough space for the books.","accepted":["I think a book exchange is a good idea because students can discover new stories without spending much money. It also gives us a chance to talk about our favorite writers. Could you tell me where we would hold the event? We will need enough space for the books."],"why":"賛否、関連する理由、情報を求める質問が必要です。書き手の意図が伝わるかを確認し、例と違う考えでも認めます。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"pre2-01-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Should towns provide more places where young people can study after school? 英語60語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I think towns should provide more study spaces. First, some students do not have a quiet place at home, so a public space would help them concentrate. Second, students could support each other when they have difficult homework. These spaces should have clear rules so that everyone can use them safely and comfortably. This would make them more useful.","accepted":["I think towns should provide more study spaces. First, some students do not have a quiet place at home, so a public space would help them concentrate. Second, students could support each other when they have difficult homework. These spaces should have clear rules so that everyone can use them safely and comfortably. This would make them more useful."],"why":"YesでもNoでもよい。理由二つが別の観点か、意見を支えているか、文同士がつながるかを評価します。模範例は唯一の正答ではありません。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":2,"questions":[{"id":"pre2-02-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"The school will ( install / insist / invent ) solar panels on the roof next month.","answer":"install","accepted":["install"],"why":"設備を設置する動作はinstallです。insistは主張する、inventは発明するです。"},{"id":"pre2-02-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"The volunteers made a valuable ( contribution / competition / confusion ) to the project.","answer":"contribution","accepted":["contribution"],"why":"プロジェクトへの貢献はcontributionです。"},{"id":"pre2-02-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"We must ( preserve / persuade / predict ) this forest so future generations can enjoy it.","answer":"preserve","accepted":["preserve"],"why":"森林を保護・保存するのでpreserveです。"},{"id":"pre2-02-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"The two reports ( differ / suffer / prefer ) in their conclusions; one recommends closing, the other staying open.","answer":"differ","accepted":["differ"],"why":"結論が異なることはdifferです。"},{"id":"pre2-02-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"Please ( fill in / give up / put out ) this form before your interview.","answer":"fill in","accepted":["fill in"],"why":"用紙に記入する表現はfill inです。"},{"id":"pre2-02-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"The hall was ( so / such / too ) crowded that we had to wait outside.","answer":"so","accepted":["so"],"why":"so形容詞that節で、非常に～なのでという結果を表します。"},{"id":"pre2-02-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"I wish I ( could / can / will ) speak several languages now.","answer":"could","accepted":["could"],"why":"現在の事実と異なる願いをwishと過去形couldで表します。"},{"id":"pre2-02-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"When we got to the cinema, the film had already ( started / start / starting ).","answer":"started","accepted":["started"],"why":"hadと過去分詞で、到着より前の開始を表します。"},{"id":"pre2-02-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"I'm looking forward to ( meeting / meet / met ) your family.","answer":"meeting","accepted":["meeting"],"why":"look forward toのtoは前置詞なのでing形を続けます。"},{"id":"pre2-02-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"This program enables children ( to explore / exploring / explored ) science through experiments.","answer":"to explore","accepted":["to explore"],"why":"enable人to動詞で、人が何かできるようにするという意味です。"},{"id":"pre2-02-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私はその計画に賛成するかどうか、まだ決めていません。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( to / whether / have / support / plan / not / I / decided / the )","answer":"I have not decided whether to support the plan.","accepted":["I have not decided whether to support the plan."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 現在完了はhave/hasと過去分詞を組み合わせます。期間はfor、開始時点はsince、経験や完了は文中の時を表す語句で確認します。"},{"id":"pre2-02-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"その店は駅から歩いて行けるほど近いです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( the / close / shop / enough / to / station / is / The / from / to / walk )","answer":"The shop is close enough to walk to from the station.","accepted":["The shop is close enough to walk to from the station."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-02-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"大雨にもかかわらず、その催しは行われました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( rain / place / took / the / the / event / heavy / Despite )","answer":"Despite the heavy rain, the event took place.","accepted":["Despite the heavy rain, the event took place."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-02-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"私たちは客に到着時に登録するよう求めました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( required / arrival / guests / We / on / to / register )","answer":"We required guests to register on arrival.","accepted":["We required guests to register on arrival."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 人に動作を求める部分は人とto不定詞のまとまりにします。"},{"id":"pre2-02-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"配達回数を減らした方法を日本語で説明しなさい。","answer":"同じ地域の配達を決まった日にまとめた。","accepted":["同じ地域の配達を決まった日にまとめた。"],"why":"本文の根拠：The bakery asked those customers whether fixed delivery days would be acceptable. Most agreed, as long as they could still change urgent orders. Combining deliveries reduced the number of trips.","context":"A local bakery considered buying a larger delivery truck because orders had increased. Before making the purchase, the manager checked the delivery records. Many customers ordered small amounts on different days, even when they lived on the same street. The bakery asked those customers whether fixed delivery days would be acceptable. Most agreed, as long as they could still change urgent orders. Combining deliveries reduced the number of trips. The bakery kept its existing truck and used the saved money to improve packaging. It will review the arrangement during the busy holiday season.","title":"A smaller delivery truck","evidence":"The bakery asked those customers whether fixed delivery days would be acceptable. Most agreed, as long as they could still change urgent orders. Combining deliveries reduced the number of trips."},{"id":"pre2-02-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"節約したお金で改善したものを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"packaging","accepted":["packaging"],"why":"本文の根拠：The bakery kept its existing truck and used the saved money to improve packaging.","context":"A local bakery considered buying a larger delivery truck because orders had increased. Before making the purchase, the manager checked the delivery records. Many customers ordered small amounts on different days, even when they lived on the same street. The bakery asked those customers whether fixed delivery days would be acceptable. Most agreed, as long as they could still change urgent orders. Combining deliveries reduced the number of trips. The bakery kept its existing truck and used the saved money to improve packaging. It will review the arrangement during the busy holiday season.","title":"A smaller delivery truck","evidence":"The bakery kept its existing truck and used the saved money to improve packaging."},{"id":"pre2-02-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"質問方法を変えた理由を日本語で説明しなさい。","answer":"決まった質問に合わない有用な思い出があり、急がされていると感じる人もいたから。","accepted":["決まった質問に合わない有用な思い出があり、急がされていると感じる人もいたから。"],"why":"本文の根拠：Older residents often remembered useful details that did not fit those questions, and some felt rushed.","context":"A town museum began recording residents' memories of a former railway line. Initially, volunteers asked everyone the same ten questions. Older residents often remembered useful details that did not fit those questions, and some felt rushed. The project leader changed the process. Volunteers still collected essential dates and locations, but then allowed residents to choose a story to tell. Recordings became longer, so short summaries were added to help researchers find relevant sections. The museum keeps both the summaries and the complete recordings, with each speaker's permission.","title":"A community recording project","evidence":"Older residents often remembered useful details that did not fit those questions, and some felt rushed."},{"id":"pre2-02-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"録音の関連箇所を探しやすくするため追加したものを本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"summaries","accepted":["summaries"],"why":"本文の根拠：Recordings became longer, so short summaries were added to help researchers find relevant sections.","context":"A town museum began recording residents' memories of a former railway line. Initially, volunteers asked everyone the same ten questions. Older residents often remembered useful details that did not fit those questions, and some felt rushed. The project leader changed the process. Volunteers still collected essential dates and locations, but then allowed residents to choose a story to tell. Recordings became longer, so short summaries were added to help researchers find relevant sections. The museum keeps both the summaries and the complete recordings, with each speaker's permission.","title":"A community recording project","evidence":"Recordings became longer, so short summaries were added to help researchers find relevant sections."},{"id":"pre2-02-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語50語程度でメールへ返信し、提案への賛否と理由を述べ、必要な情報を一つ質問しなさい。Our school is considering a day when students teach each other a useful skill. Do you think this would work well?","answer":"I think this could work well because students may feel comfortable asking classmates questions. It would also give them a chance to explain something clearly, which is useful practice. Could you tell me how long each lesson would be? Some skills may need more time than others.","accepted":[],"why":"賛否、関連する理由、必要情報への質問を含めます。授業時間への質問は具体的で、提案とつながります。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"pre2-02-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Should public libraries offer more activities for teenagers? 英語60語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I think they should. First, activities such as reading groups can help teenagers discover books they would not choose alone. Second, libraries can provide a safe place to meet people with similar interests. The activities should not disturb visitors who need quiet study space. Offering them in a separate room would make the library useful to more people.","accepted":[],"why":"読書の発見と安全な交流を別の理由にしています。静かな利用者への配慮を補足してもよいです。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":3,"questions":[{"id":"pre2-03-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"The company needs to ( expand / expect / explain ) its factory because orders have doubled.","answer":"expand","accepted":["expand"],"why":"注文増加に対応して工場を拡張するのでexpandです。"},{"id":"pre2-03-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"There is a ( shortage / journey / bargain ) of drinking water after the drought.","answer":"shortage","accepted":["shortage"],"why":"干ばつ後の飲料水不足はshortageです。"},{"id":"pre2-03-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"A recent study ( revealed / removed / repaired ) that many residents wanted a safer crossing.","answer":"revealed","accepted":["revealed"],"why":"研究が事実を明らかにしたのでrevealedです。"},{"id":"pre2-03-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"The information must be ( accurate / ancient / anxious ) because doctors will use it to choose treatment.","answer":"accurate","accepted":["accurate"],"why":"治療選択に使う情報には正確さaccurateが必要です。"},{"id":"pre2-03-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"We ( ran out of / got along with / came up to ) paper and could not print any more pages.","answer":"ran out of","accepted":["ran out of"],"why":"使い切ってなくなるのはrun out ofです。"},{"id":"pre2-03-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"The route was changed ( due to / despite / instead of ) damage to the bridge; the damage caused the change.","answer":"due to","accepted":["due to"],"why":"原因が橋の損傷なのでdue toです。"},{"id":"pre2-03-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"If I ( were / am / will be ) you, I would discuss the problem with the teacher.","answer":"were","accepted":["were"],"why":"If I were youは相手の立場を仮定した助言の表現です。"},{"id":"pre2-03-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"She couldn't find the book she had ( borrowed / borrow / borrowing ) the previous week.","answer":"borrowed","accepted":["borrowed"],"why":"hadと過去分詞で、探す時より前の借用を表します。"},{"id":"pre2-03-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"He apologized for ( arriving / arrive / arrived ) late.","answer":"arriving","accepted":["arriving"],"why":"前置詞forの後にはing形です。"},{"id":"pre2-03-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"We were encouraged ( to share / sharing / shared ) our ideas during the meeting.","answer":"to share","accepted":["to share"],"why":"be encouraged to動詞で、するよう励まされたことを表します。"},{"id":"pre2-03-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"電車が出発するまでに、私は切符をなくしたことに気付きました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( I / By / the / time / the / ticket / realized / I / that / train / lost / had / had / departed / my )","answer":"By the time the train departed, I had realized that I had lost my ticket.","accepted":["By the time the train departed, I had realized that I had lost my ticket."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-03-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"私は新しいチームに加わるのを楽しみにしています。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( new / I / to / team / forward / looking / joining / the / am )","answer":"I am looking forward to joining the new team.","accepted":["I am looking forward to joining the new team."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-03-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私はその会議がどこで開かれるのか知りません。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( held / do / will / not / know / meeting / the / be / I / where )","answer":"I do not know where the meeting will be held.","accepted":["I do not know where the meeting will be held."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-03-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"修理のため、その建物は閉鎖されました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( was / due / to / repairs / The / closed / building )","answer":"The building was closed due to repairs.","accepted":["The building was closed due to repairs."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-03-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"空の容器を先に量る説明を加えた理由を日本語で答えなさい。","answer":"容器の重さが料金に含まれるか分からない客がいたから。","accepted":["容器の重さが料金に含まれるか分からない客がいたから。"],"why":"本文の根拠：During the first week, some were confused about whether container weight was included.","context":"A supermarket tested a refill station for household soap. Customers brought empty containers and paid according to the weight of the soap. During the first week, some were confused about whether container weight was included. Staff added clear instructions and demonstrated how to weigh an empty container first. The trial reduced disposable packaging, but serving customers took longer than expected. Rather than removing the station, the store scheduled an extra employee at busy times. The manager will compare the cost of extra staff with packaging savings before deciding whether to expand the service.","title":"A refill trial","evidence":"During the first week, some were confused about whether container weight was included.","self":true},{"id":"pre2-03-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"忙しい時間に追加することにしたものを英語2語で答えなさい。","answer":"extra employee","accepted":["extra employee"],"why":"本文の根拠：Rather than removing the station, the store scheduled an extra employee at busy times.","context":"A supermarket tested a refill station for household soap. Customers brought empty containers and paid according to the weight of the soap. During the first week, some were confused about whether container weight was included. Staff added clear instructions and demonstrated how to weigh an empty container first. The trial reduced disposable packaging, but serving customers took longer than expected. Rather than removing the station, the store scheduled an extra employee at busy times. The manager will compare the cost of extra staff with packaging savings before deciding whether to expand the service.","title":"A refill trial","evidence":"Rather than removing the station, the store scheduled an extra employee at busy times."},{"id":"pre2-03-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"遮光板は光をどちらへ向けましたか。英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"downward","accepted":["downward"],"why":"本文の根拠：The council tested shields that directed light downward and timers that reduced brightness after eleven.","context":"A village installed bright lights along a riverside path to make evening walks safer. Some residents welcomed the change, while others noticed that the lights shone into their bedrooms. A wildlife group also raised concerns about constant lighting near the river. The council tested shields that directed light downward and timers that reduced brightness after eleven. Walkers still had enough light to see the path, and nearby homes were less affected. The council has not decided to use the system everywhere; it will first collect feedback over the winter, when evenings are longer.","title":"A light at night","evidence":"The council tested shields that directed light downward and timers that reduced brightness after eleven."},{"id":"pre2-03-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"全面導入を即決しなかった理由を日本語で説明しなさい。","answer":"夜が長い冬の間にも意見を集めてから判断するため。","accepted":["夜が長い冬の間にも意見を集めてから判断するため。"],"why":"本文の根拠：The council has not decided to use the system everywhere; it will first collect feedback over the winter, when evenings are longer.","context":"A village installed bright lights along a riverside path to make evening walks safer. Some residents welcomed the change, while others noticed that the lights shone into their bedrooms. A wildlife group also raised concerns about constant lighting near the river. The council tested shields that directed light downward and timers that reduced brightness after eleven. Walkers still had enough light to see the path, and nearby homes were less affected. The council has not decided to use the system everywhere; it will first collect feedback over the winter, when evenings are longer.","title":"A light at night","evidence":"The council has not decided to use the system everywhere; it will first collect feedback over the winter, when evenings are longer."},{"id":"pre2-03-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語50語程度でメールへ返信し、賛否と理由を述べ、必要な情報を一つ質問しなさい。Our neighborhood may start a tool-sharing service. People would borrow tools instead of buying them. Would you support this idea?","answer":"I would support it because many tools are used only a few times a year. Sharing could save money and reduce the space needed at home. However, the tools must be safe to use. Who would check them before they are borrowed? Clear rules would help residents trust the service.","accepted":[],"why":"賛成理由と安全管理への質問を結び付けています。反対でも、提案に関連する理由と情報質問が必要です。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"pre2-03-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Should students be allowed to choose some of their school subjects? 英語60語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I think students should choose some subjects, while still studying important basic ones. First, choice can make students more motivated because they can explore their interests. Second, different students may need different skills for their future plans. Teachers should explain the options clearly so that students do not choose only the easiest classes without considering what they will learn.","accepted":[],"why":"意欲と将来の必要技能を理由にします。基本科目も学ぶという条件は問いへの答えを妨げません。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":4,"questions":[{"id":"pre2-04-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"The city plans to ( improve / include / imagine ) the bus service by adding evening routes.","answer":"improve","accepted":["improve"],"why":"夜間便を増やしてサービスを改善するのでimproveです。"},{"id":"pre2-04-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"The price is ( reasonable / responsible / remarkable ) for a meal of this size; most students can afford it.","answer":"reasonable","accepted":["reasonable"],"why":"手頃で無理のない値段はreasonableです。"},{"id":"pre2-04-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"Parents must give ( permission / performance / pollution ) before children join the trip.","answer":"permission","accepted":["permission"],"why":"参加の許可を与えるのでpermissionです。"},{"id":"pre2-04-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"These bags are ( reusable / invisible / electrical ), so you can carry groceries in them many times.","answer":"reusable","accepted":["reusable"],"why":"何度も使えるものはreusableです。"},{"id":"pre2-04-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"I want to ( find out / turn down / take off ) why the machine stopped working.","answer":"find out","accepted":["find out"],"why":"理由を調べて知るのはfind outです。"},{"id":"pre2-04-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"( Although / During / Because of ) the task was difficult, the students completed it.","answer":"Although","accepted":["Although"],"why":"主語と動詞のある譲歩の節を導くAlthoughです。"},{"id":"pre2-04-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"I would travel more if I ( had / have / will have ) enough money now.","answer":"had","accepted":["had"],"why":"現在の事実と異なる仮定なのでif節に過去形hadです。"},{"id":"pre2-04-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"By noon, we had ( sold / sell / selling ) all the tickets.","answer":"sold","accepted":["sold"],"why":"hadと過去分詞soldで、その時までの完了を表します。"},{"id":"pre2-04-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"She is accustomed to ( working / work / worked ) at night.","answer":"working","accepted":["working"],"why":"be accustomed toのtoは前置詞なのでing形です。"},{"id":"pre2-04-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"The guide warned us ( not to approach / not approaching / didn't approach ) the animals.","answer":"not to approach","accepted":["not to approach"],"why":"warn人not to動詞で、しないよう警告します。"},{"id":"pre2-04-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"もし私にもっと時間があれば、料理を習うのに。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( would / more / had / If / I / I / to / cook / learn / time )","answer":"If I had more time, I would learn to cook.","accepted":["If I had more time, I would learn to cook."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 現在の事実と違う仮定なので、If節に過去形had、主節にwould＋動詞の原形を置きます。"},{"id":"pre2-04-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"彼女は自分の考えをより明確に説明することができました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( ideas / explain / more / clearly / to / She / her / was / able )","answer":"She was able to explain her ideas more clearly.","accepted":["She was able to explain her ideas more clearly."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-04-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"彼は予約を確認するために電話しました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( He / called / reservation / in / confirm / his / to / order )","answer":"He called in order to confirm his reservation.","accepted":["He called in order to confirm his reservation."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-04-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"あなたは私にいつまで待てばよいか教えてくれますか。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( should / long / you / how / wait / I / tell / Could / me )","answer":"Could you tell me how long I should wait?","accepted":["Could you tell me how long I should wait?"],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-04-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"新しい絞り込み機能で選べる条件二つを日本語で答えなさい。","answer":"経験のレベルと参加できる曜日。","accepted":["経験のレベルと参加できる曜日。"],"why":"本文の根拠：Instead, they tested a filter for experience level and available days.","context":"A sports center's website listed every class in alphabetical order. Although the list was complete, visitors frequently called to ask which classes were suitable for beginners. The staff first considered adding more descriptions to the same page. Instead, they tested a filter for experience level and available days. Visitors could narrow the list before reading detailed descriptions. Calls about beginner classes decreased, but some users with older phones had trouble with the filter. The center therefore kept a simple text list as an alternative while improving the new feature.","title":"A more useful website","evidence":"Instead, they tested a filter for experience level and available days.","self":true},{"id":"pre2-04-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"旧型の電話への対応として残したものを英語2語で答えなさい。","answer":"text list","accepted":["text list"],"why":"本文の根拠：The center therefore kept a simple text list as an alternative while improving the new feature.","context":"A sports center's website listed every class in alphabetical order. Although the list was complete, visitors frequently called to ask which classes were suitable for beginners. The staff first considered adding more descriptions to the same page. Instead, they tested a filter for experience level and available days. Visitors could narrow the list before reading detailed descriptions. Calls about beginner classes decreased, but some users with older phones had trouble with the filter. The center therefore kept a simple text list as an alternative while improving the new feature.","title":"A more useful website","evidence":"The center therefore kept a simple text list as an alternative while improving the new feature."},{"id":"pre2-04-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"初心者が利用を避けた理由を日本語で答えなさい。","answer":"栽培に失敗することを心配していたから。","accepted":["栽培に失敗することを心配していたから。"],"why":"本文の根拠：At first, many beginners avoided the service because they worried about failing.","context":"A library began lending packets of vegetable seeds. Borrowers were encouraged to grow the plants and return seeds from their harvest, but returning seeds was not required. At first, many beginners avoided the service because they worried about failing. Staff replaced the phrase loan with seed sharing and explained that learning was part of the project. Experienced gardeners also offered monthly advice sessions. Participation increased, and some successful growers donated more seeds than they had received. The library now records which varieties grow well locally, without identifying individual borrowers in public reports.","title":"A seed library","evidence":"At first, many beginners avoided the service because they worried about failing.","self":true},{"id":"pre2-04-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"助言をする人の役割を本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"gardeners","accepted":["gardeners"],"why":"本文の根拠：Experienced gardeners also offered monthly advice sessions.","context":"A library began lending packets of vegetable seeds. Borrowers were encouraged to grow the plants and return seeds from their harvest, but returning seeds was not required. At first, many beginners avoided the service because they worried about failing. Staff replaced the phrase loan with seed sharing and explained that learning was part of the project. Experienced gardeners also offered monthly advice sessions. Participation increased, and some successful growers donated more seeds than they had received. The library now records which varieties grow well locally, without identifying individual borrowers in public reports.","title":"A seed library","evidence":"Experienced gardeners also offered monthly advice sessions."},{"id":"pre2-04-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語50語程度でメールへ返信し、賛否と理由を述べ、必要な情報を一つ質問しなさい。Our class may organize a weekend clean-up near the river. Do you think we should take part?","answer":"I think we should take part because rubbish can harm animals and make the area unpleasant. Working together could also help us learn about local problems. Could you tell me what safety equipment will be provided? We should avoid picking up dangerous objects without advice from an adult.","accepted":[],"why":"参加の理由と安全装備に関する質問です。危険な物への対応は提案に関係する補足です。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"pre2-04-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Is working in groups usually better than working alone? 英語60語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I do not think group work is always better. First, people sometimes spend too much time arranging meetings instead of completing the task. Second, a person working alone can concentrate deeply without frequent interruptions. Group work is valuable when different skills are needed, but the method should depend on the task rather than being used for every assignment.","accepted":[],"why":"日程調整と集中の二つの理由です。集団作業の利点も認めながら、結論を明確に保ちます。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":5,"questions":[{"id":"pre2-05-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"The scientist will ( investigate / introduce / imitate ) the cause of the sudden fish deaths.","answer":"investigate","accepted":["investigate"],"why":"原因を調査するのでinvestigateです。"},{"id":"pre2-05-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"Local shops suffered a loss of ( income / interest / injury ) when the road was closed and customers stopped coming.","answer":"income","accepted":["income"],"why":"顧客減少で収入incomeが失われたという意味です。"},{"id":"pre2-05-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"The library has a large ( collection / connection / condition ) of books about local history.","answer":"collection","accepted":["collection"],"why":"書籍の収蔵・集まりはcollectionです。"},{"id":"pre2-05-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"The manager was ( satisfied / frightened / confused ) with our work and said we had done an excellent job.","answer":"satisfied","accepted":["satisfied"],"why":"優れた仕事として評価したので、満足しているsatisfiedです。"},{"id":"pre2-05-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"We had to ( put off / take after / break into ) the trip until the storm passed.","answer":"put off","accepted":["put off"],"why":"嵐が去るまで延期するのでput offです。"},{"id":"pre2-05-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"The instructions were ( such / so / too ) a mess that nobody could follow them.","answer":"such","accepted":["such"],"why":"suchと名詞句とthat節の形です。"},{"id":"pre2-05-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"If the bus ( came / comes / will come ) more often, I would use it every day.","answer":"came","accepted":["came"],"why":"would useにつながる仮定なのでif節は過去形です。"},{"id":"pre2-05-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"She recognized the song because she had ( heard / hear / hearing ) it before.","answer":"heard","accepted":["heard"],"why":"hadと過去分詞heardで以前の経験を示します。"},{"id":"pre2-05-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"The team succeeded in ( reducing / reduce / reduced ) the amount of waste.","answer":"reducing","accepted":["reducing"],"why":"succeed inのinは前置詞なのでing形です。"},{"id":"pre2-05-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"The new rule requires visitors ( to register / registering / registered ) at the entrance.","answer":"to register","accepted":["to register"],"why":"require人to動詞で、人に何かすることを求めます。"},{"id":"pre2-05-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"その提案は検討する価値があります。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( is / The / suggestion / worth / considering )","answer":"The suggestion is worth considering.","accepted":["The suggestion is worth considering."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-05-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"私たちはイベントでプラスチックを使うのを避けました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( plastic / event / avoided / We / using / at / the )","answer":"We avoided using plastic at the event.","accepted":["We avoided using plastic at the event."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-05-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"今の私に、もっと自信があればよいのに。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( had / now / confidence / wish / I / more / I )","answer":"I wish I had more confidence now.","accepted":["I wish I had more confidence now."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 現在の願望はI wish＋主語＋過去形で表します。このhadは「持っている」というhaveの過去形です。"},{"id":"pre2-05-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"彼女はボランティアを管理する担当です。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( of / in / the / She / is / managing / volunteers / charge )","answer":"She is in charge of managing the volunteers.","accepted":["She is in charge of managing the volunteers."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-05-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"欠席増加の主な理由を日本語で説明しなさい。","answer":"仕事の勤務が6時に終わり、授業開始に間に合わない生徒がいたから。","accepted":["仕事の勤務が6時に終わり、授業開始に間に合わない生徒がいたから。"],"why":"本文の根拠：A private survey showed that several students' work shifts ended at six and they could not arrive on time.","context":"A language school offered an evening course beginning at six. Applications were high, but attendance fell after the first two weeks. Teachers assumed the lessons were too difficult. A private survey showed that several students' work shifts ended at six and they could not arrive on time. The school moved the start to six thirty and shortened the break, keeping the same total teaching time. Attendance improved without simplifying the lessons. The school will ask about schedules before opening its next course, rather than using applications alone to predict attendance.","title":"A changed class schedule","evidence":"A private survey showed that several students' work shifts ended at six and they could not arrive on time."},{"id":"pre2-05-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"変更後の開始時刻を数字で答えなさい（時:分）。","answer":"6:30","accepted":["6:30"],"why":"本文の根拠：The school moved the start to six thirty and shortened the break, keeping the same total teaching time.","context":"A language school offered an evening course beginning at six. Applications were high, but attendance fell after the first two weeks. Teachers assumed the lessons were too difficult. A private survey showed that several students' work shifts ended at six and they could not arrive on time. The school moved the start to six thirty and shortened the break, keeping the same total teaching time. Attendance improved without simplifying the lessons. The school will ask about schedules before opening its next course, rather than using applications alone to predict attendance.","title":"A changed class schedule","evidence":"The school moved the start to six thirty and shortened the break, keeping the same total teaching time."},{"id":"pre2-05-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"寄付道具の受け入れ時に新しく行うことを日本語で答えなさい。","answer":"安全点検をする。","accepted":["安全点検をする。"],"why":"本文の根拠：They introduced a safety inspection before each tool entered the collection and recorded repairs separately.","context":"Residents set up a service for borrowing tools used only occasionally. To keep costs low, donated tools were accepted at first without inspection. When two drills failed during use, volunteers realized that donations needed checking. They introduced a safety inspection before each tool entered the collection and recorded repairs separately. Borrowing still remained free, but users had to book in advance so volunteers could prepare the equipment. The service accepted fewer donations afterward, yet residents reported greater confidence because the condition of each tool was clearly shown.","title":"Borrowing useful tools","evidence":"They introduced a safety inspection before each tool entered the collection and recorded repairs separately.","self":true},{"id":"pre2-05-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"利用者が事前にする必要がある動作を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"book","accepted":["book"],"why":"本文の根拠：Borrowing still remained free, but users had to book in advance so volunteers could prepare the equipment.","context":"Residents set up a service for borrowing tools used only occasionally. To keep costs low, donated tools were accepted at first without inspection. When two drills failed during use, volunteers realized that donations needed checking. They introduced a safety inspection before each tool entered the collection and recorded repairs separately. Borrowing still remained free, but users had to book in advance so volunteers could prepare the equipment. The service accepted fewer donations afterward, yet residents reported greater confidence because the condition of each tool was clearly shown.","title":"Borrowing useful tools","evidence":"Borrowing still remained free, but users had to book in advance so volunteers could prepare the equipment."},{"id":"pre2-05-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語50語程度でメールへ返信し、賛否と理由を述べ、必要な情報を一つ質問しなさい。A local museum wants students to create short guides for younger visitors. Would this be a useful project?","answer":"I think it would be useful because explaining an exhibit simply requires us to understand it well. Younger visitors might also enjoy a guide written by students. Which exhibits would we be responsible for? We should check our information with museum staff before visitors use the guides.","accepted":[],"why":"自分たちの学習と来館者への利点を述べ、担当展示を質問しています。事実確認の提案も有効です。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"pre2-05-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Should towns spend more money on bicycle routes? 英語60語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I think towns should improve bicycle routes where there is clear demand. First, safer routes can encourage people to travel without cars, reducing traffic. Second, cycling can provide useful exercise during everyday trips. Towns should connect routes to places people actually visit, such as schools and stations, rather than building isolated paths that are attractive but rarely used.","accepted":[],"why":"交通と健康を理由にしています。使われる経路への投資という条件を付けてもよいです。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":6,"questions":[{"id":"pre2-06-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"We need to ( replace / represent / remain ) the broken window with a new one.","answer":"replace","accepted":["replace"],"why":"新しいものに取り替えるのでreplaceです。"},{"id":"pre2-06-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"The hotel offers a ( discount / distance / discovery ) of ten percent to students.","answer":"discount","accepted":["discount"],"why":"学生への一割の値引きはdiscountです。"},{"id":"pre2-06-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"It was an ( emergency / exhibition / estimate ); we needed an ambulance immediately.","answer":"emergency","accepted":["emergency"],"why":"救急車をすぐ必要とする緊急事態はemergencyです。"},{"id":"pre2-06-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"The two designs are ( similar / single / social ); both use the same shape and colors.","answer":"similar","accepted":["similar"],"why":"形と色が同じようなものなのでsimilarです。"},{"id":"pre2-06-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"Please ( keep up with / look down on / get rid of ) the group so you do not fall behind.","answer":"keep up with","accepted":["keep up with"],"why":"遅れずについていく表現はkeep up withです。"},{"id":"pre2-06-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"You can borrow the bike ( as long as / even though / instead of ) you return it tonight; that is the condition.","answer":"as long as","accepted":["as long as"],"why":"明示された条件「今夜返す限り」はas long asです。"},{"id":"pre2-06-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"I wish the room ( were / is / will be ) quieter right now.","answer":"were","accepted":["were"],"why":"現在と異なる願望なのでwishの後に過去形wereです。"},{"id":"pre2-06-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"The guests had ( left / leave / leaving ) by the time we arrived.","answer":"left","accepted":["left"],"why":"到着より前に去っていたのでhadと過去分詞leftです。"},{"id":"pre2-06-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"They are responsible for ( checking / check / checked ) the safety equipment.","answer":"checking","accepted":["checking"],"why":"前置詞forの後にはing形です。"},{"id":"pre2-06-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"She reminded me ( to charge / charging / charged ) my phone before the trip.","answer":"to charge","accepted":["to charge"],"why":"remind人to動詞で、忘れずするよう注意します。"},{"id":"pre2-06-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"彼らはエネルギーを節約する新しい方法を考え出しました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( save / They / to / energy / up / way / came / a / with / new )","answer":"They came up with a new way to save energy.","accepted":["They came up with a new way to save energy."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-06-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"天気が改善しない限り、私たちは出発できません。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( we / the / weather / Unless / leave / cannot / improves )","answer":"Unless the weather improves, we cannot leave.","accepted":["Unless the weather improves, we cannot leave."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-06-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私たちが到着した時には、客はすでに帰っていました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( when / The / left / had / we / guests / arrived / already )","answer":"The guests had already left when we arrived.","accepted":["The guests had already left when we arrived."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-06-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"私は週末に働くことに慣れています。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( weekends / I / working / am / to / used / on )","answer":"I am used to working on weekends.","accepted":["I am used to working on weekends."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-06-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"観光案内の一グループの上限人数を数字で答えなさい。","answer":"8","accepted":["8"],"why":"本文の根拠：Local shops provided information about quiet routes, and each group was limited to eight visitors.","context":"A coastal town wanted to attract tourists outside the summer season. A consultant suggested large weekend events, but residents worried about noise and traffic. The town instead tried small guided walks on weekday afternoons. Local shops provided information about quiet routes, and each group was limited to eight visitors. The walks brought fewer people than a major festival would, but visitors stayed longer in shops and cafes. The town will continue the program if local businesses benefit without disturbing daily life. It is tracking spending as well as visitor numbers.","title":"A balanced visitor plan","evidence":"Local shops provided information about quiet routes, and each group was limited to eight visitors."},{"id":"pre2-06-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"町が来訪人数だけでなく確認する指標を日本語で答えなさい。","answer":"観光客が使ったお金。","accepted":["観光客が使ったお金。"],"why":"本文の根拠：It is tracking spending as well as visitor numbers.","context":"A coastal town wanted to attract tourists outside the summer season. A consultant suggested large weekend events, but residents worried about noise and traffic. The town instead tried small guided walks on weekday afternoons. Local shops provided information about quiet routes, and each group was limited to eight visitors. The walks brought fewer people than a major festival would, but visitors stayed longer in shops and cafes. The town will continue the program if local businesses benefit without disturbing daily life. It is tracking spending as well as visitor numbers.","title":"A balanced visitor plan","evidence":"It is tracking spending as well as visitor numbers.","self":true},{"id":"pre2-06-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"損傷が多かった本の保管場所の問題を日本語で説明しなさい。","answer":"湿った壁の近くに置かれていた。","accepted":["湿った壁の近くに置かれていた。"],"why":"本文の根拠：They examined the books and found that many damaged copies were older editions stored near a damp wall.","context":"A school library noticed that books with damaged covers were returned more frequently than before. Staff first thought students were careless. They examined the books and found that many damaged copies were older editions stored near a damp wall. The library moved the shelves and replaced badly worn covers. It also showed students how to protect books in rainy weather. Damage decreased over the following term. The librarian said investigating the cause had been more useful than simply reminding everyone to be careful, although careful handling remained important.","title":"A lesson from returned books","evidence":"They examined the books and found that many damaged copies were older editions stored near a damp wall."},{"id":"pre2-06-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"生徒に本を守る方法を示したのはどんな天気のときですか。英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"rainy","accepted":["rain","rainy","raining"],"why":"本文の根拠：It also showed students how to protect books in rainy weather.","context":"A school library noticed that books with damaged covers were returned more frequently than before. Staff first thought students were careless. They examined the books and found that many damaged copies were older editions stored near a damp wall. The library moved the shelves and replaced badly worn covers. It also showed students how to protect books in rainy weather. Damage decreased over the following term. The librarian said investigating the cause had been more useful than simply reminding everyone to be careful, although careful handling remained important.","title":"A lesson from returned books","evidence":"It also showed students how to protect books in rainy weather."},{"id":"pre2-06-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語50語程度でメールへ返信し、賛否と理由を述べ、必要な情報を一つ質問しなさい。Our school may replace printed notices with online messages. Do you think this is a good plan?","answer":"I think online messages would be convenient because families could check them wherever they are. They could also reduce paper use. However, some families may have difficulty getting online. Will printed copies still be available for them? Providing both options would help important information reach everyone.","accepted":[],"why":"便利さの理由と、オンラインが使えない家庭への対応を問う質問です。情報が届くことが中心になります。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"pre2-06-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Should shops clearly explain the environmental impact of their products? 英語60語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I think they should. First, clear information can help customers compare products and choose ones that create less waste. Second, it can encourage companies to improve their materials and packaging. The explanations must be accurate and easy to understand. Vague claims may confuse customers, so shops should describe specific facts rather than simply calling every product environmentally friendly.","accepted":[],"why":"顧客の選択と企業の改善を別の理由にします。説明の正確さという条件は主張を支えます。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":7,"questions":[{"id":"pre2-07-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"We should ( prevent / provide / promote ) accidents by repairing the damaged stairs.","answer":"prevent","accepted":["prevent"],"why":"階段の修理で事故を防ぐのでpreventです。"},{"id":"pre2-07-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"The speaker's ( explanation / expectation / experiment ) helped us understand the difficult rule.","answer":"explanation","accepted":["explanation"],"why":"規則を理解させた話し手の説明はexplanationです。"},{"id":"pre2-07-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"The event was ( postponed / published / produced ) until June because the hall was being repaired.","answer":"postponed","accepted":["postponed"],"why":"会場の修理を理由に六月まで延期されたのでpostponedです。"},{"id":"pre2-07-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"The medicine is ( effective / expensive / electric ) at reducing pain; patients feel better after taking it.","answer":"effective","accepted":["effective"],"why":"痛みを和らげる効果があることはeffectiveです。"},{"id":"pre2-07-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"I ( came across / broke down / turned off ) an old photograph while cleaning the cupboard.","answer":"came across","accepted":["came across"],"why":"偶然見つけることはcome acrossです。"},{"id":"pre2-07-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"The students worked hard ( in order to / in spite of / according to ) finish the project on time.","answer":"in order to","accepted":["in order to"],"why":"原形finishにつながる目的のin order toです。"},{"id":"pre2-07-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"If she ( knew / knows / will know ) the answer, she would tell us.","answer":"knew","accepted":["knew"],"why":"would tellにつながる仮定なので過去形knewです。"},{"id":"pre2-07-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"I realized that I had ( forgotten / forget / forgetting ) to attach the file.","answer":"forgotten","accepted":["forgotten"],"why":"気付く時点より前のことなのでhadと過去分詞forgottenです。"},{"id":"pre2-07-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"We avoided ( using / use / used ) plastic plates at the picnic.","answer":"using","accepted":["using"],"why":"avoidの後にはing形を置きます。"},{"id":"pre2-07-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"The charity persuaded several companies ( to donate / donating / donated ) supplies.","answer":"to donate","accepted":["to donate"],"why":"persuade人to動詞で、人を説得して何かしてもらう形です。"},{"id":"pre2-07-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"彼は自分の無礼なコメントについて謝りました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( for / rude / He / apologized / his / comment )","answer":"He apologized for his rude comment.","accepted":["He apologized for his rude comment."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-07-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"私たちは新しい設備を設置するかどうかを議論しました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( to / install / whether / discussed / new / We / equipment )","answer":"We discussed whether to install new equipment.","accepted":["We discussed whether to install new equipment."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-07-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"その説明は非常に分かりにくく、誰も理解できませんでした。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( understand / confusing / it / that / was / The / could / so / explanation / nobody )","answer":"The explanation was so confusing that nobody could understand it.","accepted":["The explanation was so confusing that nobody could understand it."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-07-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"私は医者に数日間休むよう勧められました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( rest / a / to / for / few / days / advised / I / was )","answer":"I was advised to rest for a few days.","accepted":["I was advised to rest for a few days."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 人に動作を求める部分は人とto不定詞のまとまりにします。"},{"id":"pre2-07-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"苦情を減らすため追加した写真は何を示すものですか。日本語で答えなさい。","answer":"その座席から見える舞台の眺め。","accepted":["その座席から見える舞台の眺め。"],"why":"本文の根拠：Instead, it added photographs showing the view from those seats and offered exchanges before the performance if other seats were available.","context":"A theater introduced cheaper tickets for seats at the side of the stage. Some customers complained after discovering that part of the performance was difficult to see. The theater did not remove the discount. Instead, it added photographs showing the view from those seats and offered exchanges before the performance if other seats were available. Fewer complaints followed, even though sales of the discounted seats remained steady. The manager concluded that customers could make useful choices when the limitations were explained clearly, rather than only being told that the price was low.","title":"A flexible ticket","evidence":"Instead, it added photographs showing the view from those seats and offered exchanges before the performance if other seats were available.","self":true},{"id":"pre2-07-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"席の交換が可能な時点を英語3語で答えなさい。","answer":"before the performance","accepted":["before the performance"],"why":"本文の根拠：Instead, it added photographs showing the view from those seats and offered exchanges before the performance if other seats were available.","context":"A theater introduced cheaper tickets for seats at the side of the stage. Some customers complained after discovering that part of the performance was difficult to see. The theater did not remove the discount. Instead, it added photographs showing the view from those seats and offered exchanges before the performance if other seats were available. Fewer complaints followed, even though sales of the discounted seats remained steady. The manager concluded that customers could make useful choices when the limitations were explained clearly, rather than only being told that the price was low.","title":"A flexible ticket","evidence":"Instead, it added photographs showing the view from those seats and offered exchanges before the performance if other seats were available."},{"id":"pre2-07-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"部屋を二つの区画に分けた理由を日本語で説明しなさい。","answer":"グループ学習が廊下に移り、他の活動の邪魔になっていたから。","accepted":["グループ学習が廊下に移り、他の活動の邪魔になっていたから。"],"why":"本文の根拠：Students working on group projects therefore met in the corridor, where they disturbed other activities.","context":"A community center opened a room for students to study after school. It initially required complete silence throughout the room. Students working on group projects therefore met in the corridor, where they disturbed other activities. The center divided the room into a quiet area and a discussion area, with clear signs between them. Staff checked noise levels regularly rather than banning conversation everywhere. More students began using the room, including those studying alone. The center will keep both areas, while adjusting their sizes according to demand during examination periods.","title":"A place to study","evidence":"Students working on group projects therefore met in the corridor, where they disturbed other activities."},{"id":"pre2-07-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"広さを調整する際に考慮するものを英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"demand","accepted":["demand"],"why":"本文の根拠：The center will keep both areas, while adjusting their sizes according to demand during examination periods.","context":"A community center opened a room for students to study after school. It initially required complete silence throughout the room. Students working on group projects therefore met in the corridor, where they disturbed other activities. The center divided the room into a quiet area and a discussion area, with clear signs between them. Staff checked noise levels regularly rather than banning conversation everywhere. More students began using the room, including those studying alone. The center will keep both areas, while adjusting their sizes according to demand during examination periods.","title":"A place to study","evidence":"The center will keep both areas, while adjusting their sizes according to demand during examination periods."},{"id":"pre2-07-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語50語程度でメールへ返信し、賛否と理由を述べ、必要な情報を一つ質問しなさい。Our club wants to invite a guest speaker every month. Do you think this would benefit members?","answer":"It could benefit members because speakers can introduce experiences we do not hear about in normal lessons. However, a different talk every month may leave little time for our regular activities. How would the speakers be chosen? I would prefer topics connected to what the club is already doing.","accepted":[],"why":"利点と時間上の懸念を述べています。選び方への質問が提案と直接つながっています。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"pre2-07-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Should teenagers have a fixed limit on screen time every day? 英語60語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I do not think the same fixed limit suits every teenager. First, some screen use is necessary for homework and creative projects. Second, individual schedules differ, so a strict daily limit may be difficult to follow. It is better to consider the purpose of screen use and ensure enough time for sleep, exercise, and conversations with other people.","accepted":[],"why":"学習での必要性と生活日程の違いを理由にします。無制限を薦める必要はありません。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":8,"questions":[{"id":"pre2-08-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"The workshop will ( focus / follow / force ) on ways to reduce food waste.","answer":"focus","accepted":["focus"],"why":"focus onで、ある話題に重点を置くことを表します。"},{"id":"pre2-08-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"The athlete made a full ( recovery / reminder / request ) after the injury and returned to training.","answer":"recovery","accepted":["recovery"],"why":"けがから回復し練習に戻ったのでrecoveryです。"},{"id":"pre2-08-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"The instructions are ( available / valuable / various ) in three languages on our website.","answer":"available","accepted":["available"],"why":"利用できるという意味のavailableです。"},{"id":"pre2-08-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"Your suggestion is ( practical / personal / painful ); we can use it without buying expensive equipment.","answer":"practical","accepted":["practical"],"why":"高価な設備なしで実行できるので実用的なpracticalです。"},{"id":"pre2-08-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"The teacher asked us to ( hand in / hold on / hang up ) the essays by Friday.","answer":"hand in","accepted":["hand in"],"why":"提出するという表現はhand inです。"},{"id":"pre2-08-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"There was ( so / such / too ) little time that we skipped the last activity.","answer":"so","accepted":["so"],"why":"so littleと名詞とthat節で、少なすぎる時間の結果を述べます。"},{"id":"pre2-08-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"I would help you if I ( weren't / am not / will not be ) busy today.","answer":"weren't","accepted":["weren't"],"why":"現在の事実と異なる条件はif節の過去形です。"},{"id":"pre2-08-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"The train had ( departed / depart / departing ) before we reached the platform.","answer":"departed","accepted":["departed"],"why":"到着前の出発なのでhadと過去分詞です。"},{"id":"pre2-08-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"I don't mind ( waiting / wait / waited ) a few more minutes.","answer":"waiting","accepted":["waiting"],"why":"mindのあとで動作を表すにはing形を使います。"},{"id":"pre2-08-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"His parents allowed him ( to attend / attending / attended ) the evening class.","answer":"to attend","accepted":["to attend"],"why":"allow人to動詞で、人にすることを許可します。"},{"id":"pre2-08-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"もし彼女が近くに住んでいたら、私たちはもっと頻繁に会えるのに。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( often / nearby / we / lived / meet / If / she / more / could )","answer":"If she lived nearby, we could meet more often.","accepted":["If she lived nearby, we could meet more often."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-08-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"このキャンペーンは若者に本を読むよう奨励します。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( people / books / to / young / read / encourages / This / campaign )","answer":"This campaign encourages young people to read books.","accepted":["This campaign encourages young people to read books."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 人に動作を求める部分は人とto不定詞のまとまりにします。"},{"id":"pre2-08-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"彼はわずかな道具で椅子の修理に成功しました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( in / tools / succeeded / with / the / chair / few / He / repairing )","answer":"He succeeded in repairing the chair with few tools.","accepted":["He succeeded in repairing the chair with few tools."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-08-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"私はその問題がなぜ起きたのか知りたいです。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( find / the / why / I / problem / occurred / want / out / to )","answer":"I want to find out why the problem occurred.","accepted":["I want to find out why the problem occurred."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-08-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"見積もり方法をどう変えたか日本語で説明しなさい。","answer":"一つの価格ではなく価格の範囲を示し、すぐ確認できない部分も説明した。","accepted":["一つの価格ではなく価格の範囲を示し、すぐ確認できない部分も説明した。"],"why":"本文の根拠：The shop began providing a price range and explaining which parts could not be checked immediately.","context":"A repair shop used to give customers one estimated price before opening a damaged device. When hidden damage was found, the final price sometimes increased significantly. Customers felt the original estimate had been misleading. The shop began providing a price range and explaining which parts could not be checked immediately. If extra work was needed, staff contacted the customer before continuing. Repairs took slightly longer because approval was required, but complaints decreased. The owner decided that clear communication was more valuable than promising a low price that might not be possible.","title":"An honest repair estimate","evidence":"The shop began providing a price range and explaining which parts could not be checked immediately."},{"id":"pre2-08-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"追加作業の前に連絡する相手を英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"customer","accepted":["customer"],"why":"本文の根拠：If extra work was needed, staff contacted the customer before continuing.","context":"A repair shop used to give customers one estimated price before opening a damaged device. When hidden damage was found, the final price sometimes increased significantly. Customers felt the original estimate had been misleading. The shop began providing a price range and explaining which parts could not be checked immediately. If extra work was needed, staff contacted the customer before continuing. Repairs took slightly longer because approval was required, but complaints decreased. The owner decided that clear communication was more valuable than promising a low price that might not be possible.","title":"An honest repair estimate","evidence":"If extra work was needed, staff contacted the customer before continuing."},{"id":"pre2-08-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"最初に生徒が誤解したことを日本語で説明しなさい。","answer":"おかわりを頼むと追加料金がかかると思っていた。","accepted":["おかわりを頼むと追加料金がかかると思っていた。"],"why":"本文の根拠：During the first week, some students thought asking for more would cost extra.","context":"A school tested smaller initial lunch portions, allowing students to ask for more. The aim was to reduce food waste without leaving students hungry. During the first week, some students thought asking for more would cost extra. Staff explained that second portions were included and placed a clear sign by the serving area. Leftover food decreased, while the amount eaten remained similar. The school will continue monitoring both measures because less waste alone would not prove that students were receiving enough food. Student comments will also be considered before changing the menu.","title":"A school meal experiment","evidence":"During the first week, some students thought asking for more would cost extra."},{"id":"pre2-08-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"廃棄量だけで成功を判断しない理由を日本語で答えなさい。","answer":"生徒が十分な量を食べていることも確かめる必要があるため。","accepted":["生徒が十分な量を食べていることも確かめる必要があるため。"],"why":"本文の根拠：The school will continue monitoring both measures because less waste alone would not prove that students were receiving enough food.","context":"A school tested smaller initial lunch portions, allowing students to ask for more. The aim was to reduce food waste without leaving students hungry. During the first week, some students thought asking for more would cost extra. Staff explained that second portions were included and placed a clear sign by the serving area. Leftover food decreased, while the amount eaten remained similar. The school will continue monitoring both measures because less waste alone would not prove that students were receiving enough food. Student comments will also be considered before changing the menu.","title":"A school meal experiment","evidence":"The school will continue monitoring both measures because less waste alone would not prove that students were receiving enough food.","self":true},{"id":"pre2-08-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語50語程度でメールへ返信し、賛否と理由を述べ、必要な情報を一つ質問しなさい。A community center may open a quiet study room in the evenings. Would students find it helpful?","answer":"I think students would find it helpful, especially if their homes are noisy or crowded. A quiet room could make it easier to concentrate on homework. What time would the room close? Students need to know whether they can use it after clubs and still travel home safely.","accepted":[],"why":"集中の利点と終了時刻への質問を含めています。部活後の利用と帰宅の安全を具体化しています。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"pre2-08-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Should schools give students more opportunities to repair things? 英語60語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I think they should. First, repairing simple objects teaches students to solve practical problems instead of immediately buying replacements. Second, keeping items in use can reduce waste. Lessons must begin with safe tasks and suitable tools. Students should understand when a repair requires a trained adult, so the aim is useful judgment as well as practical skill.","accepted":[],"why":"問題解決と廃棄物削減を理由にしています。安全な範囲の条件は、主張と矛盾しません。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":9,"questions":[{"id":"pre2-09-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"The organizers will ( announce / arrange / achieve ) the winner's name on stage.","answer":"announce","accepted":["announce"],"why":"受賞者の名前を公に発表するのはannounceです。"},{"id":"pre2-09-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"The new crossing improved pedestrian ( safety / salary / scenery ) and reduced accidents.","answer":"safety","accepted":["safety"],"why":"歩行者の安全safetyが改善されたという意味です。"},{"id":"pre2-09-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"Customers can ( request / respect / repeat ) a refund by showing the receipt.","answer":"request","accepted":["request"],"why":"返金を求める動作はrequestです。"},{"id":"pre2-09-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"The machine is ( reliable / familiar / flexible ); it has worked without failure for years.","answer":"reliable","accepted":["reliable"],"why":"長年故障せずに動くので信頼できるreliableです。"},{"id":"pre2-09-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"We should ( get rid of / get along with / get back to ) the broken furniture that cannot be repaired.","answer":"get rid of","accepted":["get rid of"],"why":"修理不能の家具を処分するのでget rid ofです。"},{"id":"pre2-09-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"( Unless / During / Despite ) you book in advance, you may not get a seat.","answer":"Unless","accepted":["Unless"],"why":"事前に予約しない限りという条件はUnlessです。"},{"id":"pre2-09-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"If I ( lived / live / will live ) closer to school, I would walk there.","answer":"lived","accepted":["lived"],"why":"would walkにつながる仮定なのでif節に過去形です。"},{"id":"pre2-09-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"The ground was wet because it had ( rained / rain / raining ) during the night.","answer":"rained","accepted":["rained"],"why":"地面を見る時点より前の雨なのでhadと過去分詞です。"},{"id":"pre2-09-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"He suggested ( taking / take / took ) a different route.","answer":"taking","accepted":["taking"],"why":"suggestのあとに動作を置く場合はing形です。"},{"id":"pre2-09-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"We expect the work ( to be completed / completing / complete ) by Monday.","answer":"to be completed","accepted":["to be completed"],"why":"expect目的語to動詞と受動態で、作業が完成することを期待します。"},{"id":"pre2-09-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"私がなくした傘はその駅で見つかりました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( station / had / lost / at / the / found / The / I / umbrella / was )","answer":"The umbrella I had lost was found at the station.","accepted":["The umbrella I had lost was found at the station."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-09-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"彼らは会場を変更することを提案しました。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( suggested / changing / venue / the / They )","answer":"They suggested changing the venue.","accepted":["They suggested changing the venue."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-09-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"たとえ雨が降っても、試合は行われます。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( will / the / place / it / if / match / rains / take / Even )","answer":"Even if it rains, the match will take place.","accepted":["Even if it rains, the match will take place."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-09-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"この制度によって学生は安く旅行できます。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( students / allows / This / to / travel / cheaply / system )","answer":"This system allows students to travel cheaply.","accepted":["This system allows students to travel cheaply."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-09-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"集合場所の変更を見落とした理由を日本語で答えなさい。","answer":"長いメールの末尾近くに警告が書かれていたから。","accepted":["長いメールの末尾近くに警告が書かれていたから。"],"why":"本文の根拠：Several members missed the warning that the starting point had changed because it appeared near the end.","context":"A hiking club sent members a long email containing weather details and equipment advice. Several members missed the warning that the starting point had changed because it appeared near the end. The organizer began putting essential changes at the top, followed by a short checklist and detailed information below. Members still received the full explanation, but could quickly see what action was required. At the next trip, everyone arrived at the correct starting point. The club now uses the same structure for messages, especially when a last-minute change affects travel plans.","title":"A weather message","evidence":"Several members missed the warning that the starting point had changed because it appeared near the end.","self":true},{"id":"pre2-09-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"重要な変更の直後に置くものを英語2語で答えなさい。","answer":"short checklist","accepted":["short checklist"],"why":"本文の根拠：The organizer began putting essential changes at the top, followed by a short checklist and detailed information below.","context":"A hiking club sent members a long email containing weather details and equipment advice. Several members missed the warning that the starting point had changed because it appeared near the end. The organizer began putting essential changes at the top, followed by a short checklist and detailed information below. Members still received the full explanation, but could quickly see what action was required. At the next trip, everyone arrived at the correct starting point. The club now uses the same structure for messages, especially when a last-minute change affects travel plans.","title":"A weather message","evidence":"The organizer began putting essential changes at the top, followed by a short checklist and detailed information below."},{"id":"pre2-09-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"在宅勤務の日に新人の質問を支援する方法を日本語で答えなさい。","answer":"短いオンラインの質問時間を設ける。","accepted":["短いオンラインの質問時間を設ける。"],"why":"本文の根拠：Instead, it introduced a shared office day for each team and scheduled short online question sessions on other days.","context":"A company allowed employees to work from home twice a week. Some teams found it easier to concentrate, but new employees struggled to ask quick questions. The company considered requiring everyone to return daily. Instead, it introduced a shared office day for each team and scheduled short online question sessions on other days. New employees received more support without removing the option to work from home. The company will compare training progress and employee feedback after three months. It does not expect one arrangement to suit every role equally well.","title":"A shared office trial","evidence":"Instead, it introduced a shared office day for each team and scheduled short online question sessions on other days.","self":true},{"id":"pre2-09-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"新しい方式を評価するまでの期間を数字で答えなさい（か月）。","answer":"3","accepted":["3"],"why":"本文の根拠：The company will compare training progress and employee feedback after three months.","context":"A company allowed employees to work from home twice a week. Some teams found it easier to concentrate, but new employees struggled to ask quick questions. The company considered requiring everyone to return daily. Instead, it introduced a shared office day for each team and scheduled short online question sessions on other days. New employees received more support without removing the option to work from home. The company will compare training progress and employee feedback after three months. It does not expect one arrangement to suit every role equally well.","title":"A shared office trial","evidence":"The company will compare training progress and employee feedback after three months."},{"id":"pre2-09-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語50語程度でメールへ返信し、賛否と理由を述べ、必要な情報を一つ質問しなさい。Our class is thinking about making a podcast about local history. Do you think we should try it?","answer":"I think we should try it because interviewing local people could teach us things that are not in a textbook. A podcast would also let more people hear their stories. How would we get permission to share recordings? We should explain the project clearly to everyone we interview.","accepted":[],"why":"学習と共有の理由、録音公開の許可に関する質問を答えます。人物の意思を確認する提案も含みます。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"pre2-09-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Should people choose experiences rather than objects as gifts? 英語60語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I think experiences can be good gifts, but they are not always better than objects. First, an event may be difficult to attend because of the receiver's schedule. Second, a useful object can be enjoyed for many years. The best choice depends on the person's interests and needs, so asking or learning about them is more important than following one rule.","accepted":[],"why":"日程と長く使えることを理由にします。常に一方がよいという結論でなくても意見が明確なら成立します。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]},{"n":10,"questions":[{"id":"pre2-10-01","n":1,"kind":"cloze","q":"Please ( confirm / confuse / complain ) your reservation by replying to this email.","answer":"confirm","accepted":["confirm"],"why":"予約の確認を返信で行うのでconfirmです。"},{"id":"pre2-10-02","n":2,"kind":"cloze","q":"The village depends on tourism for much of its ( revenue / responsibility / reputation ).","answer":"revenue","accepted":["revenue"],"why":"観光による収入はrevenueです。"},{"id":"pre2-10-03","n":3,"kind":"cloze","q":"The school will ( participate / permit / perform ) in the regional science festival.","answer":"participate","accepted":["participate"],"why":"participate inで行事に参加するという意味です。"},{"id":"pre2-10-04","n":4,"kind":"cloze","q":"We need a more ( efficient / enormous / emotional ) system that uses less time and electricity.","answer":"efficient","accepted":["efficient"],"why":"時間と電力を少なく使う効率のよいシステムはefficientです。"},{"id":"pre2-10-05","n":5,"kind":"cloze","q":"This tradition has been ( passed down / taken off / thrown away ) from one generation to the next.","answer":"passed down","accepted":["passed down"],"why":"世代から世代へ受け継がれることはpass downです。"},{"id":"pre2-10-06","n":6,"kind":"cloze","q":"The flight was canceled ( owing to / even though / so that ) a technical problem.","answer":"owing to","accepted":["owing to"],"why":"名詞句を続けて原因を表すowing toです。"},{"id":"pre2-10-07","n":7,"kind":"cloze","q":"I wish I ( hadn't / haven't / don't ) forgotten to bring the camera yesterday.","answer":"hadn't","accepted":["hadn't"],"why":"過去を後悔する願望はwishと過去完了です。"},{"id":"pre2-10-08","n":8,"kind":"cloze","q":"After they had ( discussed / discuss / discussing ) the plan, they voted on it.","answer":"discussed","accepted":["discussed"],"why":"投票より前の議論なのでhadと過去分詞です。"},{"id":"pre2-10-09","n":9,"kind":"cloze","q":"We are considering ( moving / move / moved ) the event to a larger room.","answer":"moving","accepted":["moving"],"why":"considerの目的語として動作を示すにはing形です。"},{"id":"pre2-10-10","n":10,"kind":"cloze","q":"He was advised ( not to drive / not driving / didn't drive ) until his eyesight improved.","answer":"not to drive","accepted":["not to drive"],"why":"be advised not to動詞で、しないよう助言されたことを表します。"},{"id":"pre2-10-11","n":11,"kind":"order","q":"その催しは席が足りないほど人気でした。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( that / seats / The / enough / was / there / so / popular / were / not / event )","answer":"The event was so popular that there were not enough seats.","accepted":["The event was so popular that there were not enough seats."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-10-12","n":12,"kind":"order","q":"この問題を解決するには全員の協力が必要です。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( everyone's / solve / this / to / problem / need / cooperation / We )","answer":"We need everyone's cooperation to solve this problem.","accepted":["We need everyone's cooperation to solve this problem."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-10-13","n":13,"kind":"order","q":"私は環境に優しい製品を選ぶよう努めています。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( to / I / try / friendly / environmentally / choose / products )","answer":"I try to choose environmentally friendly products.","accepted":["I try to choose environmentally friendly products."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。"},{"id":"pre2-10-14","n":14,"kind":"order","q":"私は数年前にその機会を受け入れていたらよかったと思います。（語句を並べ替えて英文にする）\n( ago / years / had / few / the / I / wish / I / opportunity / a / accepted )","answer":"I wish I had accepted the opportunity a few years ago.","accepted":["I wish I had accepted the opportunity a few years ago."],"why":"日本語の意味に合う主語と動詞を最初に確認し、動詞が求める目的語・補語を続けます。時や場所のまとまりを崩さず、すべての語句を一回ずつ使います。 過去への後悔はI wish＋主語＋had＋過去分詞で表します。acceptedは過去分詞で、実際には受け入れなかった機会を述べます。"},{"id":"pre2-10-15","n":15,"kind":"reading","q":"デジタル応募を認めた理由を日本語で答えなさい。","answer":"高品質の印刷が高く、応募できない生徒がいたから。","accepted":["高品質の印刷が高く、応募できない生徒がいたから。"],"why":"本文の根拠：This prevented some students from entering because high-quality printing was expensive.","context":"A town photography contest originally accepted only printed photographs. This prevented some students from entering because high-quality printing was expensive. Organizers added a digital entry option but required the same image dimensions for every entry. Judges viewed all images on identical screens, without seeing the photographers' names. Printed copies were displayed only after the results were announced. More students entered, and the organizers kept the judging process unchanged. They said making entry easier did not mean lowering the standard used to choose winners.","title":"A fair competition","evidence":"This prevented some students from entering because high-quality printing was expensive.","self":true},{"id":"pre2-10-16","n":16,"kind":"reading","q":"審査時に見えない情報を本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"names","accepted":["names"],"why":"本文の根拠：Judges viewed all images on identical screens, without seeing the photographers' names.","context":"A town photography contest originally accepted only printed photographs. This prevented some students from entering because high-quality printing was expensive. Organizers added a digital entry option but required the same image dimensions for every entry. Judges viewed all images on identical screens, without seeing the photographers' names. Printed copies were displayed only after the results were announced. More students entered, and the organizers kept the judging process unchanged. They said making entry easier did not mean lowering the standard used to choose winners.","title":"A fair competition","evidence":"Judges viewed all images on identical screens, without seeing the photographers' names."},{"id":"pre2-10-17","n":17,"kind":"reading","q":"最初の設計で高齢者が困った理由を日本語で説明しなさい。","answer":"肘掛けがなく、立ち上がりにくかったから。","accepted":["肘掛けがなく、立ち上がりにくかったから。"],"why":"本文の根拠：Visitors liked the appearance, but older users found it hard to stand up because there were no armrests.","context":"A city planned to replace all park benches with a new design. Before placing the full order, it tested three benches in different locations. Visitors liked the appearance, but older users found it hard to stand up because there were no armrests. The city asked the manufacturer to modify the design and delayed the large order. Although the project took longer, officials said the trial had prevented an expensive mistake. The final benches kept the original materials but included armrests, and users were invited to test the revised version before delivery.","title":"A useful delay","evidence":"Visitors liked the appearance, but older users found it hard to stand up because there were no armrests."},{"id":"pre2-10-18","n":18,"kind":"reading","q":"修正版に追加した部品を本文と同じ英語1語で答えなさい。","answer":"armrests","accepted":["armrests"],"why":"本文の根拠：The final benches kept the original materials but included armrests, and users were invited to test the revised version before delivery.","context":"A city planned to replace all park benches with a new design. Before placing the full order, it tested three benches in different locations. Visitors liked the appearance, but older users found it hard to stand up because there were no armrests. The city asked the manufacturer to modify the design and delayed the large order. Although the project took longer, officials said the trial had prevented an expensive mistake. The final benches kept the original materials but included armrests, and users were invited to test the revised version before delivery.","title":"A useful delay","evidence":"The final benches kept the original materials but included armrests, and users were invited to test the revised version before delivery."},{"id":"pre2-10-19","n":19,"kind":"writing","q":"英語50語程度でメールへ返信し、賛否と理由を述べ、必要な情報を一つ質問しなさい。The student council may run a uniform exchange before next term. Do you think families would use it?","answer":"I think many families would use it because uniforms can become too small while they are still in good condition. An exchange could save money and reduce waste. Where would families bring the uniforms? Clear information about sizes and cleanliness would make the event easier to organize.","accepted":[],"why":"利用する理由と持込場所への質問です。サイズや清潔さという実施条件も具体的に述べます。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true},{"id":"pre2-10-20","n":20,"kind":"writing","q":"Should towns ask teenagers for their opinions before making public plans? 英語60語程度で意見と理由二つを書きなさい。","answer":"I think they should. First, teenagers use parks, roads, and public transport, so their experiences can reveal problems adults may overlook. Second, taking part in discussions can help young people understand how decisions are made. Officials should explain which suggestions can be used and why, so asking for opinions becomes a meaningful part of planning rather than a formality.","accepted":[],"why":"利用者としての経験と意思決定を学ぶことが理由です。提案への返答の必要性は補足として有効です。","rubric":["指定された内容を満たす","意見と理由がつながる","語順と時制が適切","文章が自然につながる"],"self":true}]}]}]}
